WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.501
Nikhil: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.836
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:05.572
between Pizza Hut in the US and in India.

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:07.907
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.214
The smallest pizza in the US
is the personal pan pizza,

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:17.317
and it is 6 inches across.

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.652
In India, our pizzas
start at personal size.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.756
It's seven inches wide
and has four slices.

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:24.924
The US also has a small pizza,

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.494
but only with the gluten-free crust,

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:29.396
and it is

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:30.430
difficult.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.400
10 inches wide. So depressing looking.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.667
Then we're on to the mediums.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.970
A medium pizza here in India is 10 inches

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.671
and has six slices.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:42.475
Joe: A US medium pizza
comes in at 12 inches wide.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:46.279
This medium pizza is equal
to the small pizza in the US.

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:48.481
People in the US, sometimes
it's just really hard

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:50.150
not to stereotype you guys.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:53.286
Next up in India, we have nothing.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.488
Because medium is our largest size.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.892
That's right, we have only
two sizes, personal or medium.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.960
No large for us because

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.098
Pizza Hut is watching our weight, I guess.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:06.533
Stereotype away, my man,

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:09.235
because in the US, you
know we got this large,

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:12.338
and it is 14 inches in diameter.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.840
So America's largest pizza

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.676
is 4 inches wider than India's largest.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.578
That doesn't sound so bad.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.546
However.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:22.015
If you calculate the surface
area of the two pizzas,

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:24.117
those few inches make a big difference.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:28.655
The Indian medium has a surface
area of 78.5 square inches,

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:33.159
while the US large clocks
in at 153.9 square inches.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:36.396
To save you from doing the
math, that's a 96% increase.

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.431
That means the US large pizza

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:41.501
is nearly double our Indian medium.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.670
What the heck, Pizza Hut?

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:44.871
The type of crust you get

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.539
doesn't affect the width of the pizza,

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.108
but how does it affect the value?

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:51.044
We're going to weigh a
medium hand-tossed slice

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:53.113
versus a medium pan-crust slice

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:56.216
to see which one gives you
more pizza for your money.

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:57.984
All right, I'm going to
do the same with our pan

00:01:57.984 --> 00:02:01.688
and San Francisco-style
pizzas, the medium size.

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:04.757
All right. So, medium hand-tossed weighs

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:06.726
94 grams.

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:08.228
Pan, the thick boy.

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:09.295
Boy!

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:11.798
Whoa! 104 grams.

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:15.135
That's a difference of --
what was the first one?

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:18.138
That's a difference of this many grams.

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:22.675
This one is pan style,
and it weighs 78 grams.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.377
This slice

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:28.081
weighs 66 grams.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.149
Fairly lighter,

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:31.551
and I think this is because
when they make this pizza,

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.319
they press it down into the pan,

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.155
and that's the San Francisco style.

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:38.391
This weighs more and therefore is more,

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:39.459
'cause it's more bread.

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:40.627
You want the cheese and the sauce.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:41.761
You want the fun stuff, right?

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.129
I don't -- no.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:47.167
Oh, boy, this is gonna be trouble.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:50.703
Here is everything you'll find on the menu

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.706
at Pizza Hut India that you
will not find in the US.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.709
And here are all the Pizza
Hut menu items from the US

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.144
you won't find in India.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:01.047
Let's start off with the
foundation of any pizza:

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.049
the crust, starting with

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:06.886
the San Francisco signature style.

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:09.155
To my understanding, it's
basically a pan pizza,

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:11.858
but they press the dough
in with their hands

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.226
so it's kind of hand-tossed.

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:14.661
Next up, we have something very special.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:17.397
It's a Schezwan pan pizza.

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:21.301
Oh, my God, yeah. I really like this.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:23.102
It's spicy. Really yum.

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.370
Just to give you some comparison,

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.173
the way chicken tikka masala
was invented in the UK

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:29.576
but clearly inspired by Indian cuisine,

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:32.679
Schezwan sauce was actually
invented here in Kolkata

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:34.881
by the Chinese community
that settled down here.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.350
But it's obviously inspired
by Chinese cuisine,

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.586
and now it's become
part of Indian cuisine.

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:43.122
We have accepted it wholly,
and we eat it all across India.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.892
Very exciting to see it integrated
into the Pizza Hut menu,

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:48.928
and it actually tastes
very good on this pizza.

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:52.966
Next up they have a
stuffed cheese crust Maxx,

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:55.802
with two X's for emphasis.

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:59.005
You can already see that this
thing is loaded with cheese.

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:00.773
Next to the cheese, alongside it,

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:03.142
there's, like, a sort of creamy sauce,

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:06.913
which Pizza Hut is calling
Peruvian creamy sauce.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.316
Whoa!

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:13.586
Oh, my God, yeah. This is decadent food.

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:17.123
Next up we have a stuffed
crust with veg kebab.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.324
That's right. If you
don't know what kebab is,

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:21.594
it's basically meat that's
cooked in a tandoor.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:22.895
If you don't know what a tandoor is,

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:25.098
please go watch the older
episodes of "Food Wars."

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.466
I've explained it eight times.

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:28.735
A lot of people like to
leave the crust behind,

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:30.637
but I feel like Pizza Hut is making sure

00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:33.106
all of the pizza is eaten,
because even this looks

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.341
like a dish in itself at this point.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.110
Oh, my God, that's really yum.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.012
And the final option:

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:43.316
the stuffed crust with
a non-vegetarian kebab.

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:44.717
Ooh.

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:47.754
As you can see, this is what
looks to be chicken seekh.

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.592
Oh, that's the best of the lot.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:55.061
That was amazing. Oh, my God.

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.296
Smashed it, Pizza Hut.

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.898
That might be the best pizza
I've had on "Food Wars" so far,

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.833
and I didn't even eat the pizza part.

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:03.836
We also have a variety of
crust options in the US,

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.672
starting down here. You saw it already.

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.106
Here it is again, the hand-tossed.

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:09.942
This to me is, like,
classic. This is the default.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:11.244
You guys don't have hand-tossed?

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:13.279
Moving on: Thin 'N Crispy.

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:15.348
I mean, how much -- look at this.

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:18.151
They can't charge the same
amount for this, right?

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:19.052
I don't think they should.

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:22.488
Moving on over here: the
original stuffed crust.

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:24.457
They put cheese in the crust.

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:25.591
Can you believe that?

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:28.394
Ugh, no, it is solidified.

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.263
That doesn't stop me from biting into it.

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:34.067
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:38.237
Last and, let's be honest,
least: gluten-free crust.

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:40.506
Look, I don't know what's
going on with gluten allergies,

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:42.942
and my apologies if you have
one, but I'm looking at this,

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:44.143
I'm just like, I'm sorry, guys.

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:45.712
I mean, is this that much better?

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:48.348
I don't know how you can enjoy this.

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:49.415
And for a limited time,

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:53.186
Pizza Hut in the US has
Detroit-style pizza!

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:54.721
Let's go! Let us go.

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:56.222
Look at this. Are you
kidding me with this?

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:57.957
Detroit-style pizza. What's Detroit style?

00:05:57.957 --> 00:06:01.227
Well, they cook it in a square
pan that has sides to it.

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:02.662
It's like when you cook brownies

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:06.132
and every brownie is
a corner or end piece.

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:07.433
It's like that, for pizza.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:09.802
So every slice is going to have

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:12.038
the crispy crust on the
outside. It's thicker.

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:13.706
One of my favorite pizza styles.

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.041
I'm glad Pizza Hut's doing it.

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:17.410
Generous with the pepperoni,
guys. I appreciate it.

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:22.014
Not the best Detroit-style
pizza I've ever had,

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:23.416
but it's pretty good.

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:26.185
I think they go bread,
cheese, topping, sauce.

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:28.988
These are the toppings we
found under the categories

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:31.591
classic, favorites, and delight.

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:33.025
Very arbitrarily named,

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:34.560
but, yeah, let's jump into it.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.863
The first option is chicken sausage.

00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:38.297
Smells really good.

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:41.734
A lot of onions. I love onions.

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:45.171
Mm.

00:06:45.171 --> 00:06:46.339
It's pretty classic.

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:48.708
The next pizza is spiced paneer.

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:50.443
Paneer, if you don't
know, is cottage cheese.

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:52.078
We make it all over the
place here in India,

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:54.147
and it's one of our favorite ingredients.

00:06:54.147 --> 00:06:57.417
We use it on everything, even pizzas.

00:06:58.518 --> 00:06:59.485
Not very spicy,

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:01.888
but definitely it's got,
like, a tangy twist to it.

00:07:01.888 --> 00:07:04.157
Next up we have the Veggie Feast.

00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:08.694
It's got some herbed onion,
capsicum, and sweet corn.

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:13.399
This is such a wholesome, chill pizza.

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:14.600
It's definitely a classic.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.602
It's something your
mom would make at home.

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:18.871
Next up, we have the veggie tandoori,

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:20.540
which I have already taken a bite of.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.875
We got this one with the Schezwan crust,

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:24.177
so it's definitely spicier

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:26.546
than the typical pan pizza you'll get.

00:07:26.546 --> 00:07:29.348
And I already tasted it,
and I told you I loved it.

00:07:29.348 --> 00:07:30.550
I love the spice.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:34.720
Next up, we have spiced
chicken meat-a-balls!

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.489
It's a very straightforward pizza,

00:07:36.489 --> 00:07:39.759
but we got it with the
cheese-burst filling.

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:41.994
Next up, we have the
Chicken N Corn Delight.

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:43.496
It already has the word
"delight" in the name,

00:07:43.496 --> 00:07:45.298
so I'm assuming it should be a delight,

00:07:45.298 --> 00:07:46.632
but I'll be the judge of that.

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:50.803
Capsicum; chicken, just
strewn across; and corn.

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:54.941
It's got too much going on, I would say.

00:07:54.941 --> 00:07:57.643
Personally, I would not
order a pizza like this.

00:07:57.643 --> 00:07:59.145
Next up, to round it all off,

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:02.148
this is the double chicken sausage pizza.

00:08:02.148 --> 00:08:04.350
Am I wrong in saying
that this just looks like

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:07.453
a boring version of the
normal chicken sausage pizza,

00:08:07.453 --> 00:08:11.157
which has onions and
just feels a lot better?

00:08:11.157 --> 00:08:13.893
We have a pepperoni pizza

00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:15.928
that is made of pork and not chicken

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:18.097
and a Pepperoni Lover's pizza.

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:20.032
Which one has more pepperoni?

00:08:20.032 --> 00:08:20.867
I can't tell!

00:08:20.867 --> 00:08:22.435
The supreme pizza.

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:26.772
It has pepperoni, mushrooms,
green peppers, onions,

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:27.874
and that's it.

00:08:27.874 --> 00:08:30.109
But if that's not
supreme-y enough for you,

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:33.145
we have the super supreme,

00:08:33.145 --> 00:08:35.448
which, now they've
introduced black olives.

00:08:35.448 --> 00:08:37.216
Meat Lover's, baby!

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:39.385
Meat Lover's!

00:08:39.385 --> 00:08:42.889
You got pepperoni, you got
bacon, you got sausage.

00:08:42.889 --> 00:08:44.323
I bet there's something else on there

00:08:44.323 --> 00:08:45.525
that I don't know, another meat.

00:08:45.525 --> 00:08:47.360
I just, it's beautiful.

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:50.530
This next pizza is the Veggie Lover's,

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:52.064
and I absolutely hate it.

00:08:52.064 --> 00:08:53.933
You want veggies? Go get a
salad. Don't put it on pizza.

00:08:53.933 --> 00:08:55.434
Like, you're not fooling
anyone, all right?

00:08:55.434 --> 00:08:57.503
Backyard barbecue chicken.

00:08:57.503 --> 00:08:59.705
Yuelei, do you have enough B-roll?

00:08:59.705 --> 00:09:01.073
I think, it's barbecue chicken,

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:03.776
but I think they use barbecue
sauce instead of pizza sauce.

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:05.878
Genius. Genius!

00:09:08.147 --> 00:09:09.448
This is so good.

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:12.485
Oh, yeah! The Buffalo chicken.

00:09:12.485 --> 00:09:14.253
It's, like, surprisingly good.

00:09:14.253 --> 00:09:16.789
Pizza Hut does not have a straight

00:09:16.789 --> 00:09:19.158
Hawaiian pizza on the menu.

00:09:19.158 --> 00:09:22.228
The only thing they have
is Hawaiian chicken.

00:09:22.228 --> 00:09:24.130
I see, obviously, chicken.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:25.831
I see a pineapple.

00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:27.633
I think I see ham? Yep.

00:09:27.633 --> 00:09:30.169
I think Hawaiian should
just be pineapple and bacon,

00:09:30.169 --> 00:09:31.637
and if you want to throw some
chicken on it that's fine,

00:09:31.637 --> 00:09:33.372
but if you have a strong opinion

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:35.875
either for or against pineapple
on pizza, you're wrong.

00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:37.143
It's a perfectly fine topping.

00:09:37.143 --> 00:09:39.545
I don't know why everyone
gets so worked up about it.

00:09:39.545 --> 00:09:41.581
More pizzas, and these are all part

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:43.649
of the signature collection.

00:09:43.649 --> 00:09:45.585
There are 11 pizzas in front of me?

00:09:45.585 --> 00:09:47.853
Two, four, six ... ah, OK.

00:09:47.853 --> 00:09:50.089
First off, the Country Feast.

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:52.058
It looks super saucy.

00:09:52.058 --> 00:09:53.459
It's all loaded with vegetables.

00:09:53.459 --> 00:09:55.695
There's mushrooms,
capsicum, onion, sweet corn,

00:09:55.695 --> 00:09:58.531
roasted peppers; everything that you want

00:09:58.531 --> 00:10:01.334
on a country-themed pizza.

00:10:01.334 --> 00:10:03.669
All right, next up we
have tandoori paneer.

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:05.638
If you remember in the
previous categories,

00:10:05.638 --> 00:10:07.273
we had spiced paneer.

00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:09.775
So all I'm looking for
is, why is this different?

00:10:11.777 --> 00:10:14.780
Oh, my God, that's really yum.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.582
Next up is the Veggie Lover.

00:10:16.582 --> 00:10:19.719
It's basically got
tomato, onion, capsicum,

00:10:19.719 --> 00:10:21.787
mushrooms, and some red paprika

00:10:21.787 --> 00:10:24.156
and hopefully a whole lot of flavor.

00:10:27.159 --> 00:10:28.761
It's underwhelming. I'm gonna be honest.

00:10:28.761 --> 00:10:30.863
Next up, we have chicken tikka.

00:10:30.863 --> 00:10:32.365
Everybody knows chicken tikka.

00:10:33.699 --> 00:10:35.901
It's a bit too strong, too tangy,

00:10:35.901 --> 00:10:37.136
and I think they could have gone

00:10:37.136 --> 00:10:38.904
with a thinner layer of sauce.

00:10:38.904 --> 00:10:41.240
Next up we have the malai chicken tikka.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:42.842
Malai is basically cream.

00:10:42.842 --> 00:10:45.911
So malai kebabs, they
basically grill the chicken

00:10:45.911 --> 00:10:47.513
and they pour malai on top.

00:10:47.513 --> 00:10:51.484
We have the chicken pepperoni.

00:10:51.484 --> 00:10:53.653
Double paneer supreme.

00:10:53.653 --> 00:10:56.589
You like paneer? You like Supreme clothes?

00:10:56.589 --> 00:10:59.325
Well, this has double of
it, minus the clothes.

00:10:59.325 --> 00:11:01.160
Veggie supreme.

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:03.596
Everybody in India has
heard of this pizza.

00:11:03.596 --> 00:11:04.897
This is a painting.

00:11:04.897 --> 00:11:08.801
I can genuinely see this on
the wall of an art gallery.

00:11:08.801 --> 00:11:12.071
There's capsicum, there's
olives, there's corn,

00:11:12.071 --> 00:11:15.908
there's onions, there's corn again.

00:11:15.908 --> 00:11:17.476
Veg Kebab Surprise.

00:11:17.476 --> 00:11:21.213
I'm curious to know what's
gonna be surprising about this.

00:11:22.682 --> 00:11:25.718
Surprise, surprise, it tastes bland.

00:11:25.718 --> 00:11:28.387
And now on to our
penultimate signature pizza.

00:11:28.387 --> 00:11:31.257
This is the chicken tikka supreme!

00:11:31.257 --> 00:11:32.692
Woohoo!

00:11:32.692 --> 00:11:34.493
Basically what they've
done is they've taken

00:11:34.493 --> 00:11:36.328
four different kinds of chicken

00:11:36.328 --> 00:11:38.097
and they put it on a pizza.

00:11:38.097 --> 00:11:41.333
And finally, in the line
of signature pizzas,

00:11:41.333 --> 00:11:44.737
we have Triple Chicken Feast.

00:11:44.737 --> 00:11:48.074
It has all of the above ingredients,

00:11:48.074 --> 00:11:49.909
and we've also gone the extra mile

00:11:49.909 --> 00:11:53.079
and taken it with a chicken
stuffing in the crust.

00:11:53.079 --> 00:11:55.514
Overall, Pizza Hut has actually killed it.

00:11:55.514 --> 00:11:57.783
I think all the ingredients
have tasted super fresh,

00:11:57.783 --> 00:11:59.518
all the meat has also tasted really soft

00:11:59.518 --> 00:12:01.420
and juicy and delicious,

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:03.989
and the sauce has been
consistently yum throughout.

00:12:03.989 --> 00:12:06.926
Damn, Pizza Hut. Good job.

00:12:06.926 --> 00:12:08.394
As mentioned before,

00:12:08.394 --> 00:12:13.032
currently have a Detroit-style
pizza at the US Pizza Hut.

00:12:13.032 --> 00:12:14.934
This is what it looks like.
Two slices are missing.

00:12:14.934 --> 00:12:17.036
I skipped lunch, and
breakfast, to be honest.

00:12:17.036 --> 00:12:19.004
For those of you outside
of the United States,

00:12:19.004 --> 00:12:20.906
Detroit is a city in Michigan.

00:12:20.906 --> 00:12:23.109
They have their own style
of pizza. I really enjoy it.

00:12:23.109 --> 00:12:25.978
You can also get it as
a supreme Detroit style

00:12:25.978 --> 00:12:28.447
and a meaty deluxe Detroit style.

00:12:28.447 --> 00:12:29.648
And I didn't get them

00:12:29.648 --> 00:12:31.417
because it all looks exactly like this.

00:12:31.417 --> 00:12:33.686
One fun option on the Pizza Hut India menu

00:12:33.686 --> 00:12:36.956
is their new range of Momo Mia pizzas,

00:12:36.956 --> 00:12:39.024
which are pan pizzas

00:12:39.024 --> 00:12:42.094
with momos baked into the crust.

00:12:42.094 --> 00:12:43.429
Now, if you don't know what momos are,

00:12:43.429 --> 00:12:46.098
they're basically dumplings
from Nepal and Tibet.

00:12:46.098 --> 00:12:47.466
They're served all across India,

00:12:47.466 --> 00:12:50.503
and they've become huge favorites
for everybody over here.

00:12:50.503 --> 00:12:54.173
They've also given a
Schezwan sauce to the side,

00:12:54.173 --> 00:12:56.342
which is what you
typically eat with momos.

00:12:58.010 --> 00:12:58.844
Hm.

00:12:59.845 --> 00:13:00.679
No.

00:13:01.714 --> 00:13:04.350
That ain't right. I don't
see how this is working.

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:05.718
I can't think of a single Italian

00:13:05.718 --> 00:13:07.286
who would put a pocket of ravioli

00:13:07.286 --> 00:13:09.989
on top of pizza and
then bake them together.

00:13:09.989 --> 00:13:12.124
And this is effectively what that is.

00:13:12.124 --> 00:13:15.828
We also have a range of
Flavour Fun personal pan pizzas

00:13:15.828 --> 00:13:18.297
that you can get with
a host of new flavors.

00:13:18.297 --> 00:13:20.399
Starting off with classic corn.

00:13:20.399 --> 00:13:23.335
Next up, we have the
classic onion and capsicum.

00:13:23.335 --> 00:13:25.137
Tandoori mushroom and corn.

00:13:25.137 --> 00:13:26.772
So, it looks similar to this,

00:13:26.772 --> 00:13:29.375
but it used tandoori sauce
and the varied mushrooms.

00:13:29.375 --> 00:13:32.278
Next up, we have the classic
paneer, onion, and capsicum.

00:13:32.278 --> 00:13:35.014
Then we have the classic chicken sausage,

00:13:35.014 --> 00:13:36.682
but personal-pan-sized.

00:13:36.682 --> 00:13:38.984
Next, we have the Italian
pepperoni and onion.

00:13:38.984 --> 00:13:40.719
And just a reminder that the pepperoni

00:13:40.719 --> 00:13:42.621
that they've used is chicken pepperoni.

00:13:42.621 --> 00:13:43.989
Tandoori chicken tikka and onion,

00:13:43.989 --> 00:13:46.425
and the classic loaded chicken delight.

00:13:46.425 --> 00:13:48.127
Personally, [crickets chirping]

00:13:48.127 --> 00:13:50.162
I wouldn't order these pans.

00:13:50.162 --> 00:13:51.831
I would get the larger pizzas,

00:13:51.831 --> 00:13:53.699
'cause they tasted way better.

00:13:53.699 --> 00:13:55.568
On top of set menu items,

00:13:55.568 --> 00:13:58.671
we can also customize our
pizzas in unique ways.

00:13:58.671 --> 00:14:00.806
For example, if you don't want
tomato sauce as your base,

00:14:00.806 --> 00:14:03.709
you can sub it out for
creamy garlic Parmesan,

00:14:03.709 --> 00:14:05.411
barbecue sauce, remember from before?

00:14:05.411 --> 00:14:08.414
Buffalo sauce, or a no-sauce option

00:14:08.414 --> 00:14:10.249
if you are a maniac.

00:14:10.249 --> 00:14:12.451
And if you want you can specify light,

00:14:12.451 --> 00:14:13.986
regular, or extra sauce.

00:14:13.986 --> 00:14:15.988
Unfortunately, we can't change the sauces

00:14:15.988 --> 00:14:17.223
on our pizza bases,

00:14:17.223 --> 00:14:19.692
but we have a bunch of custom toppings

00:14:19.692 --> 00:14:20.993
that you will not find in the US,

00:14:20.993 --> 00:14:23.896
like baby corn, sweet
corn, herbed veggies,

00:14:23.896 --> 00:14:26.765
spiced paneer, and veg kebab.

00:14:26.765 --> 00:14:28.267
And we also have exclusive toppings

00:14:28.267 --> 00:14:29.401
you cannot get in India.

00:14:29.401 --> 00:14:32.471
For instance, we have
pepperoni, which is pork;

00:14:32.471 --> 00:14:34.473
our Italian sausage has pork;

00:14:34.473 --> 00:14:36.475
bacon, ah, I believe is pork;

00:14:36.475 --> 00:14:38.244
meatballs, beef and pork;

00:14:38.244 --> 00:14:39.645
ham, pork;

00:14:39.645 --> 00:14:41.847
and then beef;

00:14:41.847 --> 00:14:42.681
and pork.

00:14:42.681 --> 00:14:44.884
Then the vegetables: We got white onion;

00:14:44.884 --> 00:14:46.685
we got pineapple, which is a fruit;

00:14:46.685 --> 00:14:48.254
and we have banana
peppers, which I don't know

00:14:48.254 --> 00:14:50.422
if it's a fruit or a
vegetable or a pepper.

00:14:50.422 --> 00:14:51.523
Are peppers fruit?

00:14:51.523 --> 00:14:53.425
Whenever we have the
option of customizations

00:14:53.425 --> 00:14:55.561
on "Food Wars," we like
to combine all of our

00:14:55.561 --> 00:14:59.365
exclusive ingredients to
make an India-only pizza.

00:14:59.365 --> 00:15:03.302
So this pizza has a Schezwan
base with baby corn,

00:15:03.302 --> 00:15:07.773
veg kebab, spiced paneer,
and herbed veggies.

00:15:07.773 --> 00:15:09.775
It looks pretty gnarly, I'm not gonna lie,

00:15:09.775 --> 00:15:11.477
but let's see how it tastes.

00:15:14.246 --> 00:15:15.414
Hm.

00:15:15.414 --> 00:15:17.349
I can see why Pizza Hut didn't put this

00:15:17.349 --> 00:15:18.517
officially on their menu,

00:15:18.517 --> 00:15:21.053
'cause maybe the ingredients
don't go that well together,

00:15:21.053 --> 00:15:25.190
but, hey, this is an
India-only Pizza Hut pizza,

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.592
and that means something.

00:15:26.592 --> 00:15:30.896
And, of course, we had to
create our own US-only pizza.

00:15:30.896 --> 00:15:35.401
So, the thin crispy base,
creamy garlic Parmesan sauce,

00:15:35.401 --> 00:15:37.937
beef, bacon, white onion,

00:15:37.937 --> 00:15:42.107
and everyone's favorite
vegetable, banana peppers.

00:15:43.375 --> 00:15:46.545
No!

00:15:46.545 --> 00:15:48.681
This looks like a cartoon pizza.

00:15:48.681 --> 00:15:49.982
Ah.

00:15:52.685 --> 00:15:54.086
OK, it's not bad.

00:15:54.086 --> 00:15:55.788
It's not great. I wouldn't get it.

00:15:55.788 --> 00:15:57.489
Yeah, it tastes like onion and bacon.

00:15:57.489 --> 00:15:58.324
Don't get this.

00:15:58.324 --> 00:15:59.391
Oop!

00:15:59.391 --> 00:16:01.193
Pizza Hut has a bunch of sides.

00:16:01.193 --> 00:16:02.895
So, let's start off with the breads.

00:16:02.895 --> 00:16:05.364
First off, we have cheese garlic bread.

00:16:05.364 --> 00:16:09.134
Then we have spicy supreme
cheese garlic bread.

00:16:09.134 --> 00:16:10.269
It's basically cheese melted

00:16:10.269 --> 00:16:12.104
on top of a garlic bread baguette.

00:16:12.104 --> 00:16:15.407
It's got some green chili
and some chopped onions.

00:16:15.407 --> 00:16:16.976
It's very delicious when it's hot.

00:16:16.976 --> 00:16:21.280
Mexican garlic breadsticks.
Oregano sprinkled on top,

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:24.283
some jalapeño, some
chopped olives, and onions.

00:16:24.283 --> 00:16:25.417
It looks really delicious.

00:16:25.417 --> 00:16:27.786
Creamy garlic breadsticks.

00:16:27.786 --> 00:16:30.856
And finally we have garlic
breadsticks in a little packet

00:16:30.856 --> 00:16:33.058
that says "GARLIC BREAD STIX."

00:16:33.058 --> 00:16:34.793
The US Pizza Hut only offers

00:16:34.793 --> 00:16:36.528
regular breadsticks and cheese sticks.

00:16:36.528 --> 00:16:38.964
So, in fact, the only
actual exclusive side

00:16:38.964 --> 00:16:42.334
that we have in the US is fries.

00:16:42.334 --> 00:16:43.769
We have a bunch of other sides,

00:16:43.769 --> 00:16:47.139
including baked cheesy momos veg

00:16:47.139 --> 00:16:49.675
and baked cheesy momos non-veg.

00:16:50.843 --> 00:16:52.811
Whew. That's a potent smell.

00:16:52.811 --> 00:16:54.613
You know what?

00:16:54.613 --> 00:16:56.482
It's not half bad.

00:16:56.482 --> 00:16:58.050
Next up we have potato poppers,

00:16:58.050 --> 00:16:59.618
which are pretty much Tater Tots.

00:16:59.618 --> 00:17:02.521
We have the Indi Rockin Roll veg

00:17:02.521 --> 00:17:05.657
and the Indi Rockin Roll non-veg.

00:17:05.657 --> 00:17:06.525
This is basically a roll,

00:17:06.525 --> 00:17:08.527
but I like how the wrap is kind of thin.

00:17:10.095 --> 00:17:12.798
Again, it's quite good.

00:17:12.798 --> 00:17:15.267
Next up, we have the zesty paneer pocket

00:17:15.267 --> 00:17:17.403
and the zesty chicken pocket.

00:17:17.403 --> 00:17:19.638
These are pretty much like pizza pockets.

00:17:19.638 --> 00:17:22.841
There's some mint mayo, some
normal mayo, some cream cheese,

00:17:22.841 --> 00:17:25.377
chicken, and jalapeños.

00:17:25.377 --> 00:17:27.446
We have jalapeño poppers.

00:17:27.446 --> 00:17:29.648
I imagine they're just filled with cheese

00:17:29.648 --> 00:17:30.749
and some jalapeño bits.

00:17:30.749 --> 00:17:33.218
Oh, ugh, I did not
expect that consistency.

00:17:33.218 --> 00:17:36.188
And that brings us to an
old classic: chicken wings.

00:17:36.188 --> 00:17:38.023
Spicy baked chicken wings.

00:17:38.023 --> 00:17:41.226
So I suppose they're a
healthier alternative?

00:17:41.226 --> 00:17:44.163
WingStreet wings.

00:17:44.163 --> 00:17:44.997
Yes!

00:17:44.997 --> 00:17:47.066
Both traditional and boneless.

00:17:47.066 --> 00:17:49.168
You can get them in the following flavors.

00:17:49.168 --> 00:17:52.204
Lemon pepper. Oh, let's go, lemon pepper.

00:17:52.204 --> 00:17:53.272
I usually don't like lemon pepper,

00:17:53.272 --> 00:17:54.106
but these are pretty good.

00:17:54.106 --> 00:17:55.274
Ooh, honey barbecue.

00:17:55.274 --> 00:17:58.444
Ugh, these things are like condensation.

00:17:58.444 --> 00:18:01.313
Ah, ooh, the medium Buffalo.

00:18:01.313 --> 00:18:02.614
Ooh, Cajun style!

00:18:04.383 --> 00:18:05.517
Eh, just OK.

00:18:05.517 --> 00:18:08.087
Spicy garlic. What?

00:18:08.087 --> 00:18:10.556
Naked. That's wings with nothing on it.

00:18:10.556 --> 00:18:11.957
Why would you do that? I don't know.

00:18:11.957 --> 00:18:13.859
Buffalo Burnin' Hot.

00:18:13.859 --> 00:18:15.961
Three flames!

00:18:15.961 --> 00:18:18.730
Mm, this should be your medium.

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:20.799
Oh, wait!

00:18:20.799 --> 00:18:22.367
Yeah, OK.

00:18:22.367 --> 00:18:23.435
Sweet chili.

00:18:23.435 --> 00:18:25.337
Am I sweating? I feel like I'm sweating.

00:18:26.939 --> 00:18:29.508
They're all just eh. You
know, I mean, I like wings.

00:18:29.508 --> 00:18:31.577
Maybe my wing standards are too high.

00:18:31.577 --> 00:18:34.246
Garlic Parmesan. Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho!

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:36.048
[sighs]

00:18:37.883 --> 00:18:38.951
Oh, my God!

00:18:38.951 --> 00:18:41.553
I mean, the sauce is like
pasta sauce. It's really thick.

00:18:41.553 --> 00:18:42.521
It's got a lot of flavor to it,

00:18:42.521 --> 00:18:45.357
but it's just, like, sitting in the sauce,

00:18:45.357 --> 00:18:47.559
so either you get a
mouthful of sauce or none.

00:18:47.559 --> 00:18:51.730
And these come in portions
of six, 12, 18, or 36.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:53.665
And next up on the menu,

00:18:53.665 --> 00:18:56.535
you can also find a range of pastas,

00:18:56.535 --> 00:18:58.770
starting with the creamy mushroom.

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:00.739
[sauce squishing]

00:19:00.739 --> 00:19:03.742
You know what? If I have to
listen to this, so will you all.

00:19:03.742 --> 00:19:06.979
[sauce squishing]

00:19:06.979 --> 00:19:08.780
Just get some in the boom mic.

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:11.316
[sauce squishing]

00:19:12.684 --> 00:19:15.053
Decent pasta for a fast-food restaurant.

00:19:15.053 --> 00:19:17.356
They have a cheesy comfort veg pasta

00:19:17.356 --> 00:19:20.025
and a cheesy comfort chicken pasta.

00:19:20.025 --> 00:19:21.360
It's too gooey.

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:23.996
We have the spiced Tomato Twist veg pasta

00:19:23.996 --> 00:19:26.798
and the spiced Tomato Twist non-veg pasta.

00:19:26.798 --> 00:19:30.102
If you come to Pizza Hut to order pasta,

00:19:30.102 --> 00:19:31.904
I hope we never cross paths.

00:19:31.904 --> 00:19:33.839
Nikhil, you have no idea.

00:19:33.839 --> 00:19:36.475
We absolutely love our
carbs in this country.

00:19:36.475 --> 00:19:37.476
And as you can see,

00:19:37.476 --> 00:19:41.046
we have bowls and bowls of
carbs that we call pasta.

00:19:41.046 --> 00:19:44.449
You can get four exclusive
oven-baked pastas

00:19:44.449 --> 00:19:47.553
at pa -- pasta hut. At Pizza Hut.

00:19:48.554 --> 00:19:51.089
I'm not eating any of these.
They all taste terrible.

00:19:51.089 --> 00:19:52.224
All right? The end.

00:19:52.224 --> 00:19:56.295
You can get a oven-baked
chicken Alfredo. Don't get this.

00:19:56.295 --> 00:19:57.896
Or, if you don't like chicken,

00:19:57.896 --> 00:20:00.632
you can just get cheesy Alfredo.

00:20:00.632 --> 00:20:03.168
And then, of course, we have
the Italian meats pasta,

00:20:03.168 --> 00:20:04.836
which is pepperoni and Italian sausage.

00:20:04.836 --> 00:20:08.640
I mean, oh, Italy. Oh, Italy.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:09.875
I'm so sorry.

00:20:09.875 --> 00:20:13.579
And, lastly, the oven-baked veggie pasta.

00:20:13.579 --> 00:20:16.315
I mean, this is a doorstop.

00:20:17.783 --> 00:20:21.019
I can't stand the Pizza Hut pasta.

00:20:21.019 --> 00:20:22.187
I cannot stand it.

00:20:22.187 --> 00:20:25.190
You see the sauces. You
know what time it is.

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:26.558
Sauce talk.

00:20:26.558 --> 00:20:29.761
Starting down here, get
yourself blue cheese sauce,

00:20:29.761 --> 00:20:32.164
then get ranch.

00:20:32.164 --> 00:20:34.233
Ooh, a garlic sauce.

00:20:34.233 --> 00:20:36.435
We can have a honey barbecue sauce,

00:20:36.435 --> 00:20:40.038
a medium Buffalo sauce,
and a side of marinara,

00:20:40.038 --> 00:20:42.107
just for dipping your breadsticks.

00:20:42.107 --> 00:20:46.044
And also icing, the Cinnabon
icing for the Cinnabuns.

00:20:46.044 --> 00:20:47.079
And there's a note that says,

00:20:47.079 --> 00:20:50.849
"I really want to see Joe dipping
some pizza in the frosting

00:20:50.849 --> 00:20:52.351
and eat it."

00:20:53.986 --> 00:20:55.153
[sighs]

00:20:56.054 --> 00:20:57.356
Give me this.

00:21:03.729 --> 00:21:04.696
Oh!

00:21:06.031 --> 00:21:06.999
Actually ...

00:21:06.999 --> 00:21:09.268
At first I was like, yuck,
but this is kind of good.

00:21:09.268 --> 00:21:11.737
And now on to dips. You dips---s.

00:21:11.737 --> 00:21:14.940
First off, we have tomato ketchup. Ha ha.

00:21:17.843 --> 00:21:18.910
[crew laughing]

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:21.079
Then we have a mayonnaise.

00:21:21.079 --> 00:21:23.048
Fun fact: It's veg mayonnaise,

00:21:23.048 --> 00:21:24.516
doesn't have any egg, because a huge

00:21:24.516 --> 00:21:28.220
population of this country
is pure vegetarians,

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:29.855
which means that they don't eat anything

00:21:29.855 --> 00:21:32.291
from an animal, even egg.

00:21:32.291 --> 00:21:34.059
Then we have a cheese dip.

00:21:34.059 --> 00:21:36.361
And finally, it's a Schezwan sauce.

00:21:36.361 --> 00:21:37.829
And they serve it with the momos,

00:21:37.829 --> 00:21:39.531
they serve it with a
bunch of other things.

00:21:43.368 --> 00:21:44.202
Yeah.

00:21:44.202 --> 00:21:46.471
We got desserts you're
not gonna find in India.

00:21:46.471 --> 00:21:49.474
That includes, down here,
the cinnamon sticks.

00:21:49.474 --> 00:21:52.944
They're like breadsticks, only cinnamony.

00:21:52.944 --> 00:21:55.681
Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho.

00:21:55.681 --> 00:21:57.616
Get your mind out of the gutter.

00:21:57.616 --> 00:21:59.351
And moving on, we have here are the

00:21:59.351 --> 00:22:02.220
Cinnabon mini cinnamon rolls.

00:22:02.220 --> 00:22:05.924
This is the triple chocolate brownie.

00:22:05.924 --> 00:22:07.959
If I had to guess, 2 pounds.

00:22:07.959 --> 00:22:10.696
What do we got here? The
ultimate chocolate chip cookie.

00:22:12.864 --> 00:22:13.732
Right?

00:22:13.732 --> 00:22:15.400
This is like a Frisbee.

00:22:16.768 --> 00:22:19.905
And for all you sweetie pies
out there with sweet tooths,

00:22:19.905 --> 00:22:22.341
here are India's exclusive desserts,

00:22:22.341 --> 00:22:26.511
starting with a choco lava cake, baby!

00:22:26.511 --> 00:22:27.646
Ooh!

00:22:28.613 --> 00:22:29.848
Molten.

00:22:29.848 --> 00:22:33.618
The choco lava cake in
Domino's? Much better.

00:22:33.618 --> 00:22:35.087
Next up, you get a whole
range of ice cream.

00:22:35.087 --> 00:22:36.288
Some Kwality Wall's,

00:22:36.288 --> 00:22:39.157
one of India's biggest
ice cream manufacturers.

00:22:39.157 --> 00:22:42.594
You can get a tiny tub of
Choco-Tastic Supreme Sundae.

00:22:42.594 --> 00:22:45.163
Then you can get a Cornetto, a cone.

00:22:45.163 --> 00:22:47.833
Super delicious. And I
really love the end of this,

00:22:47.833 --> 00:22:49.768
because it's just a block of chocolate,

00:22:49.768 --> 00:22:52.371
and I used to fight over
this with my friends.

00:22:52.371 --> 00:22:55.340
Then you get a Magnum.
Everybody loves a Magnum.

00:22:55.340 --> 00:22:59.211
And finally, you can even get
a family pack of ice cream.

00:22:59.211 --> 00:23:00.412
Soda!

00:23:00.412 --> 00:23:03.181
Last exclusive are, of course, the drinks.

00:23:03.181 --> 00:23:06.017
Both countries have Pepsi,
but the Pizza Hut in the US

00:23:06.017 --> 00:23:10.021
you can also get wild
cherry Pepsi, orange Crush,

00:23:10.021 --> 00:23:11.656
Mountain Dew, baby!

00:23:11.656 --> 00:23:13.525
Sierra Mist, which they didn't have,

00:23:13.525 --> 00:23:15.594
and Aquafina.

00:23:15.594 --> 00:23:18.263
Here in Pizza Hut India,
our exclusive drink options

00:23:18.263 --> 00:23:22.334
are Pepsi, 7Up, Mirinda, and Pepsi black.

00:23:22.334 --> 00:23:24.369
They also serve an iced
tea at the restaurant,

00:23:24.369 --> 00:23:26.304
but they don't deliver it, unfortunately.

00:23:26.304 --> 00:23:28.306
I would've gone for the iced tea.

00:23:31.042 --> 00:23:33.445
All right, now let's take a
look at Pizza Hut's pricing,

00:23:33.445 --> 00:23:35.514
particularly some clever marketing tricks

00:23:35.514 --> 00:23:37.315
they're using to make you
believe you're getting

00:23:37.315 --> 00:23:39.785
more value for money
than you actually are.

00:23:39.785 --> 00:23:43.288
In the US, a medium cheese
pizza on the pan crust

00:23:43.288 --> 00:23:46.425
will cost you $13.49.

00:23:46.425 --> 00:23:49.027
In India, a medium Margherita
pizza will cost you

00:23:49.027 --> 00:23:53.565
319 rupees, which is
currently 3.93 US dollars.

00:23:53.565 --> 00:23:56.802
That means over here you
are paying 11.9 cents

00:23:56.802 --> 00:23:58.870
per square inch of pizza.

00:23:58.870 --> 00:23:59.938
While over here in India,

00:23:59.938 --> 00:24:03.842
you're just paying 4.4 cents
per square inch of pizza.

00:24:03.842 --> 00:24:07.913
That makes the US pizza
170% more expensive.

00:24:07.913 --> 00:24:09.681
Generally with pizza, the more you buy,

00:24:09.681 --> 00:24:10.749
the cheaper it gets.

00:24:10.749 --> 00:24:15.720
A US large has a surface
area of 153.9 square inches

00:24:15.720 --> 00:24:18.557
and costs $15.49.

00:24:18.557 --> 00:24:21.626
That brings the cost per
square inch down to 10 cents,

00:24:21.626 --> 00:24:24.696
making it 15% cheaper than the medium.

00:24:24.696 --> 00:24:28.433
Ladies and gentlemen, it's
time for pizza pop quiz!

00:24:28.433 --> 00:24:30.735
Which has the higher surface area,

00:24:30.735 --> 00:24:35.006
one medium pizza or two personal pizzas?

00:24:35.006 --> 00:24:38.910
If you said two personal
pizzas, congratulations!

00:24:38.910 --> 00:24:40.111
You're an idiot.

00:24:40.111 --> 00:24:42.547
Because when it comes to
calculating the surface area

00:24:42.547 --> 00:24:44.950
of a circle, small changes in diameter

00:24:44.950 --> 00:24:47.886
can create huge differences
in surface area.

00:24:47.886 --> 00:24:50.856
On the Pizza Hut India website,
you can get a combo offer

00:24:50.856 --> 00:24:54.493
of two personal pan pizzas for rupees 279.

00:24:54.493 --> 00:24:57.963
However, a medium pizza
costs pretty much the same.

00:24:57.963 --> 00:25:01.066
But I guess if you want two
different flavors of pizza,

00:25:01.066 --> 00:25:03.468
it makes sense to go with the combo.

00:25:05.770 --> 00:25:07.906
In this medium cheese pan-crust pizza,

00:25:07.906 --> 00:25:10.008
it is 1,940 calories,

00:25:10.008 --> 00:25:14.980
79 grams of total fat, 33
grams of saturated fat,

00:25:14.980 --> 00:25:19.417
224 grams of carbs, and
the sodium, oh, boy,

00:25:19.417 --> 00:25:22.454
3,480 milligrams.

00:25:22.454 --> 00:25:25.390
A medium Margherita pizza
in India will cost you

00:25:25.390 --> 00:25:27.993
1,377 calories,

00:25:27.993 --> 00:25:30.529
total fat 40.29 grams,

00:25:30.529 --> 00:25:33.298
of which saturates are 14.7 grams,

00:25:33.298 --> 00:25:35.433
carbohydrates, 192 grams,

00:25:35.433 --> 00:25:40.005
and 2,717 milligrams of sodium.

00:25:40.005 --> 00:25:40.839
Yikes.

00:25:40.839 --> 00:25:43.074
Now, the American stats look a lot worse,

00:25:43.074 --> 00:25:44.809
but I do want to point out that our medium

00:25:44.809 --> 00:25:46.311
is much larger than India's.

00:25:46.311 --> 00:25:48.780
So if you break it down per square inch,

00:25:48.780 --> 00:25:51.416
you'll see that the US version

00:25:51.416 --> 00:25:53.451
does have more fat and more saturated fat,

00:25:53.451 --> 00:25:55.720
but India's pizza actually contains

00:25:55.720 --> 00:25:58.723
more calories, carbs, and sodium.

00:25:58.723 --> 00:26:02.661
But what about the most calorific
item on the Indian menu?

00:26:02.661 --> 00:26:04.829
If you really want to mess up your day,

00:26:04.829 --> 00:26:09.200
you have to order the medium
veg Surprise Kebab pizza

00:26:09.200 --> 00:26:12.203
with veg-kebab-stuffed crust.

00:26:12.203 --> 00:26:14.739
A whole one of these pizzas will contain

00:26:14.739 --> 00:26:17.876
2,673 calories.

00:26:17.876 --> 00:26:21.212
That's 133.65% of your daily

00:26:21.212 --> 00:26:23.381
caloric-intake allowance.

00:26:23.381 --> 00:26:25.083
Oh, my God.

00:26:25.083 --> 00:26:28.320
OK, the calories are high,
but the sodium is even higher.

00:26:28.320 --> 00:26:32.424
There is 6,344 milligrams
of sodium in here,

00:26:32.424 --> 00:26:37.262
which is 275% of your daily
recommended allowance.

00:26:37.262 --> 00:26:40.031
What about the most calorific
pizza in the US, you ask?

00:26:40.031 --> 00:26:44.069
Well, that would be a large
pan-crusted Meat Lover's,

00:26:44.069 --> 00:26:45.870
which this isn't.

00:26:45.870 --> 00:26:48.039
So imagine it bigger and thicker. OK.

00:26:48.039 --> 00:26:50.675
An entire one of these contains a whopping

00:26:50.675 --> 00:26:53.311
3,570 calories.

00:26:53.311 --> 00:26:56.147
That's 178% of your daily allowance.

00:26:56.147 --> 00:26:59.517
And the sodium is even
worse than that of India's.

00:26:59.517 --> 00:27:03.455
There's 7,150 milligrams
of sodium in here.

00:27:03.455 --> 00:27:06.558
That is 298%

00:27:06.558 --> 00:27:08.693
your daily recommended amount.

00:27:09.260 --> 00:27:10.762
Nikhil: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:27:10.762 --> 00:27:12.163
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:27:12.163 --> 00:27:14.966
between Dunkin' Donuts
in India and in the US.

00:27:14.966 --> 00:27:16.901
This is "Food Wars."

00:27:20.572 --> 00:27:22.574
Here in the US, you can get your doughnuts

00:27:22.574 --> 00:27:25.644
in one; six, or a half dozen;

00:27:25.644 --> 00:27:29.180
or 12, aka a dozen.

00:27:29.180 --> 00:27:30.915
Don't put that in there.

00:27:30.915 --> 00:27:32.450
Here in India, you can get your doughnuts

00:27:32.450 --> 00:27:36.488
in packs of one, three, or six.

00:27:36.488 --> 00:27:40.425
One US sticky glazed doughnut.

00:27:40.425 --> 00:27:41.559
Nikhil: Indian glazed doughnut.

00:27:41.559 --> 00:27:43.428
Joe: It weighs ...

00:27:43.428 --> 00:27:44.529
Nikhil: 49 grams.

00:27:44.529 --> 00:27:46.164
Joe: 59 grams.

00:27:46.164 --> 00:27:49.234
In the US, we have four
sizes of hot coffee.

00:27:49.234 --> 00:27:52.337
The small, the medium, the large,

00:27:52.337 --> 00:27:54.272
which, unfortunately, they forgot.

00:27:54.272 --> 00:27:56.207
Dunkin'!

00:27:56.207 --> 00:27:57.976
And the extra large.

00:27:57.976 --> 00:27:59.511
Here in India, our filter coffee

00:27:59.511 --> 00:28:02.247
comes in one size, this one.

00:28:02.247 --> 00:28:03.782
If you're wondering what filter coffee is,

00:28:03.782 --> 00:28:06.551
it's one of the most popular
drinks here in India.

00:28:06.551 --> 00:28:08.953
It's made by taking a decoction of coffee,

00:28:08.953 --> 00:28:11.122
mixing it with sweetened milk,

00:28:11.122 --> 00:28:12.624
and typically when they're preparing it,

00:28:12.624 --> 00:28:16.061
they pour it from a huge
height to create this froth.

00:28:16.061 --> 00:28:18.563
It's super delicious,
and it's very strong.

00:28:18.563 --> 00:28:20.198
It'll wake you right up in the morning.

00:28:20.198 --> 00:28:22.400
As for our other drinks,
they come in two sizes.

00:28:22.400 --> 00:28:24.736
Either medium or large.

00:28:24.736 --> 00:28:26.171
This is an Americano.

00:28:26.171 --> 00:28:28.740
Let's weigh it to see how much we got.

00:28:28.740 --> 00:28:31.476
I might have to go to
the bathroom after this.

00:28:31.476 --> 00:28:34.479
10.14 fluid ounces.

00:28:34.479 --> 00:28:35.947
If that's not enough for you,

00:28:35.947 --> 00:28:39.017
Dunkin's in the US also has a Box 'O Joe,

00:28:39.017 --> 00:28:42.620
which contains 100 ounces of hot coffee.

00:28:42.620 --> 00:28:43.955
And ...

00:28:43.955 --> 00:28:45.223
[groaning]

00:28:45.223 --> 00:28:46.791
Guzh!

00:28:46.791 --> 00:28:47.792
Oh, yeah.

00:28:49.661 --> 00:28:50.929
Oh, yeah.

00:28:50.929 --> 00:28:52.530
This should be the extra large.

00:28:52.530 --> 00:28:56.267
In the US, we "only" have
three iced-coffee sizes.

00:28:56.267 --> 00:28:58.503
The small, the medium, and the large.

00:28:58.503 --> 00:29:00.705
No extra large, but they did remember

00:29:00.705 --> 00:29:02.841
the large iced coffee,
so, thanks, Dunkin'.

00:29:02.841 --> 00:29:04.609
So, the Dunkin' India website says

00:29:04.609 --> 00:29:05.910
that they serve an iced Americano.

00:29:05.910 --> 00:29:08.747
But we asked three
outlets here in Bengaluru,

00:29:08.747 --> 00:29:10.582
and they said no iced Americano.

00:29:10.582 --> 00:29:11.416
We even asked them,

00:29:11.416 --> 00:29:13.184
"Hey, can you put some
ice in our Americano?"

00:29:13.184 --> 00:29:14.018
They said no.

00:29:14.018 --> 00:29:16.254
So if you really must have an Americano

00:29:16.254 --> 00:29:18.523
that's iced from Dunkin',

00:29:18.523 --> 00:29:20.325
you have to take your
own ice and go there.

00:29:24.262 --> 00:29:26.097
So, what's the large?

00:29:26.097 --> 00:29:27.232
Is this supposed to be 32?

00:29:27.232 --> 00:29:28.333
I mean, I think it's --

00:29:28.333 --> 00:29:30.769
Yeah, cup says 32, it's supposed to be 32.

00:29:30.769 --> 00:29:34.405
Yuelei, zoom in on that
and shame this business!

00:29:34.405 --> 00:29:35.940
32?

00:29:38.042 --> 00:29:39.444
This is everything that
you'll find on the menu

00:29:39.444 --> 00:29:42.614
at Dunkin' Donuts India that
you will not find in the US.

00:29:42.614 --> 00:29:45.316
Here is everything you can
get in a US Dunkin' Donuts

00:29:45.316 --> 00:29:47.252
you can't get in India.

00:29:47.252 --> 00:29:51.156
Let's start off with this
one. It is called Choco Villa.

00:29:51.156 --> 00:29:52.090
And I think it's called that

00:29:52.090 --> 00:29:53.925
because there's a little
triangle of chocolate,

00:29:53.925 --> 00:29:56.628
which looks like those houses
we used to draw as kids.

00:29:59.130 --> 00:30:00.932
Oh, my God.

00:30:00.932 --> 00:30:02.200
Yum!

00:30:02.200 --> 00:30:04.903
It's filled with my favorite
doughnut filling ever,

00:30:04.903 --> 00:30:06.671
which is Bavarian cream.

00:30:06.671 --> 00:30:08.239
Choco almond.

00:30:10.642 --> 00:30:13.011
Hm, it's OK.

00:30:13.011 --> 00:30:15.113
It's filled with the Bavarian cream again.

00:30:17.382 --> 00:30:20.018
With the cream, unreal.

00:30:20.018 --> 00:30:22.720
On to the next one. This
is called a Chocoholic.

00:30:22.720 --> 00:30:25.957
It's got a piece of KitKat
sticking through it.

00:30:25.957 --> 00:30:28.259
I want to see if it's one KitKat
bar or if they've taken two

00:30:28.259 --> 00:30:30.061
and they've sandwiched them together.

00:30:30.061 --> 00:30:31.563
Let's pull from this end.

00:30:31.563 --> 00:30:33.264
Yeah, I was right.

00:30:35.533 --> 00:30:38.069
If you're a chocoholic,
this is the one for you.

00:30:38.069 --> 00:30:41.706
The inside has also got
chocolaty filling in there.

00:30:41.706 --> 00:30:44.976
Chocolate is starting to
hit me real hard right now.

00:30:44.976 --> 00:30:46.644
This stuff is so sweet.

00:30:46.644 --> 00:30:48.847
This is called Rainbow Crunch.

00:30:51.382 --> 00:30:52.183
Oh.

00:30:52.183 --> 00:30:54.919
There's strawberry frosting on top.

00:30:54.919 --> 00:30:57.255
So this has a strawberry taste.

00:30:57.255 --> 00:30:59.123
It's OK. It's a doughnut.

00:30:59.123 --> 00:31:01.326
Next up, we have Cookie Delight.

00:31:01.326 --> 00:31:02.360
It's called Cookie Delight

00:31:02.360 --> 00:31:05.396
'cause they've taken cookie
powder and smacked it on top.

00:31:05.396 --> 00:31:06.998
This one's called Crispy Crunch.

00:31:06.998 --> 00:31:09.234
For people who have trypophobia,

00:31:09.234 --> 00:31:11.069
this one is probably not for you.

00:31:13.371 --> 00:31:15.506
Oh, my God, this ain't it.

00:31:15.506 --> 00:31:18.109
The crispy stuff on top
is just not working.

00:31:18.109 --> 00:31:20.812
Again, however, they do have
the Bavarian cream inside --

00:31:21.713 --> 00:31:25.016
I feel like there's a hurricane
inside my body right now.

00:31:25.016 --> 00:31:28.386
Next up, we have a
doughnut called the Gemmy.

00:31:28.386 --> 00:31:31.990
My fellow Indians will recognize
that there are gems on top.

00:31:31.990 --> 00:31:35.526
This is one of the most nostalgic
chocolates here in India,

00:31:35.526 --> 00:31:37.629
and I've eaten them since I was a kid.

00:31:38.997 --> 00:31:39.831
Super yum.

00:31:42.500 --> 00:31:44.636
You'd think a kid would like them,

00:31:44.636 --> 00:31:47.138
but I can't even imagine
a kid version of myself

00:31:47.138 --> 00:31:49.073
liking something that's so overdosed

00:31:49.073 --> 00:31:50.541
with sweetness and chocolate.

00:31:50.541 --> 00:31:52.210
Is it Gemmy? Yes.

00:31:52.210 --> 00:31:54.212
Too Gemmy? Also yes.

00:31:54.212 --> 00:31:55.179
I'd avoid.

00:31:55.179 --> 00:31:57.615
So, I thought this was all
the exclusive signatures,

00:31:57.615 --> 00:32:00.051
but I've been told that
there are two more.

00:32:00.051 --> 00:32:02.921
And let's start off with this
one. It's called Choco Pop.

00:32:02.921 --> 00:32:05.056
It's got chocolate on
top, chocolate sprinkles,

00:32:05.056 --> 00:32:08.092
chocolate wavy line things,
and it's filled with chocolate.

00:32:08.092 --> 00:32:09.193
It's very sweet.

00:32:13.765 --> 00:32:14.933
Ah.

00:32:17.302 --> 00:32:19.070
Whew!

00:32:28.012 --> 00:32:28.980
All right.

00:32:28.980 --> 00:32:30.281
And on to our last doughnut.

00:32:30.281 --> 00:32:33.051
This one is called the Choco Berry Bomb.

00:32:35.586 --> 00:32:37.422
That's actually quite nice.

00:32:37.422 --> 00:32:40.591
It has definitely cut the
sweetness that I've experienced.

00:32:40.591 --> 00:32:43.428
There's, like, some berry jam inside,

00:32:43.428 --> 00:32:45.596
which is kind of tart and nice.

00:32:45.596 --> 00:32:49.033
The top is milk chocolate with
shavings of white chocolate.

00:32:49.033 --> 00:32:49.867
Whew!

00:32:49.867 --> 00:32:51.502
Yeah, it's a good doughnut.

00:32:51.502 --> 00:32:53.271
I wouldn't order it. It's too much.

00:32:53.271 --> 00:32:54.973
All of this, I would
not order any of these.

00:32:54.973 --> 00:32:56.040
They're too much.

00:32:56.040 --> 00:32:58.276
Exclusive doughnuts you can get in the US

00:32:58.276 --> 00:33:00.211
you can't get in India.

00:33:00.211 --> 00:33:03.314
Now, we're filming this
the first week of October.

00:33:03.314 --> 00:33:06.484
Of course, the No. 1 flavor
you get this month is pumpkin.

00:33:08.252 --> 00:33:10.188
Mm, so pumpkiny.

00:33:10.188 --> 00:33:11.923
Yeah, this tastes just like pumpkin pie.

00:33:11.923 --> 00:33:14.926
Also, you can get yourself
a glazed blueberry doughnut.

00:33:14.926 --> 00:33:15.893
See? Look at that.

00:33:15.893 --> 00:33:19.063
Glaze on top, blueberry
dough on the inside.

00:33:19.063 --> 00:33:21.032
Also delicious. Love it.

00:33:21.032 --> 00:33:24.936
Glazed chocolate. Figured
this was everywhere, right?

00:33:26.871 --> 00:33:27.705
So good.

00:33:27.705 --> 00:33:29.407
Ooh, Boston cream.

00:33:29.407 --> 00:33:31.009
The Ben Affleck of doughnuts.

00:33:31.009 --> 00:33:32.043
Looks like a regular doughnut,

00:33:32.043 --> 00:33:33.411
doesn't it, everyone in India?

00:33:33.411 --> 00:33:34.645
But

00:33:35.747 --> 00:33:38.516
surprise, there's cream on the inside!

00:33:38.516 --> 00:33:39.450
I know everyone likes doughnuts,

00:33:39.450 --> 00:33:40.351
maybe I haven't had a doughnut in a while,

00:33:40.351 --> 00:33:42.253
but crap, this is really good.

00:33:42.253 --> 00:33:43.354
One of my favorites.

00:33:43.354 --> 00:33:44.422
I f--- with these.

00:33:44.422 --> 00:33:46.491
Double chocolate, maybe my favorite,

00:33:46.491 --> 00:33:48.126
'cause they just did what they had to do.

00:33:48.126 --> 00:33:50.395
Take a chocolate doughnut and
put that chocolate frosting

00:33:50.395 --> 00:33:53.331
I like right on top of
it. A double threat.

00:33:53.331 --> 00:33:54.565
Oh, these are so good.

00:33:56.801 --> 00:33:59.170
I am in heaven!

00:33:59.170 --> 00:34:02.540
A strawberry frosting with sprinkles?

00:34:02.540 --> 00:34:03.875
You don't got this?

00:34:03.875 --> 00:34:05.943
This is, like, the Homer
Simpson doughnut, right?

00:34:05.943 --> 00:34:08.279
This is the one that you
always see him eating.

00:34:08.279 --> 00:34:10.081
Oh, the vanilla cream.

00:34:10.081 --> 00:34:12.050
Gotta say, don't think I've
ever had this one before.

00:34:15.253 --> 00:34:16.354
Look at me.

00:34:16.354 --> 00:34:18.623
It's like "Scarface" over
here. I'm just covered.

00:34:18.623 --> 00:34:19.590
A little much.

00:34:19.590 --> 00:34:20.925
Ugh! Ugh!

00:34:20.925 --> 00:34:22.026
Oh, God.

00:34:22.026 --> 00:34:24.228
Here's some powder right here.

00:34:24.228 --> 00:34:25.229
Powdered doughnut.

00:34:25.229 --> 00:34:26.664
India, you don't know what this is?

00:34:26.664 --> 00:34:28.633
C'mon. It's, like, doughnut No. 1, right?

00:34:30.835 --> 00:34:33.704
Also in the US you can get a
vanilla frosted with sprinkles,

00:34:33.704 --> 00:34:36.474
and a bear claw, which they
unfortunately did not have

00:34:36.474 --> 00:34:37.742
at the time of shooting this.

00:34:37.742 --> 00:34:39.911
Anyway, ah.

00:34:39.911 --> 00:34:42.547
Munchkins? You guys don't got Munchkins?

00:34:42.547 --> 00:34:43.915
What?

00:34:43.915 --> 00:34:45.650
We have a variety of Munchkin flavors,

00:34:45.650 --> 00:34:49.487
but this one specifically
is the pumpkin Munchkin,

00:34:49.487 --> 00:34:51.389
and,

00:34:51.389 --> 00:34:52.723
mm!

00:34:53.691 --> 00:34:56.294
Tastes just like pumpkin pie. Fantastic.

00:34:56.294 --> 00:34:58.896
Hey, guys, we're now on to a
different category of doughnuts

00:34:58.896 --> 00:35:00.832
called the all-time favorites.

00:35:00.832 --> 00:35:03.835
I took a quick hospital visit,
and I'm completely fine now.

00:35:03.835 --> 00:35:05.703
I'm sorry about the madness

00:35:05.703 --> 00:35:08.339
from the previous set of doughnuts.

00:35:08.339 --> 00:35:11.075
I'm fine now. I don't
know what came over me.

00:35:11.075 --> 00:35:14.479
OK, so we'll start off with
this specimen over here.

00:35:14.479 --> 00:35:16.547
It's called a Cookie Cartwheel.

00:35:16.547 --> 00:35:19.183
Adorable name, and, yes,
it does look like a wheel.

00:35:19.183 --> 00:35:21.319
I like how they put the white stripes.

00:35:23.654 --> 00:35:24.789
Yeah.

00:35:24.789 --> 00:35:26.090
It's sweet.

00:35:26.090 --> 00:35:27.525
Next up on our list is a doughnut

00:35:27.525 --> 00:35:28.793
that's not intimidating at all,

00:35:28.793 --> 00:35:32.597
it's only called Death by Chocolate.

00:35:32.597 --> 00:35:34.098
Will this kill me?

00:35:34.098 --> 00:35:35.099
Probably not.

00:35:35.099 --> 00:35:38.302
But will this give me some
diabetes if I eat too much?

00:35:38.302 --> 00:35:39.337
Absolutely.

00:35:39.337 --> 00:35:41.672
And for that reason,
it's a win in my book.

00:35:41.672 --> 00:35:44.342
If you thought Death
by Chocolate was scary,

00:35:44.342 --> 00:35:46.377
this is Alive by Chocolate.

00:35:46.377 --> 00:35:48.279
In terms of visual
differences, I can already tell

00:35:48.279 --> 00:35:50.781
this one has more of a
cookie crumble on top.

00:35:50.781 --> 00:35:53.384
They're very similar, as expected.

00:35:53.384 --> 00:35:56.654
I will say, this one, it feels more, like,

00:35:56.654 --> 00:36:00.057
it lifts your spirits
and you feel more alive.

00:36:00.057 --> 00:36:03.895
And this one will probably
put you to sleep, in a coma.

00:36:03.895 --> 00:36:06.164
So death and alive, it makes sense.

00:36:06.164 --> 00:36:10.635
[ears ringing]

00:36:12.336 --> 00:36:14.071
Mm, whoa!

00:36:14.071 --> 00:36:16.974
On to the next one. We
have something called

00:36:16.974 --> 00:36:19.644
Very Very Strawberry.

00:36:19.644 --> 00:36:22.413
Vanilla frosting on top,
it's got some pink streaks,

00:36:22.413 --> 00:36:25.583
and it looks to be stuffed
with strawberry jam.

00:36:25.583 --> 00:36:26.551
Which sounds amazing,

00:36:26.551 --> 00:36:28.886
especially after all
this chocolate overdose.

00:36:31.088 --> 00:36:32.957
It's sweet.

00:36:32.957 --> 00:36:34.225
Oh, my God.

00:36:34.225 --> 00:36:35.426
It's nice, though.

00:36:35.426 --> 00:36:37.662
All right, it's time
for our final doughnut,

00:36:37.662 --> 00:36:41.265
and this one is a bit of a boss battle.

00:36:41.265 --> 00:36:42.533
So, this is a doughnut eclair.

00:36:42.533 --> 00:36:45.736
It's called the Breakup Party Eclair.

00:36:45.736 --> 00:36:48.973
I guess because if you
go through a breakup,

00:36:48.973 --> 00:36:50.441
this is what you end up eating.

00:36:53.711 --> 00:36:56.714
So, the first few bites were quite nice.

00:36:56.714 --> 00:36:59.951
They weren't as sweet, and
they didn't feel as rich.

00:36:59.951 --> 00:37:02.486
But I realized most of the
chocolate is kind of centered

00:37:02.486 --> 00:37:05.256
towards the center of the eclair.

00:37:05.256 --> 00:37:07.992
And so it's a lot more
decadent the closer you get.

00:37:07.992 --> 00:37:11.362
Great for breakups, great as
a metaphor for what you feel

00:37:11.362 --> 00:37:12.797
when you're going through a breakup,

00:37:12.797 --> 00:37:15.600
and as a doughnut itself, pretty average.

00:37:15.600 --> 00:37:18.769
Both hot and cold espresso
and coffee drinks in the US

00:37:18.769 --> 00:37:21.706
have options for flavors
you can add as flavor shots,

00:37:21.706 --> 00:37:22.740
which are unsweetened,

00:37:22.740 --> 00:37:25.176
or flavor swirls, which
are sweet and creamy.

00:37:25.176 --> 00:37:29.280
Now, flavors unique to
the US include shots of

00:37:29.280 --> 00:37:32.316
vanilla, toasted almond, blueberry,

00:37:32.316 --> 00:37:34.518
raspberry, and coconut.

00:37:34.518 --> 00:37:37.154
And flavor swirls, you can get

00:37:37.154 --> 00:37:39.223
French vanilla and pumpkin.

00:37:39.223 --> 00:37:43.561
So, I went ahead and had each
one of those swirls and shots

00:37:43.561 --> 00:37:46.297
added to one coffee,
right here in front of me.

00:37:46.297 --> 00:37:49.133
We'll call it the Food Wars DrinkAroo.

00:37:49.133 --> 00:37:50.601
I don't know what it is.

00:37:50.601 --> 00:37:52.970
All the flavors in one drink.

00:37:52.970 --> 00:37:55.640
The lady when I ordered
it was like, "Really?"

00:37:55.640 --> 00:37:57.308
And I was like, "Really."

00:38:00.344 --> 00:38:02.179
Oh, God, this is so bad.

00:38:02.179 --> 00:38:03.347
Oh, ugh!

00:38:03.347 --> 00:38:05.116
Just blegh. Whoa!

00:38:05.116 --> 00:38:06.284
Oh, man.

00:38:07.251 --> 00:38:08.519
[exhales sharply]

00:38:08.519 --> 00:38:10.288
It's like, there's, like,
an electric charge to it

00:38:10.288 --> 00:38:12.089
at the end I don't quite understand.

00:38:14.025 --> 00:38:15.293
Mm.

00:38:15.293 --> 00:38:16.994
Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho!

00:38:16.994 --> 00:38:18.896
This is poison. Don't get it.

00:38:18.896 --> 00:38:19.997
All right, it's time for drinks.

00:38:19.997 --> 00:38:21.832
Let's start off with the cold options

00:38:21.832 --> 00:38:23.834
that we have here at Dunkin' India.

00:38:23.834 --> 00:38:26.203
The first one is a classic lemonade.

00:38:26.203 --> 00:38:27.238
Let's go ahead and try it.

00:38:27.238 --> 00:38:28.506
It looks very clear.

00:38:29.874 --> 00:38:31.008
That was nice. Refreshing.

00:38:31.008 --> 00:38:33.411
They have not made it too
sweet, and I kind of like it.

00:38:33.411 --> 00:38:35.446
Next up, we have a virgin mojito.

00:38:38.783 --> 00:38:42.019
I don't see why somebody
would go to Dunkin' Donuts,

00:38:42.019 --> 00:38:45.856
get a doughnut, and then a
virgin mojito on the side.

00:38:45.856 --> 00:38:48.192
Quick point to make: You can
get them in a small bottle,

00:38:48.192 --> 00:38:50.728
or you can even get
them in larger options.

00:38:50.728 --> 00:38:52.530
Next up, we have two flavors of iced tea.

00:38:52.530 --> 00:38:55.232
We have lemon and peach.
I'm going to try the peach.

00:38:57.435 --> 00:39:00.338
If I had to pick one of these,
this is the one I'd go for.

00:39:00.338 --> 00:39:03.941
Exclusive hot drinks here in
the US, we have these three.

00:39:03.941 --> 00:39:07.044
The first one is, like, a
specific coffee blend at Dunkin'

00:39:07.044 --> 00:39:09.013
called Dunkin' Midnight.

00:39:11.482 --> 00:39:14.318
Oh, wow, that has,
[stammers] that's strong.

00:39:14.318 --> 00:39:15.953
Wow.

00:39:15.953 --> 00:39:18.789
It's, like, really
strong. I kinda love it.

00:39:18.789 --> 00:39:21.926
Moving on, you can get
yourself a chai latte.

00:39:21.926 --> 00:39:24.829
India doesn't have chai
lattes? What's going on, guys?

00:39:24.829 --> 00:39:25.930
That's really good.

00:39:25.930 --> 00:39:27.631
And, of course, a matcha latte.

00:39:27.631 --> 00:39:29.166
No, not matcha.

00:39:29.166 --> 00:39:30.601
I hate matcha.

00:39:30.601 --> 00:39:32.002
That's the green one, right?

00:39:32.002 --> 00:39:34.171
Beverages that taste like lawn clippings.

00:39:35.906 --> 00:39:37.775
Mm-mm.

00:39:37.775 --> 00:39:38.843
Ugh. I hate it.

00:39:38.843 --> 00:39:40.845
All right, it's now
time for our milk-based

00:39:40.845 --> 00:39:42.513
cold beverages here in India.

00:39:42.513 --> 00:39:45.449
We have a range of frappés,
some iced shaken coffees.

00:39:45.449 --> 00:39:46.717
Let's start with the frappés.

00:39:46.717 --> 00:39:51.021
Coffee, caramel, and hazelnut.

00:39:51.021 --> 00:39:54.325
And they have a seasonal
flavor, which is Alphonso mango.

00:39:54.325 --> 00:39:56.961
If you've not heard of the
Alphonso variety of mangoes,

00:39:56.961 --> 00:39:58.529
it grows all over here in India,

00:39:58.529 --> 00:40:00.765
and it is the king of mangoes.

00:40:00.765 --> 00:40:02.366
You have to try it if you get a chance.

00:40:02.366 --> 00:40:03.334
I'm going to start off with this one,

00:40:03.334 --> 00:40:05.403
because I love mango-flavored anything.

00:40:07.538 --> 00:40:08.672
It's not bad.

00:40:08.672 --> 00:40:11.742
Next up, we have some shaken iced coffees

00:40:11.742 --> 00:40:15.479
in three flavors, caramel,
classic, and hazelnut.

00:40:15.479 --> 00:40:18.582
Also the classic flavored
shaken iced coffee,

00:40:18.582 --> 00:40:22.820
it's not as sweet, and I want
to put this one on a pedestal.

00:40:22.820 --> 00:40:24.655
Thank you.

00:40:24.655 --> 00:40:28.559
OK, next up, they also sell a
iced mocha and an iced latte.

00:40:28.559 --> 00:40:30.194
It's time for the chocolate milkshake,

00:40:30.194 --> 00:40:33.330
and can I just say, looks decadent.

00:40:33.330 --> 00:40:36.767
It's quite thick. It's kind of grainy.

00:40:36.767 --> 00:40:39.437
Like, you can taste the
graininess of the chocolate,

00:40:39.437 --> 00:40:41.272
which I like, but I don't know,

00:40:41.272 --> 00:40:42.773
some people might not like that.

00:40:42.773 --> 00:40:45.776
Some people might like really
smooth chocolate milkshakes.

00:40:45.776 --> 00:40:47.144
OK, so if you're traveling to India

00:40:47.144 --> 00:40:49.447
and you must eat at Dunkin',
I would recommend you have

00:40:49.447 --> 00:40:53.184
the Alphonso mango
frappé if it's in season.

00:40:53.184 --> 00:40:55.820
But I would also say, don't go to Dunkin',

00:40:55.820 --> 00:40:59.423
go to any juice shop, you'll
find them all across India,

00:40:59.423 --> 00:41:00.624
and they take fresh mangoes,

00:41:00.624 --> 00:41:01.959
and they make you a mango milkshake

00:41:01.959 --> 00:41:03.894
that will blow your mind.

00:41:03.894 --> 00:41:06.897
They'll put actual pieces
of Alphonso pulp in there,

00:41:06.897 --> 00:41:09.266
and you'll chew on it while
you drink your milkshake.

00:41:09.266 --> 00:41:10.167
Godsends.

00:41:10.167 --> 00:41:13.571
Joe: So, they made these
two hours ago. I'm sorry.

00:41:13.571 --> 00:41:14.972
Assume they don't look like this.

00:41:14.972 --> 00:41:16.841
Anyway, we have these
cold drinks in the US.

00:41:16.841 --> 00:41:17.775
They're called refreshers.

00:41:17.775 --> 00:41:19.310
They're actually pretty
good, surprisingly.

00:41:19.310 --> 00:41:23.380
Starting down here, we have
the strawberry dragon fruit.

00:41:23.380 --> 00:41:25.549
I am such a child. It's spelled

00:41:25.549 --> 00:41:30.454
S-T-R-A-W-D-R-G-N-F-R-T,

00:41:30.454 --> 00:41:32.656
and all I could think
of was "dragon fart."

00:41:34.558 --> 00:41:35.392
Wow, that's actually pretty good.

00:41:35.392 --> 00:41:36.894
Peach passion fruit.

00:41:36.894 --> 00:41:38.496
[laughing] F-R-T.

00:41:38.496 --> 00:41:40.764
I keep thinking "fart." I'm such a child.

00:41:40.764 --> 00:41:41.732
[fart tooting]

00:41:41.732 --> 00:41:44.401
Whoa! Blegh! What the hell?

00:41:44.401 --> 00:41:46.570
I think all the syrup went to the bottom.

00:41:46.570 --> 00:41:48.472
It's way stronger than it should be.

00:41:49.473 --> 00:41:51.275
Yeah, 'cause up top it's really weak.

00:41:51.275 --> 00:41:53.277
Somewhere between there's a
good sip, but I didn't find it.

00:41:53.277 --> 00:41:54.545
Anyway, all right.

00:41:54.545 --> 00:41:57.848
Peach passion fruit coconut.

00:41:57.848 --> 00:42:00.384
Oh, well this is -- is
that cool? Does that work?

00:42:03.521 --> 00:42:05.089
OK.

00:42:05.089 --> 00:42:06.156
Ah, no.

00:42:08.893 --> 00:42:10.494
Oh, gross. Yeah.

00:42:10.494 --> 00:42:12.663
The coconut ones are bad.

00:42:12.663 --> 00:42:14.198
Keeping it up on the cool drinks,

00:42:14.198 --> 00:42:16.233
you can get yourself a frozen coffee,

00:42:16.233 --> 00:42:19.803
a frozen matcha latte, a frozen chocolate,

00:42:19.803 --> 00:42:21.839
and, of course, the Coolattas.

00:42:21.839 --> 00:42:24.041
Wait, frozen hot chocolate?

00:42:24.041 --> 00:42:25.576
Isn't that just chocolate milk?

00:42:27.311 --> 00:42:29.914
Oh, man, that is strong.

00:42:29.914 --> 00:42:31.081
That is a milkshake.

00:42:31.081 --> 00:42:31.982
Yo.

00:42:33.918 --> 00:42:37.054
It's not terrible. The
flavor is very strong.

00:42:37.054 --> 00:42:39.990
This is apparently a blue raspberry.

00:42:39.990 --> 00:42:41.559
Think they have other flavors, but.

00:42:44.261 --> 00:42:47.264
Once upon a time, I
worked at a movie theater.

00:42:47.264 --> 00:42:48.232
Yes, really.

00:42:48.232 --> 00:42:51.936
But we figured out a way
to get into the syrup box,

00:42:51.936 --> 00:42:53.571
'cause fountain drinks,
it's syrup and soda water

00:42:53.571 --> 00:42:55.339
at the same time, and it mixes
right when you pour it in.

00:42:55.339 --> 00:42:56.941
It was a really dark color,

00:42:56.941 --> 00:42:58.309
and we dared each other to drink it.

00:42:58.309 --> 00:43:01.211
I remember it was so powerful,

00:43:01.211 --> 00:43:03.113
I thought I was gonna throw up.

00:43:03.113 --> 00:43:04.748
And I never experienced anything

00:43:04.748 --> 00:43:07.551
that powerful-flavored, until today.

00:43:07.551 --> 00:43:08.519
Surprise, surprise.

00:43:08.519 --> 00:43:11.121
Dunkin' Donuts also sells chai.

00:43:11.121 --> 00:43:13.490
So, you have two flavors,
this is ginger chai,

00:43:13.490 --> 00:43:15.459
and we have elaichi chai.

00:43:15.459 --> 00:43:18.963
Elaichi is cardamom.

00:43:18.963 --> 00:43:20.898
Ginger in Hindi is adrak.

00:43:20.898 --> 00:43:23.334
And it's just such a beautiful
word to say, oh, my God!

00:43:23.334 --> 00:43:25.035
Adrak chai!

00:43:26.503 --> 00:43:28.906
Oof, they've gone heavy
on the ginger for sure.

00:43:30.674 --> 00:43:33.110
As advertised, these do taste like

00:43:33.110 --> 00:43:35.512
elaichi, which is cardamom, and ginger.

00:43:35.512 --> 00:43:38.015
Yeah, they don't quite have the soul

00:43:38.015 --> 00:43:40.117
of a chai that you get on the roadside,

00:43:40.117 --> 00:43:43.253
but I really love how
Dunkin' has tried to do this.

00:43:43.253 --> 00:43:44.755
Makes you feel a little bit more at home,

00:43:44.755 --> 00:43:47.024
so thank you, Dunkin'.

00:43:47.024 --> 00:43:51.395
Sandwiches, and wraps, and
bagels, and breakfast stuff.

00:43:51.395 --> 00:43:53.097
Oh. My.

00:43:53.097 --> 00:43:54.498
Get a good look, India.

00:43:54.498 --> 00:43:56.467
We have a huge selection

00:43:56.467 --> 00:43:59.903
of non-doughnut-y breakfast sandwiches,

00:43:59.903 --> 00:44:01.538
variety stuff you can get.

00:44:01.538 --> 00:44:03.841
Oh, man, I hit a wall, and I apologize.

00:44:05.609 --> 00:44:06.443
And I'm back.

00:44:06.443 --> 00:44:10.214
You can get yourself maple
sugar bacon breakfast sandwich.

00:44:10.214 --> 00:44:13.951
We have these Wake-Up Wraps,
and Wake-Up Wraps are,

00:44:13.951 --> 00:44:17.021
I don't know, really
phoned-in breakfast tacos.

00:44:17.021 --> 00:44:18.422
I don't know how else to describe it.

00:44:18.422 --> 00:44:20.991
It's a tortilla. They put
the stuff they already had

00:44:20.991 --> 00:44:22.226
for the other sandwiches in there.

00:44:22.226 --> 00:44:23.327
They fold it over.

00:44:23.327 --> 00:44:25.029
I'll just grab one. You
can get yourself one,

00:44:25.029 --> 00:44:27.031
and oh, man, this thing is like ...

00:44:29.133 --> 00:44:29.967
[glass shattering]

00:44:29.967 --> 00:44:31.869
Hey, everyone watching this video,

00:44:31.869 --> 00:44:33.404
in the comments, let me know:

00:44:33.404 --> 00:44:36.106
I show you this, and then when I open it,

00:44:36.106 --> 00:44:38.475
are you more likely to
eat this or less likely?

00:44:38.475 --> 00:44:39.843
Let me know in the comments.

00:44:39.843 --> 00:44:41.578
Dunkin', nobody wants these.

00:44:41.578 --> 00:44:45.382
You can get yourself a
tomato pesto grilled cheese.

00:44:45.382 --> 00:44:47.951
Pesto's fine and all, but
when something has pesto on it

00:44:47.951 --> 00:44:49.286
and you don't realize it,
doesn't this look like --

00:44:49.286 --> 00:44:51.255
like, look at this green.
Does that look like,

00:44:51.255 --> 00:44:52.289
would you go, "Oh, it's pesto,"

00:44:52.289 --> 00:44:53.924
or would you be like, "Ugh,
I think that's moldy"?

00:44:53.924 --> 00:44:55.092
Also got the grilled cheese.

00:44:55.092 --> 00:44:57.061
Oh!

00:44:57.061 --> 00:45:00.064
[gavel thuds]

00:45:00.064 --> 00:45:02.900
Then you get yourself a
sourdough breakfast sandwich.

00:45:02.900 --> 00:45:06.270
Yo, these things solidified.

00:45:06.270 --> 00:45:08.072
Probably edible a few hours ago.

00:45:08.072 --> 00:45:09.339
I'll take a bite of this.

00:45:09.339 --> 00:45:10.908
Sausage, egg, and cheese.

00:45:12.576 --> 00:45:14.211
Yeah, not bad.

00:45:14.211 --> 00:45:15.312
Bacon, egg, and cheese.

00:45:15.312 --> 00:45:17.915
Somewhere encased in this
melted cheese is bacon,

00:45:17.915 --> 00:45:18.749
I assure you.

00:45:18.749 --> 00:45:22.920
There's also a turkey sausage,
egg, and cheese somewhere.

00:45:22.920 --> 00:45:27.191
Oh, you can also get bagels
at your Dunkin' Donuts.

00:45:27.191 --> 00:45:28.492
Why? I don't know.

00:45:28.492 --> 00:45:30.594
But you can get your bagels plain,

00:45:30.594 --> 00:45:33.363
cinnamon raisin, multigrain,

00:45:33.363 --> 00:45:36.800
sesame seed, and this one, everything.

00:45:36.800 --> 00:45:38.402
And you can get yourself
some cream cheeses,

00:45:38.402 --> 00:45:42.372
including garden veggie,
strawberry, and plain.

00:45:42.372 --> 00:45:44.041
Also you can get an avocado spread,

00:45:44.041 --> 00:45:45.609
which they did not include.

00:45:45.609 --> 00:45:47.211
Dunkin'!

00:45:47.211 --> 00:45:48.912
India, you're not gonna believe this.

00:45:48.912 --> 00:45:52.149
Our Dunkin' Donuts, you
can get a side of, [laughs]

00:45:52.149 --> 00:45:55.819
you can get a side of something
called snackin' bacon.

00:45:55.819 --> 00:45:57.755
What's snackin' bacon, you ask?

00:45:57.755 --> 00:46:00.657
It is a bag of bacon.

00:46:00.657 --> 00:46:02.092
Bagel minis.

00:46:02.092 --> 00:46:03.827
You can get plain and everything bagels.

00:46:03.827 --> 00:46:04.795
Here's one right now.

00:46:04.795 --> 00:46:06.630
I think these have cream
cheese inside of them.

00:46:07.831 --> 00:46:08.665
Yeah.

00:46:09.833 --> 00:46:11.835
I don't think I've ever
had one of these before.

00:46:13.637 --> 00:46:14.938
That's not a bad idea.

00:46:14.938 --> 00:46:16.006
Not bad, guys.

00:46:16.006 --> 00:46:18.709
Also in the US, you can get
an order of hash browns.

00:46:18.709 --> 00:46:21.845
Now, at Dunkin' Donuts,
apparently you can get these,

00:46:21.845 --> 00:46:22.746
what do we call these?

00:46:22.746 --> 00:46:24.281
Omelet bites?

00:46:24.281 --> 00:46:25.983
You get bacon, egg, and cheese

00:46:25.983 --> 00:46:27.351
or egg white and veggie.

00:46:27.351 --> 00:46:32.289
C'mon. This is straight
taken from Starbucks, right?

00:46:32.289 --> 00:46:34.558
We went to the Dunkin' India
website, and over there,

00:46:34.558 --> 00:46:37.127
on the menu, they claim to sell burgers

00:46:37.127 --> 00:46:39.129
and a few sides, like nachos.

00:46:39.129 --> 00:46:40.731
However, we went to the outlets,

00:46:40.731 --> 00:46:42.432
and the managers said
that they're phasing out

00:46:42.432 --> 00:46:45.202
all savory food in Dunkin' nationally.

00:46:45.202 --> 00:46:47.004
But he was kind enough to make us

00:46:47.004 --> 00:46:49.473
one single non-veg burger,

00:46:49.473 --> 00:46:51.909
just so that we get to taste
what it would've been like.

00:46:51.909 --> 00:46:53.977
It has a whole chicken piece in there,

00:46:53.977 --> 00:46:55.112
which is already kind of nice.

00:46:55.112 --> 00:46:58.448
Some onions, what looks
like tandoori mayo,

00:46:58.448 --> 00:47:00.984
and the bun. Looks pretty tasty.

00:47:05.122 --> 00:47:06.423
Oh, my God.

00:47:07.491 --> 00:47:09.059
That's actually really good.

00:47:09.059 --> 00:47:11.361
I've done many episodes of "Food Wars,"

00:47:11.361 --> 00:47:13.130
tasted many burgers from restaurants

00:47:13.130 --> 00:47:15.799
that are literally burger joints,

00:47:15.799 --> 00:47:18.702
and this literally rivals those burgers.

00:47:18.702 --> 00:47:19.837
This is pretty good.

00:47:19.837 --> 00:47:21.471
What's happening, Dunkin'?

00:47:21.471 --> 00:47:24.041
OK, so, the fact is that
Dunkin' has actually

00:47:24.041 --> 00:47:26.476
scaled down massively here in India.

00:47:26.476 --> 00:47:27.611
In Bengal, where we're filming,

00:47:27.611 --> 00:47:29.947
there used to be 20 Dunkin' Donut outlets.

00:47:29.947 --> 00:47:31.448
Now there are only three.

00:47:31.448 --> 00:47:33.383
So rumor has it that Dunkin' might be

00:47:33.383 --> 00:47:35.619
phasing out of India in general,

00:47:35.619 --> 00:47:38.488
and the decision is going to
be made in the coming weeks.

00:47:38.488 --> 00:47:41.191
So maybe this video is
the last remaining legacy

00:47:41.191 --> 00:47:42.659
of Dunkin' in India.

00:47:42.659 --> 00:47:46.697
And this is probably the last
burger that is ever eaten.

00:47:46.697 --> 00:47:48.198
Oh, dude, this might be the --

00:47:48.198 --> 00:47:51.134
guys, this might be the
last burger ever consumed

00:47:51.134 --> 00:47:53.036
from Dunkin' Donuts here in India.

00:47:56.073 --> 00:47:57.307
OK, let's talk price.

00:47:57.307 --> 00:48:00.444
This large Americano is rupees 139,

00:48:00.444 --> 00:48:03.013
which is currently $1.71.

00:48:03.013 --> 00:48:04.882
But keep in mind, at the
time that we're filming this,

00:48:04.882 --> 00:48:07.451
the Indian rupee is at an all-time low,

00:48:07.451 --> 00:48:08.852
so hopefully things will get better

00:48:08.852 --> 00:48:11.121
and this won't cost so much.

00:48:11.121 --> 00:48:14.725
That same drink in the US is $3.69,

00:48:14.725 --> 00:48:18.128
or 293.44 rupees.

00:48:18.128 --> 00:48:21.965
That's a 63.9% increase in price.

00:48:21.965 --> 00:48:24.368
OK, so the biggest menu item
that we have here in India

00:48:24.368 --> 00:48:25.802
is our box of six.

00:48:25.802 --> 00:48:27.104
Now, you can get two categories.

00:48:27.104 --> 00:48:29.640
You can get classic doughnuts,
which are a lot simpler,

00:48:29.640 --> 00:48:31.875
and it'll cost you rupees 399.

00:48:31.875 --> 00:48:33.577
Or you can get the favorites doughnuts,

00:48:33.577 --> 00:48:35.979
which we have here, which
are a lot more extravagant

00:48:35.979 --> 00:48:38.382
and will cost you rupees 499,

00:48:38.382 --> 00:48:41.184
which amounts to USD 6.12 right now.

00:48:41.184 --> 00:48:44.755
If you want 12 doughnuts, you
need to get two boxes of six,

00:48:44.755 --> 00:48:47.758
which will cost you rupees 998.

00:48:47.758 --> 00:48:52.129
For food, our biggest menu
item is a dozen doughnuts.

00:48:52.129 --> 00:48:53.797
$18.73,

00:48:53.797 --> 00:48:58.568
or 1,492.85 rupees.

00:48:58.568 --> 00:48:59.903
Thank you.

00:48:59.903 --> 00:49:03.173
Our biggest drink is
the Box O' Joe Avella.

00:49:03.173 --> 00:49:05.208
It's the most expensive single menu item.

00:49:05.208 --> 00:49:06.944
$27.48,

00:49:06.944 --> 00:49:10.881
or 2,190.25 rupees.

00:49:10.881 --> 00:49:12.883
Now, in India we have
something called a vada,

00:49:12.883 --> 00:49:15.485
which is pretty much a doughnut,

00:49:15.485 --> 00:49:17.321
but it's savory and it's fried.

00:49:17.321 --> 00:49:19.589
And I want to say that
those cost around 20 rupees,

00:49:19.589 --> 00:49:21.358
while this original glazed

00:49:21.358 --> 00:49:23.126
that I've bitten into a few times

00:49:23.126 --> 00:49:24.828
costs 85 rupees.

00:49:24.828 --> 00:49:27.864
So, it's important to know
this price difference,

00:49:27.864 --> 00:49:30.233
and people here will
definitely think about that

00:49:30.233 --> 00:49:31.935
before buying something like this.

00:49:36.173 --> 00:49:38.208
Nikhil, stop eating the props!

00:49:40.677 --> 00:49:43.013
OK, so Dunkin' Donuts
India has not released

00:49:43.013 --> 00:49:45.415
any of their nutritional
info out for the public.

00:49:45.415 --> 00:49:46.783
And they've not gotten back to us

00:49:46.783 --> 00:49:49.286
when we asked them for
information, as of now.

00:49:49.286 --> 00:49:51.655
However, I can confirm that one doughnut

00:49:51.655 --> 00:49:54.291
is probably less
nutritious than one salad.

00:49:55.792 --> 00:49:57.861
Let's talk about Dunkin' US nutrition,

00:49:57.861 --> 00:49:59.363
starting with the glazed doughnut.

00:49:59.363 --> 00:50:01.999
In the US, it has 360 calories,

00:50:01.999 --> 00:50:03.367
22 grams of fat,

00:50:03.367 --> 00:50:05.035
10 grams of saturated fat,

00:50:05.035 --> 00:50:07.404
420 milligrams of sodium --

00:50:07.404 --> 00:50:08.438
420.

00:50:08.438 --> 00:50:10.073
39 grams of carbs,

00:50:10.073 --> 00:50:12.109
and 18 grams of sugar.

00:50:12.109 --> 00:50:15.012
And let's compare that
doughnut to this one,

00:50:15.012 --> 00:50:16.179
the Boston cream.

00:50:16.179 --> 00:50:20.083
In the USA, a Boston
cream is 270 calories,

00:50:20.083 --> 00:50:21.284
11 grams of fat,

00:50:21.284 --> 00:50:23.620
320 milligrams of sodium,

00:50:23.620 --> 00:50:24.654
39 grams of carbs,

00:50:24.654 --> 00:50:26.656
and 18 grams of sugar.

00:50:26.656 --> 00:50:29.493
Dunkin' Donuts large iced
Dunkin' dark-roast coffee

00:50:29.493 --> 00:50:31.561
with cream and sugar, in the US,

00:50:31.561 --> 00:50:33.630
is 260 calories,

00:50:33.630 --> 00:50:34.898
12 grams of fat,

00:50:34.898 --> 00:50:36.933
and 37 grams of carbs.

00:50:36.933 --> 00:50:38.602
Now, assuming that the iced coffee

00:50:38.602 --> 00:50:40.570
is the same in the US and India,

00:50:40.570 --> 00:50:43.540
getting a large iced
coffee with cream and sugar

00:50:43.540 --> 00:50:46.009
and both the glazed and
a Boston cream doughnut

00:50:46.009 --> 00:50:48.178
is 890 calories.

00:50:48.178 --> 00:50:52.716
That's 35.6% of your daily calorie intake.

00:50:52.716 --> 00:50:53.717
Yo.

00:50:56.253 --> 00:50:57.888
Again, Dunkin' Donuts has not released

00:50:57.888 --> 00:51:00.190
any of their ingredients to the public.

00:51:00.190 --> 00:51:01.892
However, there is one huge difference

00:51:01.892 --> 00:51:03.627
between the US and Indian doughnuts,

00:51:03.627 --> 00:51:07.130
and that is that the Indian
doughnuts are all eggless.

00:51:07.130 --> 00:51:09.833
This is because a huge percentage
of Indians are vegetarian,

00:51:09.833 --> 00:51:13.070
especially Hindus, and so
they even consider eating egg

00:51:13.070 --> 00:51:15.338
as non-veg food, and so, yeah.

00:51:15.338 --> 00:51:18.175
Most fast-food restaurants
have decided to not use egg

00:51:18.175 --> 00:51:20.777
in any of their foods to
make it more accessible

00:51:20.777 --> 00:51:22.312
to a larger part of India.

00:51:22.312 --> 00:51:24.381
But the US does have it on its site,

00:51:24.381 --> 00:51:26.483
so we'll share with you
the ingredients right now.

00:51:26.483 --> 00:51:27.651
First up, the coffee.

00:51:27.651 --> 00:51:29.753
Regardless of getting it hot or cold,

00:51:29.753 --> 00:51:34.491
if you get it black, it's going
to be 100% arabica coffee.

00:51:34.491 --> 00:51:35.692
Nice. Now,

00:51:35.692 --> 00:51:37.461
if you want to add cream and sugar to it,

00:51:37.461 --> 00:51:39.663
then you are adding milk, cream,

00:51:39.663 --> 00:51:41.598
disodium phosphate as a stabilizer,

00:51:41.598 --> 00:51:44.734
sodium citrate as a stabilizer, and sugar.

00:51:44.734 --> 00:51:46.903
If you're going to be adding
flavor to your coffee drink,

00:51:46.903 --> 00:51:50.140
one flavor you can get in both
India and the US is caramel.

00:51:50.140 --> 00:51:54.010
And in the US, our caramel
flavor is made up of all this.

00:51:54.978 --> 00:51:56.913
In the US, our standard glazed doughnut

00:51:56.913 --> 00:51:59.249
is made up of all of these things.

00:52:00.417 --> 00:52:01.952
You think that's a lot?

00:52:01.952 --> 00:52:04.521
Here's everything in our
Boston cream doughnuts.

00:52:04.521 --> 00:52:07.557
Yikes, that's a lot of words.

00:52:07.757 --> 00:52:09.292
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:52:09.292 --> 00:52:10.627
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:52:10.627 --> 00:52:12.863
between Nando's in the UK and India.

00:52:12.863 --> 00:52:14.131
This is "Food Wars."

00:52:16.466 --> 00:52:18.068
If you're ordering chicken for one person,

00:52:18.068 --> 00:52:20.170
it comes in three sizes at a UK Nando's.

00:52:21.338 --> 00:52:22.906
As a quarter chicken,

00:52:22.906 --> 00:52:24.107
as a half chicken,

00:52:24.107 --> 00:52:26.910
or as a whole chicken.

00:52:26.910 --> 00:52:29.246
Chicken for one person
here at Nando's India

00:52:29.246 --> 00:52:30.113
comes in the form of

00:52:30.113 --> 00:52:32.549
a quarter chicken, which is one piece,

00:52:32.549 --> 00:52:35.252
or a half chicken, which is two pieces.

00:52:35.252 --> 00:52:36.686
You can also get a whole chicken,

00:52:36.686 --> 00:52:39.022
but it only comes in the
form of a sharing platter,

00:52:39.022 --> 00:52:41.625
the largest of which is a jumbo platter,

00:52:41.625 --> 00:52:44.594
two whole chickens and five large sides.

00:52:44.594 --> 00:52:48.198
I'm excited to eat this, but
all I need now is friends,

00:52:48.198 --> 00:52:50.333
so hit me up.

00:52:51.768 --> 00:52:54.137
The largest item in the
UK is the family platter.

00:52:54.137 --> 00:52:55.338
It comes with two whole chickens

00:52:55.338 --> 00:52:57.073
as well as five large sides.

00:52:57.073 --> 00:52:58.441
Family of one.

00:52:58.441 --> 00:52:59.509
I could eat this.

00:52:59.509 --> 00:53:01.178
What about some other things
from the Nando's menu?

00:53:01.178 --> 00:53:02.946
Well, in the UK, you can
get a grilled chicken burger

00:53:02.946 --> 00:53:04.314
in two sizes.

00:53:04.314 --> 00:53:06.082
As a single or as a double.

00:53:06.082 --> 00:53:08.118
Nando's India also sells chicken burgers

00:53:08.118 --> 00:53:11.154
and offers customers the
option to double their chicken,

00:53:11.154 --> 00:53:12.923
so you can get a single chicken burger

00:53:12.923 --> 00:53:14.791
or double it to a double chicken burger.

00:53:14.791 --> 00:53:16.326
Nando's India serves chicken wings,

00:53:16.326 --> 00:53:18.828
but only in one size, a pack of four.

00:53:18.828 --> 00:53:21.398
Wings from a UK Nando's
come in four portion sizes:

00:53:21.398 --> 00:53:22.699
as a three-piece,

00:53:22.699 --> 00:53:23.733
as a five-piece,

00:53:23.733 --> 00:53:24.801
as a 10-piece,

00:53:24.801 --> 00:53:26.269
and a 15-piece.

00:53:26.269 --> 00:53:27.571
It's really weird being the country

00:53:27.571 --> 00:53:28.939
with the bigger sizes for a change.

00:53:28.939 --> 00:53:30.507
Joe, I miss you.

00:53:30.507 --> 00:53:32.676
Now, the classic side for any
order of Nando's in the UK

00:53:32.676 --> 00:53:34.110
is a side of peri-peri chips.

00:53:34.110 --> 00:53:35.612
I'm allowed to call them chips, not fries,

00:53:35.612 --> 00:53:37.113
because Joe is not in this video.

00:53:37.113 --> 00:53:38.848
In the UK, these come in two sizes,

00:53:38.848 --> 00:53:40.150
regular and large.

00:53:40.150 --> 00:53:41.251
Here at Nando's India,

00:53:41.251 --> 00:53:44.588
they're advertised not
as chips but as fries,

00:53:44.588 --> 00:53:47.190
because that's what they
are, Harry, you weirdo.

00:53:47.190 --> 00:53:48.892
I'm going to weigh them.
You get them in two sizes,

00:53:48.892 --> 00:53:50.360
either regular or large.

00:53:50.360 --> 00:53:51.595
Let me weigh the regular.

00:53:54.998 --> 00:53:57.434
It's 100 grams on the dot. Nice.

00:53:57.434 --> 00:53:58.268
Next.

00:54:00.971 --> 00:54:03.740
418 grams.

00:54:03.740 --> 00:54:05.742
No, 408 grams.

00:54:05.742 --> 00:54:07.877
175 grams in the large.

00:54:07.877 --> 00:54:09.145
I don't know how to read.

00:54:10.947 --> 00:54:12.949
Here is everything on
the menu at a UK Nando's

00:54:12.949 --> 00:54:14.417
that you won't find in India.

00:54:14.417 --> 00:54:16.987
This is everything you'll find
on the menu at Nando's India

00:54:16.987 --> 00:54:18.989
that you will not find in the UK.

00:54:18.989 --> 00:54:19.889
We'll start with the chicken.

00:54:19.889 --> 00:54:21.124
Now, when you order chicken at Nando's,

00:54:21.124 --> 00:54:22.659
they'll ask you to pick a spice level.

00:54:22.659 --> 00:54:23.560
We have quite a few of these,

00:54:23.560 --> 00:54:25.895
most of which are shared
with India, except for two.

00:54:25.895 --> 00:54:27.764
Firstly, we have pimento spice.

00:54:27.764 --> 00:54:29.199
I think this is limited edition,

00:54:29.199 --> 00:54:31.101
and it sits somewhere
between medium and hot

00:54:31.101 --> 00:54:32.068
on the spice scale.

00:54:32.068 --> 00:54:34.404
And our other exclusive
spice is peri tamer.

00:54:34.404 --> 00:54:36.740
As the name suggests, this
is quite a mild, tame spice.

00:54:36.740 --> 00:54:40.010
It sits somewhere between mild
and basically plain chicken.

00:54:40.010 --> 00:54:42.212
I think it's a slightly sweeter glaze

00:54:42.212 --> 00:54:44.447
than you might find on the
regular peri-peri spice.

00:54:44.447 --> 00:54:45.982
Here in India, we just get our chicken

00:54:45.982 --> 00:54:48.585
in the classic scale of plain,

00:54:48.585 --> 00:54:50.820
lemon and herb, mild,

00:54:50.820 --> 00:54:53.890
hot, and extra hot.

00:54:53.890 --> 00:54:56.393
I'm willing to bet that our extra hot

00:54:56.393 --> 00:54:59.796
blows the UK extra hot out of the water.

00:54:59.796 --> 00:55:01.698
You see this tongue?

00:55:01.698 --> 00:55:03.833
This tongue can take spice.

00:55:03.833 --> 00:55:05.502
Oh, my God, is this some kind of joke?

00:55:05.502 --> 00:55:06.369
It's, like, tickling me.

00:55:06.369 --> 00:55:08.505
It's teasing me with spice.

00:55:08.505 --> 00:55:09.506
This is child's play.

00:55:09.506 --> 00:55:12.509
I will say, I love how the UK
Nando's has two extra flavors.

00:55:12.509 --> 00:55:15.045
I wish India Nando's experimented more.

00:55:15.045 --> 00:55:17.480
We're in India, dude!
There are so many spices!

00:55:17.480 --> 00:55:19.149
But what we lack in spices,

00:55:19.149 --> 00:55:20.550
we make up for in mains.

00:55:20.550 --> 00:55:24.020
No. 1, creamy cashew
chicken with spicy rice.

00:55:25.522 --> 00:55:26.690
Damn good.

00:55:26.690 --> 00:55:27.824
OK, now on to the next main.

00:55:27.824 --> 00:55:29.326
This is chicken cataplana.

00:55:29.326 --> 00:55:31.227
Cataplana is a type of Portuguese

00:55:31.227 --> 00:55:34.064
clam-shaped ... stove? Cooking pot?

00:55:34.064 --> 00:55:36.066
And they've also served
it with a yogurt dip.

00:55:36.066 --> 00:55:38.301
So using a cataplana
is apparently healthier

00:55:38.301 --> 00:55:40.437
because you end up using less fats

00:55:40.437 --> 00:55:42.172
to cook your meat and your veggies.

00:55:42.172 --> 00:55:44.841
Next up, we're having chicken espetada,

00:55:44.841 --> 00:55:49.279
or, as I like to call
it, chicken espe ta-da!

00:55:49.279 --> 00:55:52.148
I've been fired from this
show 16 times this season.

00:55:52.148 --> 00:55:53.917
I imagine they take the pieces of chicken,

00:55:53.917 --> 00:55:55.719
put them on skewers, put the marinade.

00:55:55.719 --> 00:55:58.955
So, Nando's is a Portuguese-inspired

00:55:58.955 --> 00:56:00.423
South African restaurant,

00:56:00.423 --> 00:56:03.126
so most of the recipes are
things that were developed

00:56:03.126 --> 00:56:06.863
by Portuguese explorers when
they were in South Africa.

00:56:06.863 --> 00:56:09.232
We also have a lot of
cuisine that's inspired

00:56:09.232 --> 00:56:13.403
by our former colonial
overlords back in Portugal.

00:56:13.403 --> 00:56:16.106
In fact, Goa, which is our
smallest state here in India,

00:56:16.106 --> 00:56:17.974
was where the Portuguese first settled,

00:56:17.974 --> 00:56:20.510
and so a lot of the cuisine is derived

00:56:20.510 --> 00:56:22.445
and inspired by Portuguese cuisine.

00:56:22.445 --> 00:56:23.913
We have a couple of
chicken mains of our own,

00:56:23.913 --> 00:56:25.482
starting with boneless thighs.

00:56:25.482 --> 00:56:27.317
These come in orders of
four, and you can get them

00:56:27.317 --> 00:56:29.552
in any of the standard
Nando's spice levels.

00:56:29.552 --> 00:56:31.688
And our other chicken exclusive is this,

00:56:31.688 --> 00:56:32.522
wing roulette.

00:56:32.522 --> 00:56:34.457
So, wing roulette is an order of 10 wings,

00:56:34.457 --> 00:56:36.626
and it's a variety of the Nando's spices.

00:56:36.626 --> 00:56:37.894
The idea is that you'll get some of these,

00:56:37.894 --> 00:56:38.762
share them with your friends,

00:56:38.762 --> 00:56:40.730
some of you might get hit
with an extra-hot wing,

00:56:40.730 --> 00:56:42.632
whereas others might get
off easy with a mild.

00:56:42.632 --> 00:56:45.402
When I go to Nando's, I'm
generally going for medium or hot.

00:56:45.402 --> 00:56:46.469
I'm not trying to be a hero.

00:56:46.469 --> 00:56:47.370
If I'm going for extra hot,

00:56:47.370 --> 00:56:48.905
I'm just not actually
going to taste the food.

00:56:48.905 --> 00:56:50.073
It's just going to kind of hurt.

00:56:50.073 --> 00:56:53.009
I may also add a little bit
of the garlic and herb sauce,

00:56:53.009 --> 00:56:54.511
which adds a little bit of spice to it,

00:56:54.511 --> 00:56:56.379
or also I've used ketchup in the past,

00:56:56.379 --> 00:56:58.615
which my friends have lambasted
me for, so don't do that.

00:57:00.083 --> 00:57:00.950
Good chicken, though.

00:57:00.950 --> 00:57:02.419
We also have some meal deals.

00:57:02.419 --> 00:57:04.254
These are more affordable options,

00:57:04.254 --> 00:57:06.089
and you will not find them in the UK.

00:57:06.089 --> 00:57:07.223
Let's start off with the first one,

00:57:07.223 --> 00:57:09.526
which is pulled-chicken sliders.

00:57:09.526 --> 00:57:12.662
Oh, my God, this is like gourmet dining.

00:57:12.662 --> 00:57:14.397
I think I would need to eat three of these

00:57:14.397 --> 00:57:16.399
to feel considerably full.

00:57:16.399 --> 00:57:18.268
Unfortunately, they only give you two.

00:57:18.268 --> 00:57:20.970
Next up is a pulled-chicken burger.

00:57:20.970 --> 00:57:23.506
Oh, my. Mother lode of chicken.

00:57:23.506 --> 00:57:25.241
That is a lot of pulled chicken.

00:57:25.241 --> 00:57:26.309
It needs a sauce.

00:57:26.309 --> 00:57:28.445
Did I just eat a part
that doesn't have sauce?

00:57:28.445 --> 00:57:30.814
Next up, we have chicken tigela,

00:57:30.814 --> 00:57:33.316
which is basically grilled
chicken, some corn,

00:57:33.316 --> 00:57:35.485
some roasted veggies, and tomato,

00:57:35.485 --> 00:57:37.787
and this is served with some spicy rice.

00:57:37.787 --> 00:57:40.390
They've also given a bunch of veggies.

00:57:40.390 --> 00:57:42.559
Nando's is really trying
to get our vitamins in.

00:57:42.559 --> 00:57:44.027
But take a look at the tigela itself.

00:57:44.027 --> 00:57:46.029
It's got a bed of rice underneath,

00:57:46.029 --> 00:57:47.897
but on top there's some pulled chicken,

00:57:47.897 --> 00:57:49.065
a lot of grilled onions,

00:57:49.065 --> 00:57:51.367
and a lot of finely chopped capsicum.

00:57:51.367 --> 00:57:54.504
Next up, you have the option
of a pulled-chicken wrap.

00:57:54.504 --> 00:57:56.306
I mean, it looks like a wrap.

00:57:56.306 --> 00:58:01.311
Or you can also get a pulled-chicken pita.

00:58:01.711 --> 00:58:03.947
Damn, this looks like a doner kebab.

00:58:03.947 --> 00:58:05.582
I guess the true test of whether Nando's

00:58:05.582 --> 00:58:07.116
is putting a lot of effort into their food

00:58:07.116 --> 00:58:12.121
is whether their wraps
and their pita taste good.

00:58:12.121 --> 00:58:13.990
Let's go.

00:58:13.990 --> 00:58:16.192
Miles better than any
other fast-food restaurant.

00:58:16.192 --> 00:58:19.629
Alongside those, you can
get a tub of veggies.

00:58:19.629 --> 00:58:21.931
So, next up is chicken skewers,

00:58:21.931 --> 00:58:24.067
for a kebab-eating nation.

00:58:24.067 --> 00:58:25.502
Good job, Nando's.

00:58:25.502 --> 00:58:27.337
You get these along with some pita bread

00:58:27.337 --> 00:58:29.372
and a couple of salsas.

00:58:29.372 --> 00:58:32.342
You get a yogurt sauce and some salsa.

00:58:32.342 --> 00:58:34.844
Next up, we have Portuguese
chicken and gravy,

00:58:34.844 --> 00:58:36.813
and if you can't tell from my face,

00:58:36.813 --> 00:58:39.015
I'm having a great time.

00:58:39.015 --> 00:58:42.452
Ooh, boy!

00:58:42.452 --> 00:58:43.786
Look at that.

00:58:43.786 --> 00:58:47.123
It looks like there's tarka
on top, dude! Oh, my God!

00:58:47.123 --> 00:58:48.725
What is a tarka, you ask?

00:58:48.725 --> 00:58:49.826
Basically it's the best way

00:58:49.826 --> 00:58:51.694
to finish off a curry here in India.

00:58:51.694 --> 00:58:55.398
We take oil, heat it,
add some spices in there,

00:58:55.398 --> 00:58:58.134
temper them, and then
pour them over our curry.

00:58:58.134 --> 00:59:00.203
And our final meal-deal dish

00:59:00.203 --> 00:59:03.406
is saucy chicken strips in spicy rice.

00:59:03.406 --> 00:59:04.340
I'm not gonna lie,

00:59:04.340 --> 00:59:06.976
this one looks like the most boring option

00:59:06.976 --> 00:59:08.411
out of everything here.

00:59:08.411 --> 00:59:10.179
Let's look at some of the
burgers and wraps from Nando's.

00:59:10.179 --> 00:59:12.549
In the UK, we have a couple
of exclusive options.

00:59:12.549 --> 00:59:14.350
Firstly, we have the Sunset burger.

00:59:14.350 --> 00:59:15.585
If I had to hazard a guess as to why

00:59:15.585 --> 00:59:16.819
this is called the Sunset burger,

00:59:16.819 --> 00:59:18.087
it might be because you kind of get

00:59:18.087 --> 00:59:20.790
a sunset yellow, orange, red effect going

00:59:20.790 --> 00:59:23.226
with the cheese, the
chicken, and the chutney,

00:59:23.226 --> 00:59:24.427
which looks very pretty.

00:59:26.195 --> 00:59:27.330
I haven't had this before.

00:59:27.330 --> 00:59:28.731
I wouldn't normally order it at Nando's,

00:59:28.731 --> 00:59:30.767
but it's actually very, very good.

00:59:30.767 --> 00:59:31.701
The bun is slightly different

00:59:31.701 --> 00:59:33.169
to the regular burger buns that we get.

00:59:33.169 --> 00:59:35.204
It's a little bit more spongy and pillowy,

00:59:35.204 --> 00:59:36.873
and that chutney stuff is delicious.

00:59:36.873 --> 00:59:38.641
Very sweet, little bit smoky.

00:59:38.641 --> 00:59:40.710
Then we also have the fino pita.

00:59:40.710 --> 00:59:41.978
I really love the packaging of this.

00:59:41.978 --> 00:59:42.946
It's great for delivery.

00:59:42.946 --> 00:59:45.181
You just tear straight through the middle,

00:59:45.181 --> 00:59:46.783
not like that,

00:59:46.783 --> 00:59:49.752
and then pop that off.

00:59:49.752 --> 00:59:52.221
You have a nicely preserved upright pita.

00:59:52.221 --> 00:59:54.190
Now, on a fino pita,
you get chicken thighs,

00:59:54.190 --> 00:59:57.226
you get some salad, you get
perinaise, you get halloumi,

00:59:57.226 --> 00:59:59.028
and I think there's also
some caramelized onions

00:59:59.028 --> 00:59:59.963
in there as well.

00:59:59.963 --> 01:00:01.397
I'll be honest. If I'm going to Nando's,

01:00:01.397 --> 01:00:02.231
this is what I'm getting.

01:00:02.231 --> 01:00:03.967
It's kind of got all my
favorite Nando's things

01:00:03.967 --> 01:00:05.201
in one little package.

01:00:05.201 --> 01:00:06.703
They took it off the
menu for the pandemic.

01:00:06.703 --> 01:00:07.704
They've recently brought it back,

01:00:07.704 --> 01:00:09.572
which I am thrilled about,
'cause I've missed it dearly.

01:00:12.275 --> 01:00:15.745
The cheeky Nando's level's
off the charts right now.

01:00:15.745 --> 01:00:17.647
We have a couple of exclusive burgers

01:00:17.647 --> 01:00:19.315
and wrap flavors of our own,

01:00:19.315 --> 01:00:23.853
starting with the chicken
Caesar salad wrap.

01:00:23.853 --> 01:00:25.321
I kind of like that packaging.

01:00:26.422 --> 01:00:27.657
Let's see how this tastes.

01:00:28.758 --> 01:00:30.126
That is a messed-up way to eat a wrap.

01:00:30.126 --> 01:00:32.261
Eat it from the top, not from
the side, please, Nikhil.

01:00:33.262 --> 01:00:34.230
Wow.

01:00:34.230 --> 01:00:36.132
Next up is the peri cheeseburger,

01:00:36.132 --> 01:00:39.168
which also comes as a
wrap or in pita form.

01:00:39.168 --> 01:00:42.105
Look how the juice is
dripping off this thing, man!

01:00:44.907 --> 01:00:45.975
That's what I'm talking about.

01:00:45.975 --> 01:00:49.345
This flavor has just taken India by storm

01:00:49.345 --> 01:00:50.546
in the past few decades.

01:00:50.546 --> 01:00:52.148
It's part of the trifecta of ingredients

01:00:52.148 --> 01:00:55.118
that are red velvet, matcha, and peri-peri

01:00:55.118 --> 01:00:57.754
that people just love to put
into every menu over here.

01:00:57.754 --> 01:00:58.888
Peri-peri, if you don't know,

01:00:58.888 --> 01:01:02.025
is a spice mix that was
discovered by Portuguese explorers

01:01:02.025 --> 01:01:04.494
when they were settling/pillaging

01:01:04.494 --> 01:01:07.330
south African countries, like
South Africa and Mozambique.

01:01:07.330 --> 01:01:09.065
On the subject of
foreigners coming to a place

01:01:09.065 --> 01:01:10.133
and taking things from it,

01:01:10.133 --> 01:01:12.435
I would like to formally
apologize to India from the UK.

01:01:12.435 --> 01:01:13.703
Feel free to come and take your stuff back

01:01:13.703 --> 01:01:15.571
from the British Museum
whenever it's convenient.

01:01:15.571 --> 01:01:18.775
I feel like most Indians
identify peri-peri

01:01:18.775 --> 01:01:21.744
as the little packets of
peri-peri you get at McDonald's,

01:01:21.744 --> 01:01:22.945
and you pour them into your fries

01:01:22.945 --> 01:01:25.181
and shake them to get peri-peri fries.

01:01:25.181 --> 01:01:26.616
I feel like when they come to Nando's,

01:01:26.616 --> 01:01:29.118
they might find it not spicy enough.

01:01:29.118 --> 01:01:31.054
If you don't eat meat, Nando's
is actually pretty good

01:01:31.054 --> 01:01:33.222
for vegetarian and
vegan options in the UK.

01:01:33.222 --> 01:01:35.324
First up, we have the Great Imitator wrap.

01:01:35.324 --> 01:01:37.226
It doesn't look very appealing right now.

01:01:37.226 --> 01:01:39.595
However, the Great
Imitator is Nando's version

01:01:39.595 --> 01:01:40.663
of fake chicken.

01:01:40.663 --> 01:01:42.031
I think it's made with pea protein,

01:01:42.031 --> 01:01:43.766
and by all accounts, I've
heard it's pretty good.

01:01:43.766 --> 01:01:45.301
Then we have the Beanie burger.

01:01:46.969 --> 01:01:49.472
As the name would suggest,
it's a bean patty.

01:01:49.472 --> 01:01:50.606
Also comes with, I believe,

01:01:50.606 --> 01:01:53.076
an egg-free mayo, some salad as well.

01:01:53.076 --> 01:01:55.278
Then we have a spiced chickpea burger.

01:01:55.278 --> 01:01:56.846
It's kind of similar to
the Beanie burger, however,

01:01:56.846 --> 01:01:58.314
once again, as the name would suggest,

01:01:58.314 --> 01:02:00.183
the patty is predominantly
made of chickpeas.

01:02:00.183 --> 01:02:02.952
This one actually mirrors the
Sunset burger a little more

01:02:02.952 --> 01:02:04.754
because it's got the same bun

01:02:04.754 --> 01:02:06.989
and also has some of
that red-pepper chutney.

01:02:06.989 --> 01:02:08.691
And then finally we have
a portobello mushroom

01:02:08.691 --> 01:02:09.926
and halloumi pita.

01:02:09.926 --> 01:02:12.662
It's a pita bread with a big
portobello mushroom inside

01:02:12.662 --> 01:02:14.497
as well as some salad, some halloumi,

01:02:14.497 --> 01:02:17.500
and more of that red pepper chutney.

01:02:17.500 --> 01:02:20.002
Pretty much every fast-food
restaurant here in India

01:02:20.002 --> 01:02:21.204
serves vegetarian food,

01:02:21.204 --> 01:02:24.107
because a huge percentage of
the country is vegetarian.

01:02:24.107 --> 01:02:26.109
Having said that, Nando's actually had

01:02:26.109 --> 01:02:28.177
quite a few non-vegetarian options,

01:02:28.177 --> 01:02:30.747
which is very cool to see
in a restaurant like this.

01:02:30.747 --> 01:02:33.783
So let's go off the list
of vegetarian food now,

01:02:33.783 --> 01:02:38.154
starting with creamy cashew
paneer and spicy rice.

01:02:38.154 --> 01:02:41.357
So, this is the same thing
as the creamy cashew chicken,

01:02:41.357 --> 01:02:44.127
except they've replaced it
with chunks of cottage cheese,

01:02:44.127 --> 01:02:45.828
and it just looks delicious.

01:02:45.828 --> 01:02:49.599
Let's see if Nando's
has done paneer right.

01:02:51.267 --> 01:02:53.870
It's really nice, and it's not as chewy.

01:02:53.870 --> 01:02:57.039
It's soft. Soft paneer
at a fast-food chain.

01:02:57.039 --> 01:02:58.007
Unheard of.

01:02:58.007 --> 01:03:01.711
The next vegetarian dish
is called Something Exotic.

01:03:01.711 --> 01:03:03.679
Ooh! It's a mystery.

01:03:03.679 --> 01:03:05.181
Even they don't know what it could be.

01:03:05.181 --> 01:03:06.883
And it is ...

01:03:08.785 --> 01:03:10.353
What the heck?

01:03:10.353 --> 01:03:13.022
I did not expect to see this.

01:03:13.022 --> 01:03:14.924
It's watermelon and paneer.

01:03:15.792 --> 01:03:18.294
You know, Nando's, watermelon and paneer,

01:03:18.294 --> 01:03:20.263
you really are walking the line between

01:03:20.263 --> 01:03:22.064
creativity and abomination.

01:03:23.065 --> 01:03:25.468
No. Those are kind of weird together,

01:03:25.468 --> 01:03:28.771
but I think overall this is a fun dish.

01:03:28.771 --> 01:03:32.241
And they serve it along
with a three-bean salad.

01:03:32.241 --> 01:03:36.746
The three beans are chickpea,
rajma, and some other one.

01:03:36.746 --> 01:03:37.947
Let's taste.

01:03:37.947 --> 01:03:40.583
Even this is flavorful. What's going on?

01:03:40.583 --> 01:03:42.251
OK, now we're moving on
to a vegetarian version

01:03:42.251 --> 01:03:43.386
of the cataplana.

01:03:43.386 --> 01:03:44.620
They have tossed the same vegetables,

01:03:44.620 --> 01:03:48.024
but this time along with
paneer and some chickpea.

01:03:48.024 --> 01:03:49.959
I'll only taste the chickpea.

01:03:49.959 --> 01:03:50.893
Very nice.

01:03:50.893 --> 01:03:54.163
This is easily the best food
I've had on "Food Wars."

01:03:54.163 --> 01:03:55.698
Hands

01:03:55.698 --> 01:03:57.567
OK, next up we have a vegetarian version

01:03:57.567 --> 01:03:59.001
of the espetada as well.

01:03:59.969 --> 01:04:01.370
Look at this!

01:04:01.370 --> 01:04:04.173
This is probably the best veg
skewer I've seen in my life.

01:04:04.173 --> 01:04:05.908
It's just too beautiful, I can't eat it.

01:04:05.908 --> 01:04:09.078
I must frame this in my home.

01:04:09.078 --> 01:04:11.214
Also, they serve it with garlic bread,

01:04:11.214 --> 01:04:13.082
because this isn't enough apparently.

01:04:13.082 --> 01:04:14.417
The first one is a veg burger.

01:04:14.417 --> 01:04:16.219
They serve it with coleslaw.

01:04:18.321 --> 01:04:19.956
It's a run-of-the-mill frozen patty.

01:04:19.956 --> 01:04:20.790
It's all right.

01:04:20.790 --> 01:04:22.592
This is probably the
most underwhelming thing

01:04:22.592 --> 01:04:23.693
on the menu so far.

01:04:23.693 --> 01:04:27.063
And finally, they have a
mushroom and paneer burger.

01:04:27.063 --> 01:04:30.833
Both of these options you can
get along with a wrap or pita.

01:04:30.833 --> 01:04:32.268
They have put

01:04:32.268 --> 01:04:35.471
a huge chunk of paneer in there.

01:04:35.471 --> 01:04:38.307
Have you seen a paneer this big?

01:04:38.307 --> 01:04:40.109
I didn't even know they made this s---.

01:04:42.211 --> 01:04:44.080
Superb burger.

01:04:44.080 --> 01:04:47.283
When there's good food in
this show, I'm so happy!

01:04:47.283 --> 01:04:48.584
And that's not all.

01:04:48.584 --> 01:04:50.686
There are more vegetarian options

01:04:50.686 --> 01:04:52.188
from the meal-deal section.

01:04:52.188 --> 01:04:53.022
Let's go from the top.

01:04:53.022 --> 01:04:54.824
First off, we have veg sliders.

01:04:54.824 --> 01:04:57.260
These ones have patties
instead of pulled chicken.

01:04:57.260 --> 01:05:00.196
Next up, you can get a veg
tigela. This one has paneer.

01:05:00.196 --> 01:05:01.731
So, same thing, it's a bed of rice,

01:05:01.731 --> 01:05:02.899
some chopped veggies on top,

01:05:02.899 --> 01:05:04.967
but with paneer as the protein.

01:05:04.967 --> 01:05:07.303
It's served along with potato wedges.

01:05:07.303 --> 01:05:09.839
Next up, we have paneer
skewers that you can get

01:05:09.839 --> 01:05:12.742
along with either spiced
rice or with some pita bread.

01:05:12.742 --> 01:05:15.578
Very similar to the skewers
we had with chicken,

01:05:15.578 --> 01:05:17.680
and they seem to have
the same sauce as well.

01:05:17.680 --> 01:05:20.549
They're served along with either
pita bread or spiced rice.

01:05:20.549 --> 01:05:22.351
You can choose which option of side,

01:05:22.351 --> 01:05:27.089
and you also get a salsa
as well as a yogurt dip.

01:05:27.089 --> 01:05:29.625
I always feel like it's hard
to do skewers with paneer,

01:05:29.625 --> 01:05:31.994
because it's such a delicate ingredient

01:05:31.994 --> 01:05:34.430
that if you fry it too
much it gets too rubbery.

01:05:34.430 --> 01:05:36.732
Oh, is that a piece of
pineapple there? Oh!

01:05:36.732 --> 01:05:38.734
There's a lot of thought
put into these dishes.

01:05:38.734 --> 01:05:40.403
Nando's is a class apart.

01:05:40.403 --> 01:05:42.438
It's just a class apart!

01:05:42.438 --> 01:05:46.175
And finally, we have a very
simple option at the end.

01:05:46.175 --> 01:05:49.045
It's roasted veg and some grilled paneer.

01:05:49.045 --> 01:05:50.546
I'd probably skip this one.

01:05:50.546 --> 01:05:52.715
Next up, the UK exclusive starters.

01:05:52.715 --> 01:05:54.750
First up, we've got
some sweet potato wedges

01:05:54.750 --> 01:05:55.918
and garlic perinaise.

01:05:57.553 --> 01:05:58.888
For some reason, they've also mixed in

01:05:58.888 --> 01:06:00.923
a bunch of regular chips as well.

01:06:00.923 --> 01:06:01.891
I don't know if that's normal,

01:06:01.891 --> 01:06:03.125
because I'm traditionally

01:06:03.125 --> 01:06:04.894
not going to order sweet potato fries.

01:06:04.894 --> 01:06:06.262
If you've watched "Food
Wars" for a long time,

01:06:06.262 --> 01:06:07.930
you will know my thoughts on sweet potato,

01:06:07.930 --> 01:06:10.166
namely that they are bad.

01:06:10.166 --> 01:06:13.169
It's just like someone
took a chip and went,

01:06:13.169 --> 01:06:15.938
"How can we make this floppier?

01:06:15.938 --> 01:06:17.573
I know!"

01:06:17.573 --> 01:06:19.942
The garlic perinaise, however, very tasty.

01:06:19.942 --> 01:06:21.043
Would recommend getting a side of this

01:06:21.043 --> 01:06:22.411
next time you're in Nando's.

01:06:22.411 --> 01:06:24.847
Also exclusive to the
UK are peri-peri nuts.

01:06:26.549 --> 01:06:28.884
You can start your meal off
with a combination of, I think,

01:06:28.884 --> 01:06:32.121
cashews, almonds, and
maybe macadamia nuts,

01:06:32.121 --> 01:06:34.357
all coated in their
signature peri-peri spice.

01:06:34.357 --> 01:06:35.391
I'm usually pretty good at this.

01:06:35.391 --> 01:06:36.225
Let's find out.

01:06:38.861 --> 01:06:41.063
In the UK, you can also
get fried halloumi sticks

01:06:41.063 --> 01:06:42.064
and a dip of your choice.

01:06:42.064 --> 01:06:43.966
However, unfortunately,
the restaurant forgot ours.

01:06:43.966 --> 01:06:45.935
Here's what they're supposed to look like.

01:06:45.935 --> 01:06:47.670
Neither of these are exclusive,
but in both countries,

01:06:47.670 --> 01:06:49.839
you can also start with hummus and olives.

01:06:49.839 --> 01:06:51.207
India has a variety of options,

01:06:51.207 --> 01:06:54.010
starting with the cheesy fiesta fries.

01:06:54.010 --> 01:06:55.177
Seems pretty straightforward,

01:06:55.177 --> 01:06:56.912
but let's see if it is a fiesta.

01:06:56.912 --> 01:07:00.750
Oh, my God. Bro, their
presentation is off the charts.

01:07:00.750 --> 01:07:03.052
Look at this. Look at this.

01:07:03.052 --> 01:07:05.554
Everybody marvel at the presentation.

01:07:05.554 --> 01:07:07.089
OK, I will say

01:07:07.089 --> 01:07:09.291
these have been in the cold for a while,

01:07:09.291 --> 01:07:11.594
so they may not taste as
good as when they're fresh.

01:07:13.295 --> 01:07:14.563
And I am right.

01:07:14.563 --> 01:07:17.299
Next up, they have cheesy fiesta chicken.

01:07:18.167 --> 01:07:19.001
Boom!

01:07:19.001 --> 01:07:21.437
It's pulled chicken,
grilled onions, same cheese,

01:07:21.437 --> 01:07:24.006
and I imagine there's fries underneath.

01:07:24.006 --> 01:07:25.508
Next up, they have something called

01:07:25.508 --> 01:07:28.944
the sweet potato and corn snack.

01:07:28.944 --> 01:07:31.847
Whoa! Why is their food so beautiful?

01:07:31.847 --> 01:07:35.651
There's corn, there's bits of red paprika,

01:07:35.651 --> 01:07:37.686
some chopped parsley,

01:07:37.686 --> 01:07:41.991
but also it's pieces
of thinly sliced lemon.

01:07:41.991 --> 01:07:42.825
That's new.

01:07:43.993 --> 01:07:45.428
Oh!

01:07:46.962 --> 01:07:48.431
Are you supposed to eat that?

01:07:48.431 --> 01:07:49.398
It's interesting.

01:07:49.398 --> 01:07:53.102
I don't know if I'd serve
lemon pieces in my salad.

01:07:53.102 --> 01:07:55.371
Next up, we have four-piece wings,

01:07:55.371 --> 01:07:58.741
but these ones are spicy, tangy wings.

01:07:58.741 --> 01:08:02.011
They look quite delicious.

01:08:02.011 --> 01:08:03.979
I'm going to sprinkle some lemon on there.

01:08:05.481 --> 01:08:06.816
I'm disproportionately jealous

01:08:06.816 --> 01:08:08.484
of that little lemon wedge with the wings.

01:08:08.484 --> 01:08:10.453
Why don't we have that? Very little touch.

01:08:10.453 --> 01:08:11.787
Lovely bit of freshness to your wing.

01:08:11.787 --> 01:08:12.922
Forget about it.

01:08:12.922 --> 01:08:14.323
I have to be honest. Pretty bland.

01:08:14.323 --> 01:08:17.193
Not tasting any spice,
not getting any tang.

01:08:17.193 --> 01:08:19.995
These are the most underwhelming
things on the menu so far.

01:08:19.995 --> 01:08:21.997
And now for something
I did not expect to see

01:08:21.997 --> 01:08:23.599
on the Nando's menu at all,

01:08:23.599 --> 01:08:28.471
we have a creamy cashew
paneer and chicken naan.

01:08:28.471 --> 01:08:30.106
More like Naando's.

01:08:30.106 --> 01:08:31.107
Am I right, guys?

01:08:34.009 --> 01:08:35.044
Bro,

01:08:35.044 --> 01:08:37.713
why is all their food looking like art

01:08:37.713 --> 01:08:39.482
that I can hang up on my wall?

01:08:39.482 --> 01:08:41.383
OK, so this naan has the chicken,

01:08:41.383 --> 01:08:44.787
so this is the naan-veg naan. [laughs]

01:08:44.787 --> 01:08:47.823
Let's go ahead and take a
bite, see how it tastes.

01:08:51.494 --> 01:08:52.394
It's damn good.

01:08:52.394 --> 01:08:55.131
The gravy on top is very
similar to a butter chicken.

01:08:55.131 --> 01:08:56.966
It's got a lot of sweetness and richness.

01:08:56.966 --> 01:08:58.434
You can tell there's cashew in it,

01:08:58.434 --> 01:09:01.470
but they've also sprinkled
on a lot of green chili,

01:09:01.470 --> 01:09:03.572
some coriander, and chopped onions,

01:09:03.572 --> 01:09:05.608
so there is a nice kick of spice,

01:09:05.608 --> 01:09:07.409
and they just drizzled
a lot of malai on top,

01:09:07.409 --> 01:09:08.444
so it's creamy.

01:09:08.444 --> 01:09:11.847
This is what it would be like
if India had to have a pizza.

01:09:11.847 --> 01:09:12.982
Banging.

01:09:12.982 --> 01:09:17.386
Also, they serve it with
something called perinaise dip.

01:09:17.386 --> 01:09:19.288
Are you sure this is for this?

01:09:20.122 --> 01:09:22.291
Let's just avoid.

01:09:22.291 --> 01:09:26.195
It's just, like, a huge tub of mayonnaise,

01:09:26.195 --> 01:09:28.297
but it's perinaise, apparently.

01:09:28.297 --> 01:09:29.665
For those looking for a healthier option,

01:09:29.665 --> 01:09:30.966
Nando's also offers salads.

01:09:30.966 --> 01:09:33.135
There are two main options in the UK.

01:09:33.135 --> 01:09:35.804
Firstly, we have this quinoa
and peri-tomato salad.

01:09:35.804 --> 01:09:38.073
This actually looks pretty
good, I have to say.

01:09:38.073 --> 01:09:40.109
It looks like kind of sun-dried tomatoes,

01:09:40.109 --> 01:09:41.777
some lettuce, some dressing,

01:09:41.777 --> 01:09:44.947
some of these little crunchy
crouton-cracker things,

01:09:44.947 --> 01:09:46.348
and, of course, quinoa.

01:09:46.348 --> 01:09:48.617
And our other salad option
is the delightfully named

01:09:48.617 --> 01:09:50.119
rainbow bowl.

01:09:50.119 --> 01:09:53.055
Now, the very colorful rainbow
bowl comes with some hummus,

01:09:53.055 --> 01:09:55.090
some coleslaw, some tenderstem broccoli.

01:09:55.090 --> 01:09:56.725
There's some grains down in the corner

01:09:56.725 --> 01:09:58.727
and I think some shredded carrot as well.

01:09:58.727 --> 01:10:00.095
I love tenderstem broccoli

01:10:00.095 --> 01:10:02.531
and will fight to the death
for tenderstem broccoli.

01:10:02.531 --> 01:10:03.866
By default, the salads come plain,

01:10:03.866 --> 01:10:06.969
but you can also add chicken
breast, chicken thighs,

01:10:06.969 --> 01:10:09.371
fake chicken, or Beanie
patties to any of them.

01:10:09.371 --> 01:10:11.974
Here at Nando's India, we
have salad options of our own,

01:10:11.974 --> 01:10:14.210
starting with the Mediterranean salad.

01:10:14.210 --> 01:10:17.279
Ooh la la! Opa!

01:10:17.279 --> 01:10:18.847
Is that something Mediterranean?

01:10:18.847 --> 01:10:21.317
Next up, we have an Algarve salad.

01:10:21.317 --> 01:10:23.752
Looks pretty much the
same, minus the olives,

01:10:23.752 --> 01:10:26.222
plus some cashew nuts and a lot of

01:10:26.222 --> 01:10:28.524
sun-dried chili or tomatoes.

01:10:28.524 --> 01:10:30.793
Then we have a quinoa salad,

01:10:30.793 --> 01:10:32.828
for those of you who are monsters

01:10:32.828 --> 01:10:35.164
and can't eat rice like a normal person.

01:10:35.164 --> 01:10:37.600
And finally, we have a Caesar salad,

01:10:37.600 --> 01:10:40.035
and the Caesar salad
comes with a dressing.

01:10:40.035 --> 01:10:42.204
Now, all of those salads
we ordered are vegetarian,

01:10:42.204 --> 01:10:44.306
but you can optionally
get some chicken strips

01:10:44.306 --> 01:10:45.741
if you need more protein in there.

01:10:45.741 --> 01:10:46.842
Then we're on to the sides.

01:10:46.842 --> 01:10:48.711
In the UK, you can get
quite a few exclusive sides

01:10:48.711 --> 01:10:50.312
to go along with your peri-peri chips.

01:10:50.312 --> 01:10:52.214
First up, we have rainbow slaw,

01:10:52.214 --> 01:10:54.750
which is coleslaw filled with Skittles.

01:10:54.750 --> 01:10:56.852
No, it's not. It's just coleslaw.

01:10:56.852 --> 01:10:58.087
But kind of colorful.

01:10:58.087 --> 01:11:00.189
We also have a mixed-leaf salad.

01:11:01.190 --> 01:11:02.591
Little box of leaves.

01:11:02.591 --> 01:11:04.593
Oh, there's some tomato and
cucumber in there as well.

01:11:04.593 --> 01:11:08.597
This one is spiced grains
with butternut squash,

01:11:08.597 --> 01:11:10.366
which actually sounds pretty good.

01:11:10.366 --> 01:11:13.369
Some grains in there, I
think that's feta cheese,

01:11:13.369 --> 01:11:16.105
some green beans, and butternut squash.

01:11:16.105 --> 01:11:18.974
Next up, we have creamy mash potato.

01:11:21.977 --> 01:11:23.345
It's mash potato.

01:11:23.345 --> 01:11:26.348
You can also get a side of
just some long-stem broccoli.

01:11:26.348 --> 01:11:28.550
This one looks a little
more sad than the one

01:11:28.550 --> 01:11:31.053
that was on the salad, but still great.

01:11:31.053 --> 01:11:34.089
I think there's some garlic
in there as well. Nice touch.

01:11:34.089 --> 01:11:37.192
And then finally we can get macho peas.

01:11:37.192 --> 01:11:39.795
Peas for macho men, just like me.

01:11:41.697 --> 01:11:43.165
I wasn't really sure where to put these,

01:11:43.165 --> 01:11:44.266
but there are a couple of extra things

01:11:44.266 --> 01:11:45.968
which you can add on to
pretty much any order,

01:11:45.968 --> 01:11:47.603
so I guess they kind of count as sides.

01:11:47.603 --> 01:11:49.405
First up, you can just
buy a couple of pieces

01:11:49.405 --> 01:11:51.540
of grilled halloumi from
a Nando's in the UK.

01:11:51.540 --> 01:11:53.742
For those of you who don't
know, halloumi is a cheese

01:11:53.742 --> 01:11:55.844
which I think is made with
sometimes a mixture of

01:11:55.844 --> 01:11:59.081
sheep and goat's milk,
predominantly produced in Cyprus.

01:11:59.081 --> 01:12:00.649
It's an interesting cheese.
When you bite into it,

01:12:00.649 --> 01:12:03.752
it doesn't really give. It's
got a kind of rubbery texture.

01:12:03.752 --> 01:12:05.254
I personally find it
very satisfying to eat,

01:12:05.254 --> 01:12:06.522
as do a lot of British people.

01:12:06.522 --> 01:12:09.158
I think we're responsible
for something like 80%

01:12:09.158 --> 01:12:11.727
of the Cyprus halloumi
consumption in the world,

01:12:11.727 --> 01:12:12.528
which is kind of wild.

01:12:12.528 --> 01:12:13.829
But, yeah, it's pretty good.

01:12:17.166 --> 01:12:19.468
It, like, squeaks on your
teeth when you eat it.

01:12:19.468 --> 01:12:21.804
The other sorts of side options include

01:12:21.804 --> 01:12:24.807
just one whole portobello mushroom.

01:12:24.807 --> 01:12:26.942
This might have looked OK when it was hot.

01:12:26.942 --> 01:12:30.813
You can also just get a single
plain tortilla from Nando's.

01:12:33.215 --> 01:12:35.384
I guess the idea is that you could buy

01:12:35.384 --> 01:12:37.753
maybe the halloumi, the mushroom,

01:12:37.753 --> 01:12:39.822
and a couple of other bits and sauces

01:12:39.822 --> 01:12:43.826
and create your own wrap
or own burrito situation.

01:12:43.826 --> 01:12:46.395
Personally, I don't think
it's worth doing that.

01:12:46.395 --> 01:12:47.830
Just buy a preassembled one.

01:12:47.830 --> 01:12:50.165
Options for sides here
at an India Nando's,

01:12:50.165 --> 01:12:51.633
you can get potato veggies.

01:12:51.633 --> 01:12:53.602
I already showed -- veggies?

01:12:53.602 --> 01:12:56.305
No, no, they're not veggies,
they're potato wedges.

01:12:56.305 --> 01:12:58.006
Run-of-the-mill potato wedges.

01:12:58.006 --> 01:13:00.109
You can also get some chargrilled veg.

01:13:00.109 --> 01:13:02.010
In fact, they give you a lot.

01:13:02.010 --> 01:13:04.813
You can also get a three-bean salad,

01:13:04.813 --> 01:13:06.048
which looks really colorful

01:13:06.048 --> 01:13:08.183
and has, like, a soupy
liquid that I want to try.

01:13:10.686 --> 01:13:13.288
Lentil soup, you say? Nay.

01:13:13.288 --> 01:13:16.625
I want three-bean-salad water.

01:13:17.860 --> 01:13:19.695
Next up, we have a Portuguese salad.

01:13:19.695 --> 01:13:20.629
Looks pretty straightforward.

01:13:20.629 --> 01:13:22.364
I have no idea what makes this Portuguese.

01:13:22.364 --> 01:13:23.665
Is it the olives?

01:13:23.665 --> 01:13:24.767
Probably.

01:13:24.767 --> 01:13:29.071
And finally, you can just
get a tub of feta cheese.

01:13:29.071 --> 01:13:32.474
They gave me six cubes of feta cheese.

01:13:32.474 --> 01:13:33.308
Yeah.

01:13:34.143 --> 01:13:35.210
Cool.

01:13:35.210 --> 01:13:36.945
Nando's actually has quite
a few dessert options

01:13:36.945 --> 01:13:38.714
in the UK. If you're in-store,

01:13:38.714 --> 01:13:40.215
many of the shops will have an option

01:13:40.215 --> 01:13:41.784
for bottomless frozen yogurt.

01:13:41.784 --> 01:13:43.819
So you can have that in
the flavors of vanilla,

01:13:43.819 --> 01:13:45.621
strawberry, chocolate, or mango.

01:13:45.621 --> 01:13:47.489
In-store and also on delivery, you can get

01:13:47.489 --> 01:13:50.325
a few more options,
including a Naughty Nata.

01:13:50.325 --> 01:13:54.263
This is Nando's take on a
Portuguese egg-custard tart,

01:13:54.263 --> 01:13:56.165
aka pastel de nata.

01:13:56.165 --> 01:13:58.000
I've probably butchered
the pronunciation of that.

01:13:58.000 --> 01:13:59.168
If I take myself out to Nando's

01:13:59.168 --> 01:14:00.436
and I'm feeling bougie,

01:14:00.436 --> 01:14:01.837
I'll probably end my
meal with one of these,

01:14:01.837 --> 01:14:02.838
'cause I love these things.

01:14:02.838 --> 01:14:05.073
We can also get a salted caramel brownie.

01:14:05.073 --> 01:14:06.208
Look at that. It's very pretty.

01:14:06.208 --> 01:14:08.577
It's got little gold sprinkles on it.

01:14:08.577 --> 01:14:10.412
I'm describing more foods as pretty.

01:14:10.412 --> 01:14:11.914
Been the theme of today.

01:14:11.914 --> 01:14:13.382
But they are kind of pretty.

01:14:13.382 --> 01:14:16.151
Next, we have a Choc-A-Lot cake,

01:14:16.151 --> 01:14:17.553
which is a slice of what looks like

01:14:17.553 --> 01:14:21.623
a pretty good, gooey, kind
of indulgent chocolate cake.

01:14:21.623 --> 01:14:23.025
Pretty moist.

01:14:23.025 --> 01:14:27.162
And then we also have this
gooey caramel cheesecake.

01:14:27.162 --> 01:14:28.664
This is actually really good.

01:14:28.664 --> 01:14:29.865
I'm a cheesecake fan,

01:14:29.865 --> 01:14:32.234
but this is a great
example of a cheesecake.

01:14:32.234 --> 01:14:33.268
I had it for the first time, I think,

01:14:33.268 --> 01:14:35.471
when we filmed the UK versus US Nando's.

01:14:35.471 --> 01:14:36.405
Go watch it now.

01:14:36.405 --> 01:14:37.406
Highly recommend.

01:14:37.406 --> 01:14:39.174
We don't share any desserts with the UK,

01:14:39.174 --> 01:14:41.243
but we have our own
desserts, starting with

01:14:41.243 --> 01:14:43.745
an ice cream and hot chocolate,
but they don't deliver it,

01:14:43.745 --> 01:14:45.314
so here's an image of it, I guess.

01:14:45.314 --> 01:14:46.849
Looks pretty good. Looks nice.

01:14:46.849 --> 01:14:48.750
Then we have a series of cakes,

01:14:48.750 --> 01:14:51.086
starting with a chocolate cake.

01:14:51.086 --> 01:14:52.788
It's parceled in a burger case,

01:14:52.788 --> 01:14:53.856
which is kind of weird,

01:14:53.856 --> 01:14:55.991
but, dude, look at this.

01:14:55.991 --> 01:14:59.561
Thick, moist, fat cake.

01:14:59.561 --> 01:15:01.330
I must taste for science.

01:15:02.598 --> 01:15:04.099
Appropriately humid.

01:15:04.099 --> 01:15:06.335
Next up, a red velvet cake.

01:15:06.335 --> 01:15:07.402
What did I say?

01:15:07.402 --> 01:15:08.670
The trifecta of ingredients.

01:15:08.670 --> 01:15:11.673
I'm surprised there's no matcha milkshake

01:15:11.673 --> 01:15:12.741
at the end of this.

01:15:12.741 --> 01:15:14.810
They have to fit in red
velvet in every restaurant.

01:15:14.810 --> 01:15:16.712
Peri-peri, red velvet, and matcha.

01:15:17.913 --> 01:15:22.684
And finally, we have an
out-and-out cheesecake.

01:15:22.684 --> 01:15:25.053
Honestly, all of these desserts are OK.

01:15:25.053 --> 01:15:26.555
I'd probably skip the dessert here.

01:15:26.555 --> 01:15:28.790
Last, but by no means least,
let's talk about the drinks.

01:15:28.790 --> 01:15:31.026
If you go into a restaurant
of a Nando's in the UK,

01:15:31.026 --> 01:15:33.629
you can get bottomless fizzy
drinks, including Coke,

01:15:33.629 --> 01:15:36.632
diet Coke, Coke zero, Sprite, and Fanta.

01:15:36.632 --> 01:15:39.101
Now, some people will ask
for a free glass of tap water

01:15:39.101 --> 01:15:40.802
and then use that at the
fizzy-drink fountains

01:15:40.802 --> 01:15:42.938
to help themselves to free fizzy drinks.

01:15:42.938 --> 01:15:45.607
But I personally have
definitely never done that

01:15:45.607 --> 01:15:47.376
and would not encourage
that kind of flagrantly

01:15:47.376 --> 01:15:48.777
illegal behavior whatsoever.

01:15:49.811 --> 01:15:52.614
On delivery, we do also have
a few exclusive drink options.

01:15:52.614 --> 01:15:54.683
The first options are
these Bottlegreen cordials.

01:15:54.683 --> 01:15:56.418
For those of you who aren't
familiar with cordials,

01:15:56.418 --> 01:15:57.920
it's like a flavor concentrate.

01:15:57.920 --> 01:15:59.788
So what you'll do is you'll
put a few splashes of this

01:15:59.788 --> 01:16:01.590
into a glass, top it up with water,

01:16:01.590 --> 01:16:03.759
and then you have a drink
that you can actually consume.

01:16:03.759 --> 01:16:05.093
I kind of thought these
would come premixed,

01:16:05.093 --> 01:16:06.228
so I was a little bit surprised

01:16:06.228 --> 01:16:08.530
to see just bottles of the cordial itself.

01:16:08.530 --> 01:16:10.832
But I guess you can make
yourself some squash at home.

01:16:10.832 --> 01:16:15.304
This is roy-boss. Roy,
roy, roy-bows. I don't.

01:16:15.304 --> 01:16:16.838
[whispers] I don't know
how to pronounce this.

01:16:16.838 --> 01:16:18.941
Rooibos teas, which are
flavored with things

01:16:18.941 --> 01:16:21.810
like lemon, peach, and berry.

01:16:21.810 --> 01:16:25.213
And finally, we have
Gingerella, by Karma Drinks.

01:16:25.213 --> 01:16:27.349
This is just a ginger ale.

01:16:27.349 --> 01:16:29.885
We can also get bottomless
soda refills here in India,

01:16:29.885 --> 01:16:32.621
but our bottled options
are fresh lime soda

01:16:32.621 --> 01:16:34.690
and two iced-tea options.

01:16:34.690 --> 01:16:36.792
I don't know if fresh lime
soda's a big thing abroad,

01:16:36.792 --> 01:16:38.226
but over here in India

01:16:38.226 --> 01:16:40.862
it is the No. 1 drink for
middle-class families.

01:16:40.862 --> 01:16:42.164
When you go out with your family,

01:16:42.164 --> 01:16:44.633
each person of the family
has a different order

01:16:44.633 --> 01:16:47.135
for fresh lime soda. Some
like it with just salt,

01:16:47.135 --> 01:16:48.403
some like it just sweet,

01:16:48.403 --> 01:16:49.938
some like it with sweet and salt,

01:16:49.938 --> 01:16:53.008
and some monsters like
it with no salt or sugar.

01:16:53.008 --> 01:16:55.243
This is from a company called Brewhouse,

01:16:55.243 --> 01:16:56.812
a tea-brewing company.

01:16:56.812 --> 01:16:59.915
This is supposed to be
a mojito lemon iced tea.

01:16:59.915 --> 01:17:00.749
It's nice.

01:17:00.749 --> 01:17:02.451
And next, a peach iced tea.

01:17:06.388 --> 01:17:07.189
It's nice.

01:17:07.189 --> 01:17:09.891
Nando's also offers these
drinks called designer drinks,

01:17:09.891 --> 01:17:13.128
which seem to be nonalcoholic
soft-drink cocktails.

01:17:13.128 --> 01:17:15.998
It seems like they just
took 7Up and blended them

01:17:15.998 --> 01:17:18.066
to form different flavors
with different colors.

01:17:18.066 --> 01:17:20.969
But I'm curious to see if
they actually taste good.

01:17:20.969 --> 01:17:23.805
Color, color, which color do you choose?

01:17:23.805 --> 01:17:25.907
Let's try the virgin mojito.

01:17:25.907 --> 01:17:30.245
Ah, tastes like a mojito
without the alcohol.

01:17:30.245 --> 01:17:32.347
You can see they've gone the extra mile.

01:17:32.347 --> 01:17:35.083
They've put in fresh lemon,
a lot of mint in there.

01:17:35.951 --> 01:17:37.285
Next one is citra,

01:17:37.285 --> 01:17:41.590
which I assume is a
mandarin/orange-flavored drink.

01:17:41.590 --> 01:17:43.191
Oh, nice.

01:17:43.191 --> 01:17:45.394
Very delicious. Super refreshing.

01:17:45.394 --> 01:17:46.528
I thought this could be something

01:17:46.528 --> 01:17:48.063
we could make fun of Nando's for,

01:17:48.063 --> 01:17:52.134
but they've actually made some
delicious, refreshing drinks.

01:17:52.134 --> 01:17:54.069
Ip dip do, the cat's got the flu,

01:17:54.069 --> 01:17:57.205
the dog's got the
chickenpox, and so have you.

01:17:57.205 --> 01:17:58.674
Portuguese lemonade.

01:17:58.674 --> 01:17:59.808
Let's go.

01:17:59.808 --> 01:18:01.309
What makes it Portuguese? I don't know.

01:18:01.309 --> 01:18:02.844
Maybe it's olive oil. Let's see.

01:18:02.844 --> 01:18:04.813
This is really yum.
So, it's not all sweet.

01:18:04.813 --> 01:18:07.149
It has some sort of powder at the bottom.

01:18:07.149 --> 01:18:08.583
Is it peri-peri powder?

01:18:08.583 --> 01:18:10.786
I don't know, but it
tastes like chaat powder

01:18:10.786 --> 01:18:13.388
that they put in a lot of
lemon sodas here in India,

01:18:13.388 --> 01:18:14.956
and it's really yum.

01:18:14.956 --> 01:18:16.291
Peach and elderflower.

01:18:16.291 --> 01:18:18.393
They actually put a
slice of peach in there!

01:18:18.393 --> 01:18:21.430
These are certified designer drinks.

01:18:24.232 --> 01:18:25.834
Half a chicken, peri-peri chips,

01:18:25.834 --> 01:18:27.402
and garlic bread at a UK Nando's

01:18:27.402 --> 01:18:29.671
will cost you £13.10.

01:18:29.671 --> 01:18:33.508
That same meal in India
will cost you rupees 800.69,

01:18:33.508 --> 01:18:34.843
which at the time of filming this video

01:18:34.843 --> 01:18:37.245
is equal to £9.85.

01:18:37.245 --> 01:18:41.149
That's almost 25% cheaper of
a meal than the one in the UK.

01:18:41.149 --> 01:18:43.485
OK, now while you Brits
might feel hard done by

01:18:43.485 --> 01:18:45.153
because of these price differences,

01:18:45.153 --> 01:18:48.323
I must say that this is
actually super expensive

01:18:48.323 --> 01:18:51.426
for a single meal for a
single person here in India.

01:18:51.426 --> 01:18:53.428
In fact, most people in this country

01:18:53.428 --> 01:18:55.764
would find that almost aspirational.

01:18:55.764 --> 01:18:58.567
You can get meals here
for close to 100 rupees.

01:18:58.567 --> 01:18:59.968
That's less than a pound.

01:18:59.968 --> 01:19:02.704
I would say that I can't
even consider this fast food.

01:19:02.704 --> 01:19:04.706
It is the most expensive
restaurant we've tried here

01:19:04.706 --> 01:19:07.275
on "Food Wars," but the food
was top class throughout,

01:19:07.275 --> 01:19:09.111
so I guess it makes sense.

01:19:09.111 --> 01:19:11.713
Now, Nando's does have some
slightly more affordable options

01:19:11.713 --> 01:19:13.081
in the form of meal deals,

01:19:13.081 --> 01:19:15.951
where you can get a single
meal for around 400 rupees,

01:19:15.951 --> 01:19:18.220
which is equal to £4.50.

01:19:18.220 --> 01:19:20.689
This doesn't seem like
a significant upgrade,

01:19:20.689 --> 01:19:21.490
and it isn't.

01:19:21.490 --> 01:19:23.291
In fact, the state that
we're filming this video

01:19:23.291 --> 01:19:25.193
is Karnataka here in India,

01:19:25.193 --> 01:19:27.829
and the daily wage is around 500 rupees.

01:19:27.829 --> 01:19:30.832
So you would have to
literally work an entire day

01:19:30.832 --> 01:19:33.835
to afford a single meal here at Nando's.

01:19:33.835 --> 01:19:35.737
In fact, my first salary as an intern

01:19:35.737 --> 01:19:37.906
was 10,000 rupees per month,

01:19:37.906 --> 01:19:41.143
which is £125 per month.

01:19:41.143 --> 01:19:43.411
And so if I ordered a "cheeky Nando's,"

01:19:43.411 --> 01:19:45.614
it would literally be nearly one-tenth

01:19:45.614 --> 01:19:47.282
of my entire monthly salary.

01:19:47.282 --> 01:19:48.316
I'm not sure I'd consider Nando's

01:19:48.316 --> 01:19:49.885
an affordable option in the UK,

01:19:49.885 --> 01:19:52.320
and I'm not even really sure
I'd consider it fast food.

01:19:52.320 --> 01:19:54.823
It sits somewhere in that
kind of fast-casual bracket,

01:19:54.823 --> 01:19:56.958
combining elements of
fast-food restaurants

01:19:56.958 --> 01:19:59.427
with elements of the more
traditional dining experience.

01:19:59.427 --> 01:20:00.996
Some Brits don't really like Nando's

01:20:00.996 --> 01:20:02.864
and might claim that
it's kind of overrated.

01:20:02.864 --> 01:20:05.967
I personally love Nando's.
It's fast, it's consistent,

01:20:05.967 --> 01:20:07.702
and I have a kind of
cultural attachment to it,

01:20:07.702 --> 01:20:10.005
as I was kind of a teenager
when it really blew up

01:20:10.005 --> 01:20:11.439
in popularity here in the UK.

01:20:11.439 --> 01:20:12.908
I might be able to get
more value for money

01:20:12.908 --> 01:20:14.609
at somewhere like a KFC, but to me,

01:20:14.609 --> 01:20:15.544
it wouldn't hit the same.

01:20:17.946 --> 01:20:19.347
Unfortunately, Nando's in the UK

01:20:19.347 --> 01:20:21.149
doesn't disclose a full ingredients list.

01:20:21.149 --> 01:20:22.884
Nando's in India also doesn't disclose

01:20:22.884 --> 01:20:23.985
a full ingredient list.

01:20:23.985 --> 01:20:25.453
So what do we know about the food?

01:20:25.453 --> 01:20:27.622
Well, the FAQ pages on
our respective websites

01:20:27.622 --> 01:20:30.091
do share some clues.
For example, in the UK,

01:20:30.091 --> 01:20:32.394
Nando's says it uses Red
Tractor-assured chicken

01:20:32.394 --> 01:20:34.963
from British farms. To
be Red Tractor-certified,

01:20:34.963 --> 01:20:36.832
chickens must be raised
with certain benefits,

01:20:36.832 --> 01:20:39.267
such as no cages and natural light.

01:20:39.267 --> 01:20:42.370
The Indian FAQ page says
that all of Nando's chicken

01:20:42.370 --> 01:20:45.507
in India is sourced from
India, and it's all cage-free.

01:20:45.507 --> 01:20:47.609
They also say that all
the chickens are A grade.

01:20:47.609 --> 01:20:48.710
Now, I don't know what this means,

01:20:48.710 --> 01:20:50.212
because it's hard to keep up with

01:20:50.212 --> 01:20:52.848
up-to-date poultry
practices here in India,

01:20:52.848 --> 01:20:56.084
but one report from 2012
said that a top-grade chicken

01:20:56.084 --> 01:20:58.186
must be "free of deformities that detract

01:20:58.186 --> 01:20:59.688
from its appearance or that affect

01:20:59.688 --> 01:21:01.590
the normal distribution of flesh.

01:21:01.590 --> 01:21:03.892
Slight deformities,
such as slightly curved

01:21:03.892 --> 01:21:06.761
or dented breast bones
and slightly curved backs

01:21:06.761 --> 01:21:07.963
may be present."

01:21:07.963 --> 01:21:09.865
Now, this sounds kind of vague,

01:21:09.865 --> 01:21:13.001
but I do hope that Nando's
is following this practice

01:21:13.001 --> 01:21:15.503
and only sourcing some A-grade chickens,

01:21:15.503 --> 01:21:16.872
'cause that's what it tasted like.

01:21:16.872 --> 01:21:18.373
Some A-grade chicken.

01:21:18.373 --> 01:21:20.141
One other thing we can
glean from the FAQ page

01:21:20.141 --> 01:21:22.110
is that the Great
Imitator wrap might not be

01:21:22.110 --> 01:21:24.446
as plant-based as Nando's
seems to think it is.

01:21:24.446 --> 01:21:26.014
This is because both the tortilla wrap

01:21:26.014 --> 01:21:28.650
and also the glaze used on
the chicken contain shellac.

01:21:28.650 --> 01:21:31.186
Shellac is a substance used
in food as a glazing agent,

01:21:31.186 --> 01:21:32.587
but it's found in various other things,

01:21:32.587 --> 01:21:35.123
such as nail polish,
fireworks, and sealants.

01:21:35.123 --> 01:21:37.092
The twist is that it's
technically an animal product.

01:21:37.092 --> 01:21:39.327
It's a resin secreted by lac beetles.

01:21:39.327 --> 01:21:41.463
Female lac beetles will
secrete it onto trees

01:21:41.463 --> 01:21:42.931
in the forests of India and Thailand,

01:21:42.931 --> 01:21:45.567
where it's then harvested,
processed, and sold for use.

01:21:45.567 --> 01:21:47.669
Do bugs count as animals
for the purpose of veganism?

01:21:47.669 --> 01:21:50.438
I'm a meat eater, so I can't
really talk, but in my opinion,

01:21:50.438 --> 01:21:52.407
I don't think a bug should
count. I think that's fine.

01:21:52.574 --> 01:21:53.909
Nikhil: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

01:21:53.909 --> 01:21:55.076
we wanted to find out all the differences

01:21:55.076 --> 01:21:57.646
between Cadbury chocolates
in the UK and in India.

01:21:57.646 --> 01:21:59.247
This is "Food Wars."

01:22:01.349 --> 01:22:04.786
Cadbury Dairy Milk in India
comes in ranges of four sizes.

01:22:04.786 --> 01:22:07.222
No. 1 is Cadbury Dairy Milk minis.

01:22:07.222 --> 01:22:08.456
It comes in this large packet

01:22:08.456 --> 01:22:11.526
with 18 smaller pieces of 7 grams each.

01:22:11.526 --> 01:22:14.162
Our smallest are these
bite-size 11-gram bars.

01:22:14.162 --> 01:22:16.331
Then we have these 18-gram little bars.

01:22:16.331 --> 01:22:19.734
A simple 24-grams tiny one.

01:22:19.734 --> 01:22:21.469
Next up we have our multipack bars,

01:22:21.469 --> 01:22:23.204
which weigh 33.5 grams.

01:22:23.204 --> 01:22:26.274
The standard individual Dairy
Milk bar weighs 45 grams.

01:22:26.274 --> 01:22:28.743
The duo bar, which comes in two halves

01:22:28.743 --> 01:22:30.512
and weighs 54.4 grams.

01:22:30.512 --> 01:22:33.148
Then a 55-grams maha pack.

01:22:33.148 --> 01:22:35.216
Next up we have this 110-gram bar.

01:22:35.216 --> 01:22:37.552
Family pack, 126 grams.

01:22:37.552 --> 01:22:39.654
Then we move to a 180-gram bar.

01:22:39.654 --> 01:22:42.457
We have this 360-gram bar.

01:22:44.225 --> 01:22:45.560
The biggest size you'll find in the UK

01:22:45.560 --> 01:22:48.663
is an 850-gram giant bar.

01:22:48.663 --> 01:22:50.432
So, in India, Cadbury is really well known

01:22:50.432 --> 01:22:51.566
for its gift boxes.

01:22:51.566 --> 01:22:54.803
In fact, they've done so much
marketing over so many years

01:22:54.803 --> 01:22:57.305
that it's become synonymous
with festivals like Diwali,

01:22:57.305 --> 01:22:59.607
Dussehra, and even
Christmas and New Year's.

01:22:59.607 --> 01:23:01.209
On their website right
now, you can get anything

01:23:01.209 --> 01:23:04.212
from an anniversary tin
box to a Ramadan tin box.

01:23:04.212 --> 01:23:06.147
And they come in several different sizes.

01:23:06.147 --> 01:23:09.050
For starters, there's a
standard personalized gift box,

01:23:09.050 --> 01:23:11.720
which contains six
Cadbury Dairy Milk bars,

01:23:11.720 --> 01:23:14.389
three of which are Silk and
three of which are standard.

01:23:14.389 --> 01:23:16.925
And that's the one we have right here.

01:23:16.925 --> 01:23:19.561
In fact, they've put my face on it!

01:23:19.561 --> 01:23:21.396
I mean, that's a whole lot of packaging

01:23:21.396 --> 01:23:24.833
for normal bars of chocolate
you can just buy, I guess.

01:23:24.833 --> 01:23:26.167
It even says "Food Wars"!

01:23:26.167 --> 01:23:28.903
Oh, it says US versus India. Sorry, Harry.

01:23:28.903 --> 01:23:30.105
Apart from this, you can also get

01:23:30.105 --> 01:23:33.008
a larger personalized birthday gift box,

01:23:33.008 --> 01:23:36.111
which will contain 450 grams of Silk bars,

01:23:36.111 --> 01:23:39.647
three birthday whistles, a
large banner, a birthday hat.

01:23:39.647 --> 01:23:41.416
So the next time you don't know what to do

01:23:41.416 --> 01:23:44.085
for your birthday, just
order this to your house,

01:23:44.085 --> 01:23:45.820
and you can have a party by yourself.

01:23:45.820 --> 01:23:47.322
Now, we have some
gift-box items of our own,

01:23:47.322 --> 01:23:49.524
but they usually come more in
the form of selection boxes.

01:23:49.524 --> 01:23:51.259
These are most commonly
seen around Christmastime,

01:23:51.259 --> 01:23:53.962
at which point Cadbury's will
release Heroes and Roses,

01:23:53.962 --> 01:23:56.064
which are selection boxes
containing 600 grams

01:23:56.064 --> 01:23:57.532
of individually wrapped chocolates.

01:23:57.532 --> 01:23:59.034
It's a real tradition
in British households

01:23:59.034 --> 01:24:00.268
to have a few of these lying around.

01:24:00.268 --> 01:24:03.371
The other options include
Quality Street and Celebrations.

01:24:03.371 --> 01:24:04.773
People tend to have their own favorites

01:24:04.773 --> 01:24:06.141
when it comes to the selection boxes

01:24:06.141 --> 01:24:07.709
and also the chocolates inside them.

01:24:07.709 --> 01:24:08.910
I think generally Heroes would be

01:24:08.910 --> 01:24:10.779
my preferred option over Roses.

01:24:10.779 --> 01:24:13.048
I prefer the kind of more
mainstream chocolate bars

01:24:13.048 --> 01:24:15.216
that you'll find, including
little Wispa bites,

01:24:15.216 --> 01:24:16.451
which I think might be my favorites.

01:24:16.451 --> 01:24:18.386
If you want a gift option
for all year round,

01:24:18.386 --> 01:24:20.889
opt for a Milk Tray. These
have been around for decades.

01:24:20.889 --> 01:24:22.557
I think my mum used to
be giving these to people

01:24:22.557 --> 01:24:23.491
when she was growing up.

01:24:23.491 --> 01:24:24.692
And for the run-up to Christmas,

01:24:24.692 --> 01:24:26.194
you gotta get yourself an Advent calendar.

01:24:26.194 --> 01:24:28.163
I don't think I'd normally
go for one of these.

01:24:28.163 --> 01:24:30.365
These are a little bit
flimsy, quite narrow.

01:24:30.365 --> 01:24:32.000
But still, you get a lot of joy

01:24:32.000 --> 01:24:34.469
from opening a tiny bite
of chocolate every morning

01:24:34.469 --> 01:24:35.503
in the run-up to Christmas.

01:24:37.305 --> 01:24:38.440
Here are all the Cadbury products

01:24:38.440 --> 01:24:41.042
that you'll find in India that
you will not find in the UK.

01:24:41.042 --> 01:24:43.044
Here are all the Cadbury
products from the UK

01:24:43.044 --> 01:24:44.679
that you won't find in India.

01:24:44.679 --> 01:24:46.281
This is so much chocolate.

01:24:46.281 --> 01:24:48.249
In terms of our classic
Dairy Milk flavors,

01:24:48.249 --> 01:24:50.018
we have two exclusives.

01:24:50.018 --> 01:24:52.954
No. 1, roast almond, and No. 2, crackle.

01:24:52.954 --> 01:24:55.790
This used to be my favorite as a child,

01:24:55.790 --> 01:24:57.492
but right now I really like this.

01:24:57.492 --> 01:24:59.727
Delicious chunks of roast almond.

01:24:59.727 --> 01:25:01.896
We have some exclusive Dairy
Milk flavors of our own.

01:25:01.896 --> 01:25:03.798
Firstly, for the
health-conscious among us,

01:25:03.798 --> 01:25:06.334
we have this 30% less sugar Dairy Milk.

01:25:06.334 --> 01:25:07.502
I guess this could be helpful as well

01:25:07.502 --> 01:25:09.204
if you find regular milk
chocolate too sweet,

01:25:09.204 --> 01:25:10.038
which some people do,

01:25:10.038 --> 01:25:12.373
but then I guess just opt for
some dark chocolate instead.

01:25:12.373 --> 01:25:14.809
Next up we have Cadbury caramel.

01:25:14.809 --> 01:25:15.743
It's a bar of Dairy Milk,

01:25:15.743 --> 01:25:18.113
but inside each square there's
a little bit of caramel.

01:25:18.113 --> 01:25:19.114
This is one of my favorite ones.

01:25:19.114 --> 01:25:21.149
It does get a little bit sickly
if you eat too much of it

01:25:21.149 --> 01:25:23.084
because of the amount of
sugar, but very tasty.

01:25:23.084 --> 01:25:24.719
We have some Big Taste bars,

01:25:24.719 --> 01:25:26.621
which are chunky versions of Dairy Milk,

01:25:26.621 --> 01:25:28.690
starting with peanut caramel crisp.

01:25:28.690 --> 01:25:32.293
And we also have a triple
choc sensation Big Taste bar,

01:25:32.293 --> 01:25:34.596
which combines dark,
milk, and white chocolate

01:25:34.596 --> 01:25:36.131
in one delicious bar.

01:25:36.131 --> 01:25:37.298
These ones look really cool.

01:25:37.298 --> 01:25:38.733
They've definitely put a bit more thought

01:25:38.733 --> 01:25:40.201
into the design of the bars.

01:25:40.201 --> 01:25:41.536
Tastes really good as well.

01:25:42.470 --> 01:25:44.772
Next up, we've got Dairy
Milk with Crunchie bits.

01:25:44.772 --> 01:25:47.475
Now, this is Crunchie with an
-ie, not crunchy with a -y.

01:25:47.475 --> 01:25:49.744
Crunchie with an -ie is
actually a bar of chocolate

01:25:49.744 --> 01:25:50.745
you can get here in the UK.

01:25:50.745 --> 01:25:52.780
It's milk chocolate
with a honeycomb center.

01:25:52.780 --> 01:25:55.450
Then we have a Dairy Milk Daim bar.

01:25:55.450 --> 01:25:56.551
Daim is another chocolate bar

01:25:56.551 --> 01:25:58.219
which Dairy Milk has
kind of collabed with.

01:25:58.219 --> 01:26:01.055
I think it's a very thin,
brittle almond-caramel bar

01:26:01.055 --> 01:26:02.524
with a little bit of
chocolate on the outside.

01:26:02.524 --> 01:26:03.992
My granddad really used to like Daim.

01:26:03.992 --> 01:26:05.927
Then we have this Marvellous Creations

01:26:05.927 --> 01:26:07.262
jelly popping candy bar.

01:26:07.262 --> 01:26:08.830
As the name suggests,
it's a bar of chocolate

01:26:08.830 --> 01:26:10.165
which contains some popping candy

01:26:10.165 --> 01:26:11.432
as well as I think jelly beans.

01:26:11.432 --> 01:26:12.567
I've not tried this in a long time.

01:26:12.567 --> 01:26:13.668
I want to see what the ratios are like

01:26:13.668 --> 01:26:15.803
and also if I can really
feel the popping candy.

01:26:15.803 --> 01:26:17.705
You can see a couple of bits of,

01:26:17.705 --> 01:26:20.108
I assume, jelly beans
peeking out of the top.

01:26:20.108 --> 01:26:21.543
The pattern is kind of odd.

01:26:21.543 --> 01:26:22.710
Usually obviously you have squares.

01:26:22.710 --> 01:26:24.612
Makes it nice and easy
to break apart and share.

01:26:24.612 --> 01:26:25.947
I'm just gonna bite into it like a madman.

01:26:30.251 --> 01:26:32.754
You really do get the popping
candy. My mouth is popping.

01:26:32.754 --> 01:26:34.556
[popping]

01:26:34.556 --> 01:26:35.890
It's actually not too bad.

01:26:35.890 --> 01:26:38.493
You get little chewy sweet
bits in with your chocolate.

01:26:38.493 --> 01:26:40.428
There's a lot going on,
but I don't hate it.

01:26:40.428 --> 01:26:43.631
For vegans in the UK, Cadbury's
also has a plant-based bar.

01:26:43.631 --> 01:26:44.699
I've never tried this, so I want to see

01:26:44.699 --> 01:26:47.368
if I can taste the difference
between this and Dairy Milk.

01:26:47.368 --> 01:26:48.937
I mean, it looks like chocolate.

01:26:51.172 --> 01:26:53.408
Definitely does taste
of almond, which is OK,

01:26:53.408 --> 01:26:54.676
'cause I quite like kind
of nut and chocolate

01:26:54.676 --> 01:26:56.811
as a combination. If I went vegan,

01:26:56.811 --> 01:26:59.347
I don't know if I'd be rushing
to the store to buy this.

01:26:59.347 --> 01:27:00.982
It's OK. The texture's pretty good,

01:27:00.982 --> 01:27:02.383
but the flavor just really isn't there.

01:27:02.383 --> 01:27:03.885
Our last two exclusive Dairy Milk bars

01:27:03.885 --> 01:27:05.053
are actually a mystery.

01:27:05.053 --> 01:27:07.822
Two bars which contain
fillings of a mystery flavor.

01:27:07.822 --> 01:27:09.123
You try and guess what the flavor is,

01:27:09.123 --> 01:27:11.159
and then you can submit
your answer online.

01:27:11.159 --> 01:27:12.994
Myself and the rest of the
crew have now got to try these

01:27:12.994 --> 01:27:14.996
and give our best
guesses. Mystery bar one.

01:27:14.996 --> 01:27:16.464
Oh, God. The last time
I threw stuff at you

01:27:16.464 --> 01:27:17.899
it didn't go very well.

01:27:17.899 --> 01:27:19.300
Leon: I've got it.
Harry: Ooh.

01:27:19.300 --> 01:27:22.637
OK, it's fruity. Currently
we're thinking maybe rose.

01:27:22.637 --> 01:27:25.206
I'm personally thinking apricot.
Struggling to agree here.

01:27:25.206 --> 01:27:27.175
We can taste more. Swear I get fruit.

01:27:27.175 --> 01:27:28.243
While we figure that one out,

01:27:28.243 --> 01:27:29.644
we'll try mystery bar No. 2.

01:27:29.644 --> 01:27:32.213
Now, this one smells aggressively fruity.

01:27:32.213 --> 01:27:33.314
Catch, Leon.

01:27:35.083 --> 01:27:36.484
I'm getting quite a lot of, like,

01:27:36.484 --> 01:27:38.186
very artificial raspberry flavor.

01:27:38.186 --> 01:27:41.089
I'd be fairly confident in
asserting that as raspberry.

01:27:41.089 --> 01:27:42.223
It might be blueberry.

01:27:42.223 --> 01:27:44.125
Plot twist, they've already
revealed the flavors.

01:27:44.125 --> 01:27:44.959
We didn't know.

01:27:44.959 --> 01:27:47.862
First one was rhubarb and
custard. Classic British dessert.

01:27:47.862 --> 01:27:49.264
Didn't really get very close to that one.

01:27:49.264 --> 01:27:50.265
Second was blue raspberry,

01:27:50.265 --> 01:27:51.566
which we actually did kind of get.

01:27:51.566 --> 01:27:53.067
I personally don't think I would buy

01:27:53.067 --> 01:27:54.202
either of those again, though.

01:27:54.202 --> 01:27:56.070
Charlie: Maybe the first one.
Harry: You don't mind it?

01:27:56.070 --> 01:27:57.939
And now for our Silk range,

01:27:57.939 --> 01:28:01.476
or, as Cadbury is trying
to rebrand it, the S range.

01:28:01.476 --> 01:28:03.111
What is this? Some sort of new iPhone?

01:28:03.111 --> 01:28:06.180
But whether you call it Silk
or S, I love these chocolates.

01:28:06.180 --> 01:28:08.416
First off, we have the typical Silk.

01:28:08.416 --> 01:28:11.319
Basically it's just Dairy
Milk but a lot silkier.

01:28:11.319 --> 01:28:13.454
Then we have Dairy Milk Silk bubbly.

01:28:13.454 --> 01:28:16.557
It's Dairy Milk Silk, but bubbly.

01:28:16.557 --> 01:28:17.892
That's nice, light, airy.

01:28:17.892 --> 01:28:20.695
Next, you have a Dairy
Milk Silk fruit and nut.

01:28:20.695 --> 01:28:23.498
Then we have Dairy Milk Silk hazelnut.

01:28:23.498 --> 01:28:27.135
Wow, there are some proper
large chunks of hazelnut.

01:28:27.135 --> 01:28:28.569
The hazelnut itself,

01:28:28.569 --> 01:28:30.438
the flavor of it really
lends to the chocolate,

01:28:30.438 --> 01:28:32.707
and it doesn't taste as sweet.

01:28:32.707 --> 01:28:35.543
Next up we have Dairy
Milk Silk roast almond.

01:28:35.543 --> 01:28:38.479
We have Dairy Milk Silk mousse.

01:28:38.479 --> 01:28:40.214
They've tried to recreate
the flavor of mousse,

01:28:40.214 --> 01:28:41.916
and you can see that
it's a lot more fudgy,

01:28:41.916 --> 01:28:43.017
the chocolate inside.

01:28:43.017 --> 01:28:44.419
It's all right.

01:28:44.419 --> 01:28:46.120
Oh, man, there's one
that I'm scared to try.

01:28:46.120 --> 01:28:49.324
Dairy Milk Silk bubbly bubble gum.

01:28:49.324 --> 01:28:50.958
Oh, no, I saw the color of it.

01:28:50.958 --> 01:28:53.561
Oh, my God, why have they done this?

01:28:53.561 --> 01:28:55.863
Growing up, we had a
bubble gum called Boomer,

01:28:55.863 --> 01:28:57.765
which is now what we have all become.

01:28:57.765 --> 01:29:00.501
That one bite was really not that bad.

01:29:00.501 --> 01:29:02.770
It definitely tastes like bubble gum

01:29:02.770 --> 01:29:04.572
and gave me that Boomer vibe.

01:29:04.572 --> 01:29:06.207
That's as much as I can have of that.

01:29:06.207 --> 01:29:08.409
Now, to cleanse the palate, Silk Oreo.

01:29:08.409 --> 01:29:09.610
Mm!

01:29:10.712 --> 01:29:12.814
That has a nice flavor to it.

01:29:12.814 --> 01:29:14.449
I think this is my
favorite out of the lot.

01:29:14.449 --> 01:29:16.951
We also have another variation of Oreo.

01:29:16.951 --> 01:29:18.553
It's red velvet Oreo.

01:29:18.553 --> 01:29:20.488
If you've watched previous
episodes of "Food Wars,"

01:29:20.488 --> 01:29:22.890
you'll remember that
one of the ingredients

01:29:22.890 --> 01:29:25.660
that has taken India by
storm in the past few decades

01:29:25.660 --> 01:29:26.928
is red velvet.

01:29:26.928 --> 01:29:28.262
And I have tasted this before,

01:29:28.262 --> 01:29:29.897
and I actually think it's really good.

01:29:29.897 --> 01:29:32.633
But it is overkill.

01:29:32.633 --> 01:29:36.704
It's literally Dairy Milk
Silk, the Oreo white cream,

01:29:36.704 --> 01:29:40.041
and chunks of Oreo that have
been turned into red velvet.

01:29:41.209 --> 01:29:42.076
Do you have a treadmill?

01:29:42.076 --> 01:29:45.780
Finally, we have Dairy
Milk Silk heart blush.

01:29:45.780 --> 01:29:47.548
I imagine you give this to your loved one.

01:29:47.548 --> 01:29:48.783
It says "pull" over here,

01:29:48.783 --> 01:29:50.284
and I'm pretty excited to pull this.

01:29:51.919 --> 01:29:54.722
"Never gonna give you up.
Never gonna let you down."

01:29:54.722 --> 01:29:57.692
I can't believe I've been
Rickrolled in my own video!

01:29:57.692 --> 01:30:00.895
At the back, there is a very
elaborate-looking tear tab,

01:30:00.895 --> 01:30:02.397
so I'm just gonna ... ah!

01:30:05.266 --> 01:30:07.068
Not very easy to -- wait, what?

01:30:08.569 --> 01:30:10.772
I'd probably break up
with whoever gave me this

01:30:10.772 --> 01:30:13.241
at this point. This is frustrating.

01:30:13.241 --> 01:30:14.942
It's more packaging.

01:30:14.942 --> 01:30:15.777
All right.

01:30:18.179 --> 01:30:19.313
More packaging.

01:30:19.313 --> 01:30:21.249
This is honestly a very wasteful way

01:30:21.249 --> 01:30:22.984
to tell somebody you like them.

01:30:22.984 --> 01:30:24.919
There you go. It's some pink chocolate.

01:30:24.919 --> 01:30:26.320
Oh, my God, I swear to God,

01:30:26.320 --> 01:30:28.489
if it's the same as the
bubble gum, I'm gonna cry.

01:30:29.724 --> 01:30:31.526
It's not bubble gum, so.

01:30:31.526 --> 01:30:34.162
This is actually quite a fun
experience, I'm not gonna lie.

01:30:36.364 --> 01:30:37.265
Now, we don't have Silk bars,

01:30:37.265 --> 01:30:38.766
but we do have something called Darkmilk.

01:30:38.766 --> 01:30:40.635
Cadbury's has kind of invented this hybrid

01:30:40.635 --> 01:30:42.904
milk and dark chocolate
for someone whose tastes

01:30:42.904 --> 01:30:44.338
lie somewhere between those two.

01:30:44.338 --> 01:30:45.773
Here is the Darkmilk.

01:30:45.773 --> 01:30:47.341
Darkmilk also comes in variations

01:30:47.341 --> 01:30:50.611
including a salted-caramel
flavor and a hazelnut flavor.

01:30:50.611 --> 01:30:52.180
I feel like they've tried to
market these a little bit more

01:30:52.180 --> 01:30:53.848
at adults, maybe, as opposed to kids.

01:30:53.848 --> 01:30:54.982
The packaging kind of gives

01:30:54.982 --> 01:30:58.286
a slightly more sophisticated
vibe. Sexy, if you will.

01:30:58.286 --> 01:30:59.487
At the other end of
the scale, we have some

01:30:59.487 --> 01:31:01.489
even sweeter options than
classic milk chocolate.

01:31:01.489 --> 01:31:03.024
Firstly, we have Caramilk,

01:31:03.024 --> 01:31:04.792
which is golden caramel chocolate.

01:31:04.792 --> 01:31:06.627
This one I have not tried.
I'm kind of intrigued.

01:31:06.627 --> 01:31:07.595
I'm going to have a bite.

01:31:07.595 --> 01:31:09.730
I worry it's going to be far too sweet.

01:31:12.567 --> 01:31:14.268
Wow, that's very sweet.

01:31:14.268 --> 01:31:15.636
You do get notes of caramel,

01:31:15.636 --> 01:31:17.071
but I really don't think I could eat

01:31:17.071 --> 01:31:18.372
more than a couple of bites of that.

01:31:18.372 --> 01:31:20.608
And, of course, we also
just have white chocolate.

01:31:20.608 --> 01:31:22.410
As I've said, I'm not really
a big fan of white chocolate,

01:31:22.410 --> 01:31:23.611
and I don't think I'm alone in that,

01:31:23.611 --> 01:31:25.012
because this basically wasn't available

01:31:25.012 --> 01:31:27.114
in any of the big
supermarkets that I looked in.

01:31:27.114 --> 01:31:29.283
The shop we were able to track
it down in was Poundland,

01:31:29.283 --> 01:31:31.352
which is a shop in the UK
where everything costs a pound.

01:31:31.352 --> 01:31:33.521
I know it sounds ridiculous
to an American audience,

01:31:33.521 --> 01:31:34.689
but that is what it's called.

01:31:34.689 --> 01:31:36.991
So, you can find Cadbury
Bournville dark chocolate

01:31:36.991 --> 01:31:38.526
in both the UK and in India,

01:31:38.526 --> 01:31:39.594
but there's a slight difference.

01:31:39.594 --> 01:31:42.530
In the UK, the packaging
is bright red, ew,

01:31:42.530 --> 01:31:44.532
and over here we have different flavors,

01:31:44.532 --> 01:31:47.702
50% dark chocolate and 70% dark chocolate.

01:31:47.702 --> 01:31:50.638
I have over the years grown
to like dark chocolate.

01:31:50.638 --> 01:31:52.540
I was never a fan of it growing up.

01:31:52.540 --> 01:31:55.176
But 70% dark chocolate? I don't know.

01:31:55.176 --> 01:31:56.577
Oh!

01:31:56.577 --> 01:32:00.081
You know, it's not as bitter
as I expected. Very creamy.

01:32:00.081 --> 01:32:03.751
Also, the cocoa is 100%
sustainably sourced.

01:32:03.751 --> 01:32:06.187
Next up, we have a fruit and nut.

01:32:06.187 --> 01:32:08.422
It's got a peanut in there.

01:32:08.422 --> 01:32:11.092
It doesn't taste as heavy
as the other chocolates

01:32:11.092 --> 01:32:13.294
I've had so far, and I
really appreciate this.

01:32:13.294 --> 01:32:15.062
Am I growing old? Is
that what's happening?

01:32:15.062 --> 01:32:17.131
And the final flavor is cranberry,

01:32:17.131 --> 01:32:19.166
which I've been the most excited about.

01:32:19.166 --> 01:32:21.435
I don't think I've had any chocolate bars

01:32:21.435 --> 01:32:23.437
that have had cranberry in them,

01:32:23.437 --> 01:32:25.706
but obviously cranberry and dark chocolate

01:32:25.706 --> 01:32:27.575
sounds like an amazing combination.

01:32:27.575 --> 01:32:30.378
That is so good! The
tartness of the cranberry

01:32:30.378 --> 01:32:31.979
and, like, the slight sugariness

01:32:31.979 --> 01:32:33.648
really complements the dark chocolate.

01:32:33.648 --> 01:32:36.050
There's the crunch of roasted
almond. This is a winner.

01:32:36.050 --> 01:32:37.885
Real nice. I like this
range of Bournvilles.

01:32:37.885 --> 01:32:40.288
Feels like a healthier guilty pleasure.

01:32:40.288 --> 01:32:41.556
We also have some Bournville products

01:32:41.556 --> 01:32:43.658
you'll find in the UK that
you won't find in India.

01:32:43.658 --> 01:32:45.693
Firstly, we have Bournville old Jamaica.

01:32:45.693 --> 01:32:48.596
The "old Jamaica" refers
to rum and raisin flavors

01:32:48.596 --> 01:32:49.697
added to the dark chocolate.

01:32:49.697 --> 01:32:51.365
And we also have an orange Bournville.

01:32:51.365 --> 01:32:53.134
I personally don't love dark chocolate,

01:32:53.134 --> 01:32:55.069
and I especially do
not love dark chocolate

01:32:55.069 --> 01:32:55.937
combined with fruit,

01:32:55.937 --> 01:32:57.939
so I'm respectfully not
going to try any of these.

01:32:57.939 --> 01:32:59.740
If you're wondering where the
name Bournville comes from,

01:32:59.740 --> 01:33:01.542
it's actually a village that was created

01:33:01.542 --> 01:33:03.344
by the Cadbury family for workers

01:33:03.344 --> 01:33:05.212
who worked in their
factory near Birmingham.

01:33:05.212 --> 01:33:07.148
Bournville still exists today,
so you can go and visit it.

01:33:07.148 --> 01:33:08.983
It's home to Cadbury
World, which is a kind of

01:33:08.983 --> 01:33:11.218
Cadbury museum
interactive-experience thing,

01:33:11.218 --> 01:33:12.853
and apparently it's a
really nice place to live.

01:33:12.853 --> 01:33:14.889
And now it's time for all of the remaining

01:33:14.889 --> 01:33:16.557
Indian Cadbury products,

01:33:16.557 --> 01:33:20.461
starting with Cadbury Fuse.

01:33:20.461 --> 01:33:24.899
Their tagline for this is, "A
delicious chocolaty feast."

01:33:24.899 --> 01:33:27.802
Like, some sort of chocolaty
mousse in the middle

01:33:27.802 --> 01:33:29.437
surrounded by caramel,

01:33:29.437 --> 01:33:32.473
and then the outer layer of
chocolate has peanuts in it.

01:33:32.473 --> 01:33:36.143
So I can imagine this
being a proper feast.

01:33:36.143 --> 01:33:37.078
Kind of nice.

01:33:37.078 --> 01:33:39.547
I think I could eat this
much of one chocolate,

01:33:39.547 --> 01:33:42.783
but the fact that I'm eating
so many varieties of chocolate

01:33:42.783 --> 01:33:47.054
one after the other is really
doing something to my brain!

01:33:47.054 --> 01:33:48.189
Like, why are we doing this?

01:33:48.189 --> 01:33:50.324
No, like, what is this? Why
are we tasting all of this?

01:33:50.324 --> 01:33:51.626
What is the point of this show?

01:33:51.626 --> 01:33:56.130
Next in line, we have
the Cadbury Crispello.

01:33:56.130 --> 01:33:58.666
I want to be on the team that gets to name

01:33:58.666 --> 01:33:59.734
all of these chocolates.

01:33:59.734 --> 01:34:01.769
Seems like you can just
get away with anything.

01:34:01.769 --> 01:34:03.671
It's clearly filled
with some rice crispies

01:34:03.671 --> 01:34:05.573
and things that are crispies.

01:34:05.573 --> 01:34:07.808
Hey, this one is actually really yum.

01:34:07.808 --> 01:34:09.977
Next up,

01:34:09.977 --> 01:34:12.913
Cadbury 5 Star 3D.

01:34:12.913 --> 01:34:14.815
If you don't know what 5
Star is, it's basically

01:34:14.815 --> 01:34:16.984
the chocolate that made
caramel cool in India.

01:34:16.984 --> 01:34:19.520
It's been around for decades,
and actually, fun fact,

01:34:19.520 --> 01:34:20.755
it's my mom's favorite chocolate.

01:34:20.755 --> 01:34:23.057
Now they've upgraded to 5 Star 3D.

01:34:23.057 --> 01:34:25.526
What's the difference between
this and any other 5 Star?

01:34:25.526 --> 01:34:26.727
It has nuts.

01:34:26.727 --> 01:34:30.531
I will say, having eaten the
past three chocolates in a row,

01:34:30.531 --> 01:34:34.068
I'm starting to realize
they're kind of the same thing.

01:34:34.068 --> 01:34:37.038
It's decent. I prefer the original 5 Star.

01:34:37.038 --> 01:34:40.574
That one sparks nostalgia.
This one just feels too modern.

01:34:40.574 --> 01:34:43.244
Next up, we have a Perk.

01:34:43.244 --> 01:34:45.446
So, Perk is another chocolate
that's been around in India

01:34:45.446 --> 01:34:48.182
for ages now, and it's gone
through a lot of evolutions,

01:34:48.182 --> 01:34:49.784
like every other chocolate has.

01:34:49.784 --> 01:34:51.819
Now they sell Perk in a double pack.

01:34:51.819 --> 01:34:53.854
It says you can "rip it, share it."

01:34:55.222 --> 01:34:56.924
Oh!

01:34:56.924 --> 01:34:59.727
Next up, some gemstones.

01:34:59.727 --> 01:35:02.463
That's right, the UK didn't
give us our gemstones back,

01:35:02.463 --> 01:35:04.265
but they definitely gave us Gems.

01:35:05.700 --> 01:35:07.334
Yeah, I mean, fair enough. Sorry, guys.

01:35:07.334 --> 01:35:10.404
So, they're M&amp;M's without
the M&amp;M branding on top.

01:35:10.404 --> 01:35:11.505
What I used to do as a kid,

01:35:11.505 --> 01:35:13.140
you would get a small packet of Gems,

01:35:13.140 --> 01:35:16.444
and I would suck on each gem
until the color would come off

01:35:16.444 --> 01:35:17.611
and it would be a white gem.

01:35:17.611 --> 01:35:19.947
And then I'd put all the
white ones in my mouth

01:35:19.947 --> 01:35:22.483
and bite them like one big chocolate.

01:35:22.483 --> 01:35:24.752
I was weird, and I had no friends.

01:35:24.752 --> 01:35:27.955
Cadbury Temptations rum and raisin. Rum?

01:35:27.955 --> 01:35:31.459
And, uh, Cad, Cadbury, Cadbrury -- whoo!

01:35:31.459 --> 01:35:35.296
Cadbury Temptations almond treat.

01:35:35.296 --> 01:35:37.732
It smells like rum.

01:35:39.133 --> 01:35:42.970
Whoa, I did not expect that
flavor to be so strong.

01:35:42.970 --> 01:35:44.672
Can they sell this to children?

01:35:44.672 --> 01:35:46.474
It kind of tastes like
a Christmas rum cake.

01:35:46.474 --> 01:35:48.409
Yeah, I don't mind it. I
think this could be a great

01:35:48.409 --> 01:35:51.545
Christmas sort of
chocolate to have around.

01:35:51.545 --> 01:35:54.081
Next up is my favorite

01:35:54.081 --> 01:35:56.784
childhood chocolate, Nutties.

01:35:56.784 --> 01:35:58.152
I freaking love Nutties,

01:35:58.152 --> 01:35:59.920
and my favorite part about Nutties

01:35:59.920 --> 01:36:02.656
is that the branding
has not really changed

01:36:02.656 --> 01:36:03.991
for, like, decades now.

01:36:03.991 --> 01:36:07.394
What this chocolate is, is
basically Cadbury chocolate

01:36:07.394 --> 01:36:10.765
coated over a cashew nut
that's covered in nougat.

01:36:12.466 --> 01:36:15.002
Oh, my God, that is so good.

01:36:15.002 --> 01:36:17.371
Then we have a load more
Cadbury exclusives in the UK,

01:36:17.371 --> 01:36:18.506
and we'll start with the bars.

01:36:18.506 --> 01:36:20.274
We'll start with what is
technically a Cadbury product

01:36:20.274 --> 01:36:21.542
but initially was not.

01:36:21.542 --> 01:36:23.611
This is the Fry's chocolate cream bar.

01:36:23.611 --> 01:36:24.578
It's a dark-chocolate bar

01:36:24.578 --> 01:36:26.747
with a creamy, smooth fondant center.

01:36:26.747 --> 01:36:28.916
A fun factor is that the
Frys were a Quaker family

01:36:28.916 --> 01:36:30.785
who were the first ones to
actually commercially produce

01:36:30.785 --> 01:36:33.387
chocolate bars in the UK.
Before the Frys came along,

01:36:33.387 --> 01:36:35.856
drinking chocolate was kind
of the only way to consume it.

01:36:35.856 --> 01:36:37.825
Fry's also makes a peppermint cream bar

01:36:37.825 --> 01:36:39.693
as well as Turkish delight.

01:36:39.693 --> 01:36:41.529
I will say, this is not the
best Turkish delight out there.

01:36:41.529 --> 01:36:42.530
If you want Turkish delight,

01:36:42.530 --> 01:36:44.698
go to a grocery store
that sells Turkish food,

01:36:44.698 --> 01:36:45.699
get some classic stuff,

01:36:45.699 --> 01:36:48.803
whereas this is a kind of
slightly cheapy Turkish delight

01:36:48.803 --> 01:36:49.970
encased in chocolate.

01:36:49.970 --> 01:36:51.272
Next up, we have Boost bars.

01:36:51.272 --> 01:36:52.139
These are chocolate bars

01:36:52.139 --> 01:36:54.241
filled with caramel and biscuit pieces.

01:36:54.241 --> 01:36:55.409
When Boost was first launched,

01:36:55.409 --> 01:36:57.812
I think they were kind of
marketed as almost an energy bar.

01:36:57.812 --> 01:37:00.047
They had loads of sugar
and glucose in them,

01:37:00.047 --> 01:37:02.516
although I think they have now
recently dropped that down,

01:37:02.516 --> 01:37:04.585
and it's just in line more
with a standard chocolate bar.

01:37:04.585 --> 01:37:06.854
Then we're on to Chomps.
I personally love a Chomp.

01:37:06.854 --> 01:37:08.489
These were also a little bit hard to find.

01:37:08.489 --> 01:37:10.424
I think we had to go to
Poundland for these ones as well,

01:37:10.424 --> 01:37:11.859
but they used to cost, like, 10p

01:37:11.859 --> 01:37:13.127
from your local news agents.

01:37:13.127 --> 01:37:16.163
It's just a chocolate bar
with toffee/caramel inside.

01:37:16.163 --> 01:37:17.364
Simple but effective.

01:37:17.364 --> 01:37:19.400
Then we have Crunchie bars,
which are chocolate bars

01:37:19.400 --> 01:37:21.335
with a large honeycomb center.

01:37:21.335 --> 01:37:23.070
Personally, don't love Crunchie bars.

01:37:23.070 --> 01:37:24.505
I don't love the texture of the honeycomb,

01:37:24.505 --> 01:37:25.539
and they're very, very sweet.

01:37:25.539 --> 01:37:27.541
What I do love, however, is a Curly Wurly.

01:37:27.541 --> 01:37:28.776
These are brilliantly named.

01:37:28.776 --> 01:37:31.312
They come in these little
individual bars, like this.

01:37:31.312 --> 01:37:32.313
They look a bit weird.

01:37:32.313 --> 01:37:35.349
It's kind of a web of
chocolate and caramel.

01:37:37.051 --> 01:37:38.552
I used to have braces as a kid,

01:37:38.552 --> 01:37:40.921
and I really missed toffee and
caramel while I had them on.

01:37:40.921 --> 01:37:42.723
Moving on, we have a Double Decker bar.

01:37:42.723 --> 01:37:44.558
A nod to the British double-decker buses,

01:37:44.558 --> 01:37:47.928
this is a two-layered chocolate
bar with a nougat layer

01:37:47.928 --> 01:37:50.898
as well as a kind of
crunchy-pieces-in-caramel layer.

01:37:50.898 --> 01:37:51.732
I like these.

01:37:51.732 --> 01:37:52.933
Next up, we have Fudge bars.

01:37:52.933 --> 01:37:55.269
Got these little bite-sized
ones today. I like these.

01:37:55.269 --> 01:37:56.604
The guys seem to disagree with me,

01:37:56.604 --> 01:37:57.504
but I think these are good.

01:37:57.504 --> 01:37:59.406
I will opt for these in a Heroes box.

01:37:59.406 --> 01:38:01.609
It's just a bar of fudge
covered with chocolate.

01:38:01.609 --> 01:38:03.143
Then we move on to the Picnic bar.

01:38:03.143 --> 01:38:05.145
It's a chocolate bar that
contains, I think, caramel,

01:38:05.145 --> 01:38:07.047
some rice-crispy kind of pieces,

01:38:07.047 --> 01:38:08.883
as well as some raisins and peanuts.

01:38:08.883 --> 01:38:10.651
Now, while India has a 5 Star bar,

01:38:10.651 --> 01:38:13.020
in the UK, we just have a Starbar.

01:38:13.020 --> 01:38:14.488
I don't think I've ever
had one of these before.

01:38:14.488 --> 01:38:16.924
Apparently it's milk chocolate
with caramel and peanut.

01:38:16.924 --> 01:38:18.559
Let's give it a try.

01:38:18.559 --> 01:38:20.094
That might get added to
my rotation, you know?

01:38:20.094 --> 01:38:20.928
That's pretty good.

01:38:20.928 --> 01:38:22.429
Next up, we have the Twirl.

01:38:22.429 --> 01:38:24.231
These are, like, ribboned chocolate bars

01:38:24.231 --> 01:38:26.667
which are then kind of
cased within more chocolate.

01:38:26.667 --> 01:38:28.235
It leads to quite an interesting texture

01:38:28.235 --> 01:38:29.103
and quite a nice taste.

01:38:29.103 --> 01:38:31.438
The only issue with Twirls
is that they do crumble

01:38:31.438 --> 01:38:32.606
and kind of go everywhere.

01:38:32.606 --> 01:38:34.375
You can also get Twirls
in an orange flavor.

01:38:34.375 --> 01:38:36.543
Then we're on to Wispa bars. Shh.

01:38:36.543 --> 01:38:37.611
I don't really know how they make these,

01:38:37.611 --> 01:38:39.713
because it's milk chocolate,
but it's, like, aerated.

01:38:39.713 --> 01:38:41.582
There's kind of little holes
all the way through it.

01:38:41.582 --> 01:38:44.451
We put a man on the moon, and
we aerated a chocolate bar.

01:38:44.451 --> 01:38:46.020
The result is a really
nice texture, actually.

01:38:46.020 --> 01:38:47.588
It sort of melts in your
mouth when you eat it.

01:38:47.588 --> 01:38:48.989
I've some American colleagues in the US.

01:38:48.989 --> 01:38:49.857
Last time I visited,

01:38:49.857 --> 01:38:51.525
this was the one thing they
asked me to bring over.

01:38:51.525 --> 01:38:53.027
You can also get Wispa gold bars.

01:38:53.027 --> 01:38:54.361
These are the same as regular Wispas,

01:38:54.361 --> 01:38:56.163
but they have a layer of
caramel running along the top.

01:38:56.163 --> 01:38:58.933
And the last-but-by-no-means-least
bar is the Freddo.

01:38:58.933 --> 01:39:01.602
It's basically just a tiny
piece of solid milk chocolate

01:39:01.602 --> 01:39:03.203
in the shape of Freddo the frog.

01:39:03.203 --> 01:39:05.372
But for people of a certain
generation, namely mine,

01:39:05.372 --> 01:39:07.141
they're also a surprising representation

01:39:07.141 --> 01:39:08.375
of economic inflation.

01:39:08.375 --> 01:39:10.344
To put on my angry-old-man
hat for a second,

01:39:10.344 --> 01:39:12.379
when I was a youngin', these were 10p,

01:39:12.379 --> 01:39:15.749
and then around 2005, prices
started to gradually creep up.

01:39:15.749 --> 01:39:17.251
Before we knew it, prices were as high

01:39:17.251 --> 01:39:18.986
as 30p for a Freddo.

01:39:18.986 --> 01:39:21.588
These outrageous prices
actually led to public outcry,

01:39:21.588 --> 01:39:23.290
so much so that they backed down,

01:39:23.290 --> 01:39:25.726
and I think nowadays they're around 25p.

01:39:25.726 --> 01:39:26.627
The Bank of England says

01:39:26.627 --> 01:39:29.530
that it should have been
around 17 or 18p by now,

01:39:29.530 --> 01:39:30.831
whereas we are getting charged 25,

01:39:30.831 --> 01:39:33.033
so Cadbury's, give us
some cheap Freddos again.

01:39:33.033 --> 01:39:34.301
Economic rant is now over.

01:39:34.301 --> 01:39:36.003
You can also get Freddos
in a caramel flavor.

01:39:36.003 --> 01:39:37.438
The last thing to add
to the chocolate bars

01:39:37.438 --> 01:39:38.672
is that you can get
pretty much all of them

01:39:38.672 --> 01:39:40.174
in the form of these share bags.

01:39:40.174 --> 01:39:42.242
They basically just condense
them into bite-size pieces

01:39:42.242 --> 01:39:44.311
and put them in a bag that
you can open and reseal.

01:39:44.311 --> 01:39:46.780
Next up, we have Dairy Milk Bites.

01:39:46.780 --> 01:39:48.415
There are two flavors
that we have right now,

01:39:48.415 --> 01:39:49.817
hazelnut and almond.

01:39:49.817 --> 01:39:53.387
They look pretty similar to
the Silk of these flavors,

01:39:53.387 --> 01:39:55.823
so I imagine these are just
smaller bite-sized versions.

01:39:55.823 --> 01:39:58.192
Next up, Lickables.

01:39:59.293 --> 01:40:00.394
Why have they done this?

01:40:00.394 --> 01:40:04.365
Thoughts on this? This is
clearly for small children.

01:40:04.365 --> 01:40:06.967
Somebody want to help me? I
have no idea how to open this.

01:40:06.967 --> 01:40:10.170
This feels like one of those puzzles.

01:40:10.170 --> 01:40:11.271
Oh!

01:40:12.673 --> 01:40:15.442
[crew clapping]

01:40:15.442 --> 01:40:17.144
The lower half of it was a chocolate,

01:40:17.144 --> 01:40:18.379
and the rest of it had this toy.

01:40:18.379 --> 01:40:19.513
Now to the chocolate.

01:40:19.513 --> 01:40:22.416
There's a QR code, because
most children have phones

01:40:22.416 --> 01:40:24.151
that they can scan this with.

01:40:24.151 --> 01:40:25.285
Oh!

01:40:25.285 --> 01:40:29.123
Looks like goopy Cadbury chocolate

01:40:29.123 --> 01:40:30.824
with chunks of Oreo,

01:40:30.824 --> 01:40:33.494
and you just gotta lick it.

01:40:35.829 --> 01:40:37.464
This is just weird, Cadbury.

01:40:37.464 --> 01:40:40.968
OK, next up we have Cadbury Chocobakes

01:40:40.968 --> 01:40:42.369
choc-filled cookies.

01:40:42.369 --> 01:40:44.605
In case you didn't think
this contained chocolate,

01:40:44.605 --> 01:40:47.041
they reminded you eight
times in the branding.

01:40:47.041 --> 01:40:50.377
The packaging and the design
feels a lot more premium.

01:40:50.377 --> 01:40:52.946
I feel like there's good
value for money here,

01:40:52.946 --> 01:40:54.681
because it was filled to the literal brim.

01:40:54.681 --> 01:40:55.716
Now we're going to go to this side.

01:40:55.716 --> 01:40:59.586
We have Oreo dipped in Cadbury, damn.

01:40:59.586 --> 01:41:01.055
I'm really enjoying this whole

01:41:01.055 --> 01:41:03.490
Oreo-Cadbury marriage over here.

01:41:03.490 --> 01:41:06.260
Now we have an Oreo biscuit

01:41:06.260 --> 01:41:08.796
coated in Cadbury chocolate.

01:41:08.796 --> 01:41:10.964
The Oreo biscuits are
just kind of overpowering,

01:41:10.964 --> 01:41:12.332
so it's all right.

01:41:12.332 --> 01:41:17.271
Next up we have this tin
can of rich dry fruits.

01:41:17.271 --> 01:41:19.406
Again, in the Cadbury Celebrations line.

01:41:19.406 --> 01:41:20.808
In India, a common gifting culture

01:41:20.808 --> 01:41:23.544
is to give a box of dry fruits and nuts,

01:41:23.544 --> 01:41:25.612
and so Cadbury's adapting
really well to that.

01:41:25.612 --> 01:41:27.347
All right, so the next thing
is something very different.

01:41:27.347 --> 01:41:30.350
This is actually Bournvita,
or Cadbury Bournvita,

01:41:30.350 --> 01:41:31.985
and this is a drinking chocolate.

01:41:31.985 --> 01:41:33.454
We drink a lot of milk here in India,

01:41:33.454 --> 01:41:35.289
and as kids, everybody was addicted

01:41:35.289 --> 01:41:38.492
to one of many different
drinking chocolates.

01:41:38.492 --> 01:41:41.595
Horlicks, Complan, I'm a Milo guy myself.

01:41:41.595 --> 01:41:44.164
There was Boost, and
then obviously Bournvita.

01:41:44.164 --> 01:41:47.367
I think most people were
not Bournvita people.

01:41:47.367 --> 01:41:51.205
This is Cadbury's range of choco melts,

01:41:51.205 --> 01:41:54.475
and it's a small disk of
chocolate that's used for baking.

01:41:54.475 --> 01:41:58.445
And finally, the last
three packets are toffees

01:41:58.445 --> 01:42:00.114
that Cadbury sells in bulk.

01:42:00.114 --> 01:42:01.915
This one is 5 Star bites.

01:42:01.915 --> 01:42:04.618
It's similar to the Dairy Milk minis.

01:42:04.618 --> 01:42:06.487
For all my Indian fans
of 5 Star out there,

01:42:06.487 --> 01:42:07.621
comment and let me know whether you're

01:42:07.621 --> 01:42:10.190
more of a Ramesh guy or Suresh guy.

01:42:10.190 --> 01:42:13.193
These are packs of toffees.
Eclairs, to be specific.

01:42:13.193 --> 01:42:14.461
This one is chocolate-flavored,

01:42:14.461 --> 01:42:16.096
and this one is coffee-flavored.

01:42:16.096 --> 01:42:17.698
Another quirky thing about India

01:42:17.698 --> 01:42:19.533
is sometimes when you
go to the local stores

01:42:19.533 --> 01:42:21.502
and you pay in cash and
they have to give you change

01:42:21.502 --> 01:42:22.369
but they don't have any,

01:42:22.369 --> 01:42:24.738
they'll just give you
one of these chocolates.

01:42:24.738 --> 01:42:27.341
And you can't really argue
it, you just grab it and go.

01:42:27.341 --> 01:42:28.509
I think it's very cute, actually.

01:42:28.509 --> 01:42:29.943
It's a very endearing thing about India.

01:42:29.943 --> 01:42:33.046
But remember, if you're gonna
take a chocolate from a store,

01:42:33.046 --> 01:42:35.415
screw all this. Take Melody.

01:42:35.415 --> 01:42:37.384
Melody is the best chocolate, all right?

01:42:37.384 --> 01:42:39.920
In the UK, Cadbury's offers
a lot of seasonal products.

01:42:39.920 --> 01:42:41.955
Now, we're recording this
episode in late October,

01:42:41.955 --> 01:42:44.324
so unfortunately we can't get
some of the most famous ones.

01:42:44.324 --> 01:42:45.526
What I'm of course referring to here

01:42:45.526 --> 01:42:47.895
are Cadbury Creme Eggs
and Cadbury Mini Eggs.

01:42:47.895 --> 01:42:49.196
In the UK, these are only available

01:42:49.196 --> 01:42:50.531
in the run-up to the Easter holidays,

01:42:50.531 --> 01:42:52.566
but while they are available,
they're wildly popular.

01:42:52.566 --> 01:42:54.301
Well, I will say, I don't like Creme Eggs.

01:42:54.301 --> 01:42:56.270
I take stick for this.
I think they're gross.

01:42:56.270 --> 01:42:58.205
The fondant in the middle is grim.

01:42:58.205 --> 01:42:59.840
You have to kind of, like, tongue it out.

01:42:59.840 --> 01:43:00.908
It's just really bizarre.

01:43:00.908 --> 01:43:02.176
Mini Eggs, however, are delicious.

01:43:02.176 --> 01:43:03.477
I don't know what they're
putting in the shells

01:43:03.477 --> 01:43:05.179
of those things, but,
God, they're amazing.

01:43:05.179 --> 01:43:06.813
While we can't get the
Easter exclusives right now,

01:43:06.813 --> 01:43:09.116
what we do have are Halloween
and Christmas options.

01:43:09.116 --> 01:43:11.285
For Halloween, I was able
to find these Goo Heads.

01:43:11.285 --> 01:43:12.686
I think these are kind
of the Halloween version

01:43:12.686 --> 01:43:14.655
of Creme Eggs, so I'm going
to crack one open and see.

01:43:14.655 --> 01:43:16.356
That does look exactly
the same as a Creme Egg,

01:43:16.356 --> 01:43:18.659
even down to the patterning
that's printed on the egg.

01:43:18.659 --> 01:43:21.161
I mean, yeah, that's pretty
much just a Creme Egg.

01:43:22.029 --> 01:43:22.963
I just don't like them.

01:43:22.963 --> 01:43:25.566
Now, for Christmas exclusives,
I found these Cadbury Puds.

01:43:25.566 --> 01:43:28.802
These are Dairy Milk chocolate
balls with a truffle center,

01:43:28.802 --> 01:43:30.804
hazelnut pieces, and rice crisps.

01:43:30.804 --> 01:43:31.638
They sound pretty good.

01:43:31.638 --> 01:43:33.707
We also found Cadbury Mini Snow Balls,

01:43:33.707 --> 01:43:35.842
which are milk chocolate
in a crisp sugar shell.

01:43:35.842 --> 01:43:36.843
They might hurt a little bit more

01:43:36.843 --> 01:43:37.878
than a normal snowball fight

01:43:37.878 --> 01:43:39.246
if you have one of these
thrown at your head.

01:43:39.246 --> 01:43:40.614
And, of course, you can get a Dairy Milk

01:43:40.614 --> 01:43:42.082
Advent calendar for Christmas.

01:43:43.183 --> 01:43:45.786
It looks like some kind of mud monster.

01:43:45.786 --> 01:43:48.255
Moving away from seasonal
items, we have Cadbury Eclairs.

01:43:48.255 --> 01:43:50.657
Cadbury Eclairs are quite
tough pieces of toffee

01:43:50.657 --> 01:43:51.825
with some chocolate in the center.

01:43:51.825 --> 01:43:53.460
They're a pretty good jaw workout,

01:43:53.460 --> 01:43:54.394
but I do quite like these.

01:43:54.394 --> 01:43:56.463
And another iconic
Cadbury item is Buttons.

01:43:56.463 --> 01:43:58.532
These are bags of disks
of Dairy Milk chocolate.

01:43:58.532 --> 01:44:00.634
Real classic. These have
been around for years.

01:44:00.634 --> 01:44:02.469
From there, we're moving on
to Cadbury's biscuit options,

01:44:02.469 --> 01:44:04.771
possibly the most iconic
of which are Fingers.

01:44:04.771 --> 01:44:06.607
These are thin sticks of sweet biscuit

01:44:06.607 --> 01:44:07.941
covered in Dairy Milk chocolate.

01:44:07.941 --> 01:44:09.309
They're very tasty,
they're pretty moreish,

01:44:09.309 --> 01:44:12.279
and they come in these kind
of iconic sleeve-tray things.

01:44:12.279 --> 01:44:13.947
I know with Joe we have a caffeine meter,

01:44:13.947 --> 01:44:16.216
but if I had a sugar meter, pew!

01:44:16.216 --> 01:44:17.684
We are blasting off right now. Whoo!

01:44:17.684 --> 01:44:19.820
We also have some other flavor
options, including mint,

01:44:19.820 --> 01:44:22.222
orange, Bournville dark,
and, finally, white.

01:44:22.222 --> 01:44:24.524
Roundies are circular
layered wafer biscuits

01:44:24.524 --> 01:44:25.592
covered in Dairy Milk chocolate.

01:44:25.592 --> 01:44:26.627
If you're a fan of wafers,

01:44:26.627 --> 01:44:28.629
you can also get Timeout Wafer bars.

01:44:28.629 --> 01:44:29.930
Again, it's chocolate wafers

01:44:29.930 --> 01:44:31.265
layered and surrounded by chocolate,

01:44:31.265 --> 01:44:33.767
but this time in more of a bar
form than a circular biscuit.

01:44:33.767 --> 01:44:35.902
The next Cadbury biscuits
option is Animals.

01:44:35.902 --> 01:44:38.572
"Freddo has hopped into the
jungle to join his friends."

01:44:38.572 --> 01:44:39.973
These are little animal-shaped biscuits

01:44:39.973 --> 01:44:41.842
which on one side are
covered with chocolate.

01:44:41.842 --> 01:44:43.377
I don't think I've eaten
one of these as an adult,

01:44:43.377 --> 01:44:44.978
but they were an excellent
lunch-box addition

01:44:44.978 --> 01:44:45.812
when I was a little kid.

01:44:45.812 --> 01:44:48.181
I'd also be remiss not
to talk about Mini Rolls.

01:44:48.181 --> 01:44:49.483
These are an iconic British snack.

01:44:49.483 --> 01:44:51.084
What it is, is a chocolate sponge

01:44:51.084 --> 01:44:52.819
with this kind of cream
swirl in the middle,

01:44:52.819 --> 01:44:54.421
surrounded by milk chocolate.

01:44:54.421 --> 01:44:56.256
I'm not sure why the Mini
Roll is currently saying,

01:44:56.256 --> 01:44:58.792
"I'm rich and famous," but
good for the Mini Roll.

01:44:58.792 --> 01:44:59.826
These are great.

01:44:59.826 --> 01:45:01.595
Finally, Cadbury's offers
some baked options,

01:45:01.595 --> 01:45:03.030
which you might find in the bakery section

01:45:03.030 --> 01:45:04.131
of your local supermarket.

01:45:04.131 --> 01:45:05.799
These can include things
like doughnuts and muffins,

01:45:05.799 --> 01:45:08.335
but the ones I was able to
find today were flapjack bites.

01:45:08.335 --> 01:45:11.071
In the UK, when we say flapjacks,
we don't mean pancakes,

01:45:11.071 --> 01:45:13.106
which I think Americans can say sometimes.

01:45:13.106 --> 01:45:15.575
Flapjacks over here are kind
of like oats held together

01:45:15.575 --> 01:45:17.844
with honey, golden syrup,
and some other stuff.

01:45:17.844 --> 01:45:18.979
And these mini cookies.

01:45:21.315 --> 01:45:22.149
Here's everything in a bar

01:45:22.149 --> 01:45:23.717
of Dairy Milk chocolate in the UK.

01:45:23.717 --> 01:45:24.985
Here's everything you'll find in a bar

01:45:24.985 --> 01:45:26.720
of Dairy Milk chocolate here in India.

01:45:26.720 --> 01:45:28.322
So, the list of ingredients
is pretty much the same

01:45:28.322 --> 01:45:29.556
in the UK and in India.

01:45:29.556 --> 01:45:31.958
But the UK uses palm and shea fats,

01:45:31.958 --> 01:45:34.461
which is not specifically
listed here in India.

01:45:34.461 --> 01:45:36.830
India goes into a little bit
more detail on the flavorings

01:45:36.830 --> 01:45:38.732
used in the chocolate,
listing natural vanillin

01:45:38.732 --> 01:45:40.600
as well as artificial ethyl vanillin.

01:45:40.600 --> 01:45:41.435
As the name suggests,

01:45:41.435 --> 01:45:43.670
this is the main component
of vanilla-bean extract.

01:45:43.670 --> 01:45:46.173
Some kind of vanillin is likely
present in the UK chocolate,

01:45:46.173 --> 01:45:48.408
it's just contained within
the flavorings on the list.

01:45:48.408 --> 01:45:49.810
But how much chocolate

01:45:49.810 --> 01:45:52.112
are you actually getting
in your chocolate?

01:45:52.112 --> 01:45:54.247
The Food Safety and
Standards Authority of India

01:45:54.247 --> 01:45:55.649
has some minimum requirements

01:45:55.649 --> 01:45:57.951
for what milk chocolate should contain.

01:45:57.951 --> 01:46:02.055
The rules are 25% total fat, 2% milk fat,

01:46:02.055 --> 01:46:06.493
2.5% cocoa solids, and 10.5% milk solids.

01:46:06.493 --> 01:46:08.261
We have equivalent rules here in the UK.

01:46:08.261 --> 01:46:11.064
The Cocoa and Chocolate
Products Regulations of 2003

01:46:11.064 --> 01:46:14.534
set the minimums for milk
chocolate at 25% total fat,

01:46:14.534 --> 01:46:17.504
5% milk fat, 20% dry cocoa solids,

01:46:17.504 --> 01:46:21.608
2.5% dry nonfat cocoa solids,
and 20% dry milk solids.

01:46:21.608 --> 01:46:23.343
Cadbury in the UK says
its chocolate contains

01:46:23.343 --> 01:46:25.045
23% milk solids

01:46:25.045 --> 01:46:28.215
and meets the EU minimum
of 20% for cocoa solids.

01:46:28.215 --> 01:46:30.250
India's Cadbury packaging says it contains

01:46:30.250 --> 01:46:32.018
over 22% milk solids.

01:46:32.018 --> 01:46:34.688
So thank you, Cadbury,
for not being chindi.

01:46:34.688 --> 01:46:37.524
It is interesting that Indian
rules do not have a minimum

01:46:37.524 --> 01:46:40.427
for dry fat-free cocoa
solids in milk chocolate.

01:46:40.427 --> 01:46:43.864
The dark chocolates, however,
have a minimum, and it's 14%.

01:46:43.864 --> 01:46:46.233
"Dry cocoa solids" tends
to refer to cocoa powder,

01:46:46.233 --> 01:46:47.934
which is one of the purest forms of cocoa.

01:46:47.934 --> 01:46:49.136
Having more cocoa solids

01:46:49.136 --> 01:46:51.538
therefore gives the end product
a stronger chocolate taste.

01:46:53.507 --> 01:46:56.309
100 grams of Dairy Milk in
the UK contains the following.

01:46:56.309 --> 01:46:58.879
100 grams of Dairy Milk in India contains:

01:46:58.879 --> 01:47:00.313
The calories are actually identical.

01:47:00.313 --> 01:47:01.581
The least-healthy bar in the UK

01:47:01.581 --> 01:47:03.583
is the Big Taste toffee whole nut bar.

01:47:03.583 --> 01:47:06.720
One of these contains 560
calories per 100 grams,

01:47:06.720 --> 01:47:08.221
a slight increase on Dairy Milk.

01:47:08.221 --> 01:47:11.391
But what is the least-healthy
chocolate bar here in India?

01:47:11.391 --> 01:47:13.493
It's the Dairy Milk Silk hazelnut.

01:47:13.493 --> 01:47:16.563
100 grams of this contains 571 calories,

01:47:16.563 --> 01:47:19.933
which is more than any bar in the UK.

01:47:19.933 --> 01:47:22.836
I guess it's a win? I'm
counting it as a win.

01:47:22.969 --> 01:47:24.304
Nikhil: From calorie
down to portion sizes,

01:47:24.304 --> 01:47:25.739
we wanted to find out all the differences

01:47:25.739 --> 01:47:28.408
between Lay's chips in
the US and in India.

01:47:28.408 --> 01:47:30.076
This is "Food Wars."

01:47:33.647 --> 01:47:35.515
Here are all the Lay's
chips you'll find in India

01:47:35.515 --> 01:47:37.551
that you won't find in the US.

01:47:37.551 --> 01:47:39.486
And here are all the Lay's chips in the US

01:47:39.486 --> 01:47:40.821
you can't find in India.

01:47:40.821 --> 01:47:44.157
Oh, my good God. Yeah!

01:47:44.157 --> 01:47:46.226
To begin things, I'm
going to go with the one

01:47:46.226 --> 01:47:49.329
I hate the most, Spanish tomato tango.

01:47:49.329 --> 01:47:51.331
Yeah, I just never
really liked this flavor.

01:47:51.331 --> 01:47:53.333
It's just too heavy on the tomato side.

01:47:56.369 --> 01:47:59.206
No. Oh, man, that aftertaste is horrible.

01:47:59.206 --> 01:48:01.174
I have nothing nice to
say about this flavor.

01:48:01.174 --> 01:48:03.143
Also, just to note, our
standard Lay's chips

01:48:03.143 --> 01:48:04.644
