01:48:04.644 --> 01:48:06.913
We do also sell the flat style,

01:48:06.913 --> 01:48:09.115
but that's more of a
special variety of Lay's.

01:48:09.115 --> 01:48:12.185
Next, it's West Indies
hot and sweet chili,

01:48:12.185 --> 01:48:14.654
formerly Caribbean hot and sweet chili.

01:48:16.189 --> 01:48:18.158
That's what I'm talking about.

01:48:18.158 --> 01:48:19.125
Get out of here!

01:48:19.125 --> 01:48:22.929
And now for the maharaja of Indian Lay's,

01:48:22.929 --> 01:48:24.898
magic masala.

01:48:24.898 --> 01:48:26.233
If you haven't heard of this,

01:48:26.233 --> 01:48:27.501
you must be living under a rock,

01:48:27.501 --> 01:48:30.470
because this is the
little emperor of chips.

01:48:30.470 --> 01:48:33.206
Commonly known as blue Lay's.

01:48:33.206 --> 01:48:36.209
Look at this chip, dude!

01:48:36.209 --> 01:48:37.511
Oh, my God.

01:48:39.980 --> 01:48:41.014
Oh, my God.

01:48:41.948 --> 01:48:44.184
It's already so spicy.

01:48:44.184 --> 01:48:47.020
The reason this chip has
become so popular in India

01:48:47.020 --> 01:48:49.322
is because they have
actually managed to capture

01:48:49.322 --> 01:48:51.625
the masala of India so well.

01:48:51.625 --> 01:48:53.727
And masala, if you're wondering,
is, like, ground-up spices

01:48:53.727 --> 01:48:57.631
that are added to every
single dish we eat here.

01:48:57.631 --> 01:48:59.299
This is truly magic.

01:48:59.299 --> 01:49:01.301
I want to know what they're like.

01:49:01.301 --> 01:49:02.602
Joe got himself something.

01:49:03.670 --> 01:49:04.504
Oh, man.

01:49:04.504 --> 01:49:08.742
And the chip bags in India
are, like, much harder to open.

01:49:08.742 --> 01:49:10.977
Oh, man! You guys got
them locked up tight.

01:49:12.646 --> 01:49:14.314
Got a rip! OK.

01:49:14.314 --> 01:49:15.615
Yeah.

01:49:15.615 --> 01:49:17.150
Oh, yeah.

01:49:17.150 --> 01:49:18.985
Damn, these are good!

01:49:18.985 --> 01:49:20.487
Not too spicy.

01:49:20.487 --> 01:49:21.788
Great flavor.

01:49:21.788 --> 01:49:23.456
We have so many flavors.

01:49:23.456 --> 01:49:25.058
I couldn't get them all for this shoot.

01:49:25.058 --> 01:49:26.826
I mean, I'll just start right here.

01:49:27.761 --> 01:49:30.030
Barbecue. This is the classic chip.

01:49:30.030 --> 01:49:32.165
I think this is more popular
than the classic, to be honest.

01:49:32.165 --> 01:49:33.867
The US has, I would say,

01:49:33.867 --> 01:49:36.736
at least 10 different variations
of barbecue, possibly more.

01:49:36.736 --> 01:49:38.538
So to have just, like,
standard barbecue is

01:49:38.538 --> 01:49:40.907
pretty bold move by Lay's.

01:49:40.907 --> 01:49:42.275
Salt and vinegar.

01:49:43.209 --> 01:49:44.277
[dreamy harp tune]

01:49:44.277 --> 01:49:45.345
Love salt and vinegar so much.

01:49:45.345 --> 01:49:47.247
I love it so much.

01:49:47.247 --> 01:49:49.416
Top chip. Top chip right here.

01:49:49.416 --> 01:49:50.650
Love salt and vinegar.

01:49:50.650 --> 01:49:51.851
Cheddar and sour cream.

01:49:51.851 --> 01:49:54.187
Ha ha ha, limón.

01:49:54.187 --> 01:49:56.556
Another favorite. Oh, man.

01:49:56.556 --> 01:50:00.126
It seems like lime-flavored
chips would be weird,

01:50:00.126 --> 01:50:01.628
or citrusy chips, but ...

01:50:02.829 --> 01:50:03.663
so good.

01:50:03.663 --> 01:50:05.732
And these are, like, really limey.

01:50:05.732 --> 01:50:08.735
All the superfans watching
know I do not like pickles.

01:50:11.938 --> 01:50:12.939
No.

01:50:12.939 --> 01:50:14.274
Let's kick it up a notch.

01:50:14.274 --> 01:50:15.742
Flamin' Hot dill pickle.

01:50:15.742 --> 01:50:17.110
And the Flamin' Hot, that font,

01:50:17.110 --> 01:50:19.713
that implies that's
Flamin' Hot Cheetos, right?

01:50:21.748 --> 01:50:23.783
Mm. Better.

01:50:23.783 --> 01:50:25.285
Still not that good.

01:50:25.285 --> 01:50:27.654
Last in this group is a chili limón.

01:50:28.922 --> 01:50:29.756
Yeah.

01:50:31.291 --> 01:50:32.525
These are coming home with me.

01:50:32.525 --> 01:50:33.927
Other flavors in this category

01:50:33.927 --> 01:50:35.528
that I couldn't get at
the time of filming,

01:50:35.528 --> 01:50:39.199
