like chicken malai tikka

01:56:17.036 --> 01:56:19.505
dipped in pudina chutney.

01:56:19.505 --> 01:56:21.341
This is very unique.

01:56:21.341 --> 01:56:25.411
Our next flavor is sizzling barbecue.

01:56:25.411 --> 01:56:28.982
Oh, the reason this is called Lay's Maxx,

01:56:28.982 --> 01:56:32.885
it's because it has
max crunch, max flavor,

01:56:32.885 --> 01:56:34.053
and max taste.

01:56:34.053 --> 01:56:37.890
And I can wholeheartedly say
both of these have delivered.

01:56:40.927 --> 01:56:44.464
Mm. It even smells
strongly of barbecue, so.

01:56:44.464 --> 01:56:45.732
These work. They're great.

01:56:47.066 --> 01:56:49.302
More fun chip styles.

01:56:49.302 --> 01:56:52.405
I think we can call these the India style,

01:56:52.405 --> 01:56:54.574
but we also call them the wavy style.

01:56:54.574 --> 01:56:56.709
They are wavy, hence the name.

01:56:56.709 --> 01:56:59.545
And you can get them in
original, reduced fat,

01:56:59.545 --> 01:57:01.914
honey barbecue, ranch,

01:57:01.914 --> 01:57:03.883
and you can also get
them in salt and pepper,

01:57:03.883 --> 01:57:05.351
lightly salted,

01:57:05.351 --> 01:57:07.954
fat, low fat, if I
didn't say that already.

01:57:07.954 --> 01:57:09.655
The waves are, like, wider.

01:57:09.655 --> 01:57:12.759
You guys have, like,
really condensed waves.

01:57:12.759 --> 01:57:15.728
Lay's apparently wanted to
answer the age-old question,

01:57:15.728 --> 01:57:17.697
how can we copy something popular

01:57:17.697 --> 01:57:20.500
and make it much, much worse?

01:57:20.500 --> 01:57:22.168
And Stax were invented.

01:57:22.168 --> 01:57:23.536
You guys know what Pringles are, right?

01:57:23.536 --> 01:57:24.804
Of course you do. Well.

01:57:24.804 --> 01:57:27.540
[chip pieces rattling] Hear that?

01:57:27.540 --> 01:57:29.075
"We'll put them in a tube.
They won't break as easily."

01:57:29.075 --> 01:57:30.977
Right? [chip pieces rattling]

01:57:30.977 --> 01:57:33.346
Holy f---.

01:57:33.346 --> 01:57:34.480
Look at this.

01:57:37.984 --> 01:57:39.619
Then what was the point of
putting it in this tube?

01:57:39.619 --> 01:57:41.220
I hate this so much.

01:57:41.220 --> 01:57:43.656
But to really prove my point,

01:57:43.656 --> 01:57:45.224
yo, dog, look what I got.

01:57:45.224 --> 01:57:49.128
By the way, paper too. Excellent idea,

01:57:49.128 --> 01:57:50.930
Dave Pringle, whatever your name is.

01:57:57.937 --> 01:57:59.138
F--- Stax.

01:57:59.138 --> 01:58:01.707
And now to our final set of exclusives,

01:58:01.707 --> 01:58:03.810
the gourmet collection.

01:58:03.810 --> 01:58:06.245
I've had a lot of gourmet food in my life,

01:58:06.245 --> 01:58:10.383
and I've very rarely been
actually impressed with the food.

01:58:10.383 --> 01:58:12.919
Vintage cheese and paprika!

01:58:14.020 --> 01:58:16.456
Vintage cheese and paprika.

01:58:17.857 --> 01:58:19.058
Oh.

01:58:19.058 --> 01:58:20.426
If I had tasted this chip

01:58:20.426 --> 01:58:22.462
without any of the fancy packaging,

01:58:22.462 --> 01:58:24.263
I don't think gourmet is the first word

01:58:24.263 --> 01:58:25.398
that would come to my head.

01:58:25.398 --> 01:58:27.166
Thai sweet chili gourmet.

01:58:29.869 --> 01:58:33.539
This literally tastes like
the West Indies hot and chili,

01:58:33.539 --> 01:58:34.540
but on a flat chip.

01:58:34.540 --> 01:58:36.609
So gourmet is just packaging.

01:58:36.609 --> 01:58:38.111
That's what we've learned
from this experiment

01:58:38.111 --> 01:58:39.879
with these two chips.

01:58:39.879 --> 01:58:41.114
Skippable.

01:58:41.114 --> 01:58:43.916
In addition to that, we
also have Lay's Poppables.

01:58:43.916 --> 01:58:46.252
Poppables come in sea salt and vinegar --

01:58:46.252 --> 01:58:49.455
oh, Julius Pringle! That
was his name. Not Dave.

01:58:49.455 --> 01:58:52.358
They also have Poppables
sea salt and vinegar,

01:58:52.358 --> 01:58:54.694
Poppables sea salt,
Poppable white cheddar,

01:58:54.694 --> 01:58:56.496
and Poppable honey barbecue.

01:58:56.496 --> 01:58:57.964
OK, I don't want to eat all these.

01:58:57.964 --> 01:59:00.066
What's the cereal that looks like this?

01:59:00.066 --> 01:59:01.134
Is it Chex?

01:59:03.536 --> 01:59:05.471
If you got these on accident, eat them,

01:59:05.471 --> 01:59:08.774
but I wouldn't reach for these
over regular potato chips.

01:59:10.810 --> 01:59:14.013
Here in India, our Lay's chips
packets come in five sizes.

01:59:14.013 --> 01:59:16.349
There's 30 grams, 50 grams,

01:59:16.349 --> 01:59:18.751
73 grams, 104 grams,

01:59:18.751 --> 01:59:21.254
and 174 grams.

01:59:21.254 --> 01:59:23.356
The big boy. The party pack.

01:59:23.356 --> 01:59:25.124
I feel like I could eat
this whole thing on my own,

01:59:25.124 --> 01:59:26.192
to be honest.

01:59:26.192 --> 01:59:30.530
In the US, our Lay's chips
come in six variety of sizes.

01:59:30.530 --> 01:59:32.832
All the way down here, got a 28-gram bag,

01:59:32.832 --> 01:59:34.400
which comes in the multipack.

01:59:34.400 --> 01:59:37.136
Next up, 74.4-gram bag.

01:59:37.136 --> 01:59:40.806
In the middle here, there's
also an elusive 78-gram bag.

01:59:40.806 --> 01:59:44.577
Look, I saw it on Target.com
and Walmart.com. It exists.

01:59:44.577 --> 01:59:47.480
It just wasn't available
anywhere in Southern California.

01:59:47.480 --> 01:59:48.548
I looked, OK?

01:59:48.548 --> 01:59:50.082
One step up, we have what I think

01:59:50.082 --> 01:59:53.352
is the classic grocery-store bag,

01:59:53.352 --> 01:59:57.857
226 gram, aka the 8-ounce bag.

01:59:57.857 --> 01:59:59.492
You've seen it a million
times. This is the one.

01:59:59.492 --> 02:00:02.428
Right next to that one
is the family-sized bag,

02:00:02.428 --> 02:00:04.063
which I also couldn't get ahold of.

02:00:04.063 --> 02:00:06.432
297.6-gram bag.

02:00:06.432 --> 02:00:09.569
I couldn't find it because
the American family is dead.

02:00:09.569 --> 02:00:12.138
But what is alive and well is,
of course, our biggest size,

02:00:12.138 --> 02:00:16.242
the party size, 368 grams.

02:00:16.242 --> 02:00:20.112
All you family-less partyers,
Lay's has you covered.

02:00:20.112 --> 02:00:22.915
That means that the biggest bag in the US

02:00:22.915 --> 02:00:26.519
is this much larger than
the biggest bag in India.

02:00:26.519 --> 02:00:28.321
But wait, there's more,

02:00:28.321 --> 02:00:30.590
or less, depending on
the packet that you get,

02:00:30.590 --> 02:00:31.857
because according to Amazon,

02:00:31.857 --> 02:00:34.594
the weights of these
different packets might vary.

02:00:34.594 --> 02:00:36.529
So they're given a weight range.

02:00:36.529 --> 02:00:38.731
The biggest weight difference
is in our largest pack

02:00:38.731 --> 02:00:43.202
of 174 to 190 grams, which
is a difference of 16 grams.

02:00:43.202 --> 02:00:45.504
So let's see how much
we get in one packet.

02:00:45.504 --> 02:00:48.174
Ooh!

02:00:48.174 --> 02:00:52.712
175 grams, one gram extra
from what is advertised,

02:00:52.712 --> 02:00:53.879
which is, I'll take it.

02:00:53.879 --> 02:00:56.382
So let me show you what 16
grams of chips looks like,

02:00:56.382 --> 02:00:58.751
so you can see what you're
potentially missing out on.

02:00:58.751 --> 02:01:00.853
It doesn't seem like a
lot, but I think that's

02:01:00.853 --> 02:01:03.022
quite a substantial amount of
chips you're missing out on.

02:01:03.022 --> 02:01:07.760
To be fair, they did write
174 grams only on the pack.

02:01:07.760 --> 02:01:10.763
In the US, our flavor bags weigh less

02:01:10.763 --> 02:01:12.365
than the original-flavor bag.

02:01:12.365 --> 02:01:15.801
Take this barbecue-flavored Lay's bag.

02:01:15.801 --> 02:01:20.606
It weighs 7.75 ounces, or 7 ¾ ounces.

02:01:20.606 --> 02:01:22.308
Yuelei, can we get in there?

02:01:22.308 --> 02:01:23.409
You see that? Thank you.

02:01:23.409 --> 02:01:26.579
Compared to the 8 ounce you
get with the original bag.

02:01:26.579 --> 02:01:29.548
OK. Same price, less product.

02:01:29.548 --> 02:01:31.584
Now, Harry did research on that episode,

02:01:31.584 --> 02:01:33.552
so take it away, Harry.

02:01:33.552 --> 02:01:35.321
What? No, do your own research.

02:01:35.321 --> 02:01:37.590
According to Harry's research
from the last Lay's episode,

02:01:37.590 --> 02:01:41.027
back in 2014, PepsiCo claimed
the reason that there is

02:01:41.027 --> 02:01:44.397
a slightly higher price per
ounce for flavored chips

02:01:44.397 --> 02:01:45.698
is the added seasoning.

02:01:45.698 --> 02:01:48.267
So then, Lay's,

02:01:48.267 --> 02:01:51.470
can you explain to me why
this lightly salted bag

02:01:51.470 --> 02:01:53.472
gives you fewer chips
than the original bag?

02:01:53.472 --> 02:01:56.375
It's more money but less salt, eh, Lay's?

02:01:56.375 --> 02:01:57.543
Check it out.

02:01:57.543 --> 02:02:01.147
The lightly salted, so
less salted than this,

02:02:01.147 --> 02:02:02.782
also 7 ¾.

02:02:02.782 --> 02:02:05.184
While we're exposing potential Lay's lies,

02:02:05.184 --> 02:02:07.887
this 28-gram bag in the US

02:02:07.887 --> 02:02:12.058
supposedly contains 15 chips,
according to Lay's website.

02:02:12.058 --> 02:02:14.160
Let's see how accurate this is.

02:02:14.160 --> 02:02:16.362
And I'm going to count all the
chips in this 30-gram packet

02:02:16.362 --> 02:02:17.630
to see how many we have.

02:02:20.366 --> 02:02:23.135
I mean, it doesn't contain one whole chip.

02:02:24.270 --> 02:02:25.604
One.

02:02:25.604 --> 02:02:28.708
12, 13.

02:02:28.708 --> 02:02:32.511
I mean, if we're doing it
by chip-related piles ...

02:02:32.511 --> 02:02:33.746
six, 12, eight?

02:02:33.746 --> 02:02:35.715
Close to 18 chips per bag.

02:02:35.715 --> 02:02:38.084
Huh. All right, I'll concede.

02:02:38.084 --> 02:02:40.019
Cool, so that's 24 chips.

02:02:40.019 --> 02:02:42.755
I would say, realistically,
this is, like, 20 chips

02:02:42.755 --> 02:02:44.890
that have been broken
into many other pieces.

02:02:44.890 --> 02:02:47.226
But let's be real, they
could've fit a lot more chips

02:02:47.226 --> 02:02:48.227
into this packet.

02:02:48.227 --> 02:02:51.297
And Lay's is notorious
for filling it with air.

02:02:51.297 --> 02:02:52.698
It's actually nitrogen gas,

02:02:52.698 --> 02:02:55.167
which helps preserve the chips
and also acts as a cushion

02:02:55.167 --> 02:02:57.169
to stop them from getting
smashed in transit.

02:02:57.169 --> 02:02:58.003
I mean ...

02:02:59.171 --> 02:03:00.973
What would it have been
like without the cushion?

02:03:00.973 --> 02:03:02.942
This whole bag would've
been dust, apparently.

02:03:02.942 --> 02:03:05.711
But what is the
air-to-chip ratio, you ask?

02:03:05.711 --> 02:03:07.847
Let's find out in a new
segment I like to call

02:03:07.847 --> 02:03:10.082
the Ar-chip-medes principle.

02:03:13.886 --> 02:03:16.389
Can I just say, this is
one of the weirdest things

02:03:16.389 --> 02:03:17.556
I've done in my life.

02:03:17.556 --> 02:03:20.960
A generous 55 ml of chips in this packet.

02:03:20.960 --> 02:03:23.662
Now let's measure how
much the packet itself

02:03:23.662 --> 02:03:25.631
can hold in volume.

02:03:25.631 --> 02:03:28.033
Score!

02:03:28.033 --> 02:03:29.935
Ooh, this smells so bad.

02:03:30.803 --> 02:03:32.037
900 ml.

02:03:32.037 --> 02:03:35.608
That's 845 ml of chips

02:03:35.608 --> 02:03:37.510
that we could have had, Lay's.

02:03:37.510 --> 02:03:38.811
I feel cheated.

02:03:38.811 --> 02:03:41.514
I think to make it more
accurate, let's do four.

02:03:41.514 --> 02:03:42.815
And then we'll fill this guy up,

02:03:42.815 --> 02:03:43.916
and then we'll divide by four,

02:03:43.916 --> 02:03:45.084
and that would give us
the average of those.

02:03:45.084 --> 02:03:46.118
Does that make sense?

02:03:46.118 --> 02:03:46.952
Dust.

02:03:49.155 --> 02:03:51.390
Uh-huh, all right.

02:03:51.390 --> 02:03:52.925
Oh, man. All right.

02:03:52.925 --> 02:03:57.396
Can I please have the scientific
chip-crunching nunchucks?

02:03:57.396 --> 02:03:58.631
Throw them!

02:03:58.631 --> 02:04:01.400
Ah! Whoa!

02:04:01.400 --> 02:04:02.234
Look out, chips.

02:04:02.234 --> 02:04:04.670
Pow. Pow. Pow.

02:04:07.173 --> 02:04:11.410
2.75 fluid ounces per bag.

02:04:11.410 --> 02:04:14.413
Now that's science you can use.

02:04:14.413 --> 02:04:16.982
So, now we're going to
fill this with water.

02:04:16.982 --> 02:04:17.817
Ugh.

02:04:17.817 --> 02:04:21.520
The whole thing's 20, which is about 2.75.

02:04:21.520 --> 02:04:25.691
17.25 units of whatever.

02:04:25.691 --> 02:04:27.460
Cubic fluid ounces?

02:04:27.460 --> 02:04:29.462
Even more interesting air information.

02:04:29.462 --> 02:04:31.931
Because of India's varied geography,

02:04:31.931 --> 02:04:34.066
the amount of air that's
packed into these packets

02:04:34.066 --> 02:04:36.235
is different for different altitudes.

02:04:36.235 --> 02:04:38.404
For example, in cities of higher altitude,

02:04:38.404 --> 02:04:40.206
like Leh in the Himalayas,

02:04:40.206 --> 02:04:43.709
there is the risk of
these packets exploding

02:04:43.709 --> 02:04:45.678
due to the low atmospheric pressure.

02:04:45.678 --> 02:04:46.979
And so, when they're sent there,

02:04:46.979 --> 02:04:50.082
they're sent with no air
at all inside of them.

02:04:50.082 --> 02:04:53.085
And so they run the risk of
being crushed in transport,

02:04:53.085 --> 02:04:57.122
so they have to be taken as
delicately as a crate of eggs.

02:04:59.425 --> 02:05:01.327
But what about price?

02:05:01.327 --> 02:05:04.597
This is our largest chips
packet, the 174 grams.

02:05:04.597 --> 02:05:08.601
And on Swiggy and Amazon, this
sells for about 78 rupees,

02:05:08.601 --> 02:05:10.603
which is about a dollar right now.

02:05:10.603 --> 02:05:12.838
And that equals ...

02:05:14.607 --> 02:05:17.977
rupees 0.44 per gram.

02:05:17.977 --> 02:05:20.513
About $0.005.

02:05:20.513 --> 02:05:23.816
And, yes, I did all of that
math and conversion in my head.

02:05:23.816 --> 02:05:25.317
Here in the US, if we break it down

02:05:25.317 --> 02:05:26.485
starting with this big bag,

02:05:26.485 --> 02:05:30.489
the 226.8 gram, aka 8-ounce, bag,

02:05:30.489 --> 02:05:33.025
it's $3.99 at Target,

02:05:33.025 --> 02:05:36.061
or 316.58 rupees.

02:05:36.061 --> 02:05:37.563
Yes, it's a bigger bag, I know.

02:05:37.563 --> 02:05:41.066
So breaking it down per gram,
we found that in the US,

02:05:41.066 --> 02:05:45.237
the cost is a 260%
increase compared to India.

02:05:45.237 --> 02:05:46.705
While we do enjoy our Lay's chips,

02:05:46.705 --> 02:05:51.043
we also have a giant chip
culture here in India.

02:05:51.043 --> 02:05:53.078
In fact, these are called hot chips,

02:05:53.078 --> 02:05:54.813
and they're sold all across India

02:05:54.813 --> 02:05:57.616
at stalls called hot-chip stalls,

02:05:57.616 --> 02:06:00.152
where, basically, they
have a giant frying pan,

02:06:00.152 --> 02:06:02.187
and they cut the potato in front of you

02:06:02.187 --> 02:06:04.156
to these thin slices and fry it

02:06:04.156 --> 02:06:06.692
and give it to you nice,
hot-hot, fresh-fresh.

02:06:06.692 --> 02:06:09.328
And so, for 174 grams,
which is the same as this,

02:06:09.328 --> 02:06:13.365
you're paying rupees 45
for a lot fresher chips.

02:06:13.365 --> 02:06:15.267
So as you can see, Lay's
is competing against

02:06:15.267 --> 02:06:17.803
a giant chip market here in India

02:06:17.803 --> 02:06:20.039
and doing pretty well, I would say.

02:06:22.608 --> 02:06:24.043
Now for the burning question.

02:06:24.043 --> 02:06:26.178
Are there any questionable ingredients

02:06:26.178 --> 02:06:28.981
that are in your Lay's chips
that you need to watch out for?

02:06:28.981 --> 02:06:32.351
Fret not, because Joe and I
have found them out for you.

02:06:32.351 --> 02:06:35.154
As far as the basic salted version goes,

02:06:35.154 --> 02:06:35.988
you're totally fine.

02:06:35.988 --> 02:06:39.291
Both in India and the US,
they're made of potatoes,

02:06:39.291 --> 02:06:40.893
vegetable oil, salt.

02:06:40.893 --> 02:06:42.828
Warning! Warning alert!

02:06:42.828 --> 02:06:43.963
Here in India, some of our flavors

02:06:43.963 --> 02:06:46.198
have an ingredient called
potassium chloride.

02:06:46.198 --> 02:06:48.200
In regular doses, this is completely safe,

02:06:48.200 --> 02:06:50.636
and it's a low-sodium alternative to salt.

02:06:50.636 --> 02:06:53.539
However, it's also one of
the three ingredients used

02:06:53.539 --> 02:06:58.444
in the three-drug cocktail
for lethal injections.

02:06:58.444 --> 02:07:02.281
Too much potassium chloride
will cause irregular heartbeats,

02:07:02.281 --> 02:07:03.882
and, boom, your heart will stop.

02:07:03.882 --> 02:07:07.419
So if you've been thinking
of doing a Lay's mukbang,

02:07:07.419 --> 02:07:08.621
be careful.

02:07:08.621 --> 02:07:10.289
We don't have any of that in the US Lay's,

02:07:10.289 --> 02:07:11.991
but we do have food coloring,

02:07:11.991 --> 02:07:16.829
caramel color in our barbecue
and honey-barbecue chips.

02:07:16.829 --> 02:07:18.964
Certain types of caramel
color can contain a byproduct

02:07:18.964 --> 02:07:22.601
called 4-meI.

02:07:22.601 --> 02:07:25.304
Studies found that it caused
cancer in rats and mice,

02:07:25.304 --> 02:07:28.807
leading campaigns in support
of banning it from foods.

02:07:28.807 --> 02:07:30.509
Give me that dancing rat!

02:07:31.744 --> 02:07:34.213
All right. The FDA was
like, "Meh, it's fine.

02:07:34.213 --> 02:07:36.515
Humans don't come close
to the level of exposure

02:07:36.515 --> 02:07:38.050
that caused the rat tumors."

02:07:38.050 --> 02:07:40.452
But that didn't stop
the state of California

02:07:40.452 --> 02:07:43.789
adding it to its Proposition
65 list of chemicals, quote,

02:07:43.789 --> 02:07:47.259
"known to the state of
California to cause cancer

02:07:47.259 --> 02:07:50.562
or reproductive toxicity," end quote. Oof.

02:07:50.562 --> 02:07:52.464
Another ingredient found
in several varieties

02:07:52.464 --> 02:07:55.768
of Lay's chips here in
India is disodium glutamate,

02:07:55.768 --> 02:07:59.371
aka flavor enhancer 69.

02:07:59.371 --> 02:08:01.440
No, not 69.

02:08:01.440 --> 02:08:03.909
Flavor enhancer 627.

02:08:03.909 --> 02:08:06.612
But basically, it's used alongside MSG

02:08:06.612 --> 02:08:09.148
to enhance the flavor of the chips.

02:08:09.148 --> 02:08:10.849
Both the Food and Drug Administration,

02:08:10.849 --> 02:08:12.518
or the FDA, in the United States,

02:08:12.518 --> 02:08:15.888
and the European Food Safety
Authority, or the EFSA,

02:08:15.888 --> 02:08:18.590
consider disodium glutamate safe.

02:08:18.590 --> 02:08:21.093
But it's not recommended
for babies, children,

02:08:21.093 --> 02:08:22.861
pregnant women, and lactating mothers,

02:08:22.861 --> 02:08:24.930
and also should be avoided by asthmatics

02:08:24.930 --> 02:08:26.965
or people suffering from gout.

02:08:26.965 --> 02:08:27.800
MSG, if you're wondering,

02:08:27.800 --> 02:08:30.135
is the commonly misunderstood ingredient

02:08:30.135 --> 02:08:31.804
known as monosodium glutamate

02:08:31.804 --> 02:08:33.472
which is added to a lot of Asian cuisine

02:08:33.472 --> 02:08:35.841
and gives it that umami flavor.

02:08:35.841 --> 02:08:39.078
In 2019, Lay's sued a
bunch of Indian farmers

02:08:39.078 --> 02:08:43.215
for growing a certain variety
of potato, FC5 variety,

02:08:43.215 --> 02:08:46.452
saying it has a patent on that variety.

02:08:46.452 --> 02:08:48.754
This type of potato is
ideal for snack chips,

02:08:48.754 --> 02:08:51.256
as it has a lower moisture content.

02:08:51.256 --> 02:08:53.325
But strike one up for the little guy.

02:08:53.325 --> 02:08:55.227
Farmers'-rights activists
petitioned to the

02:08:55.227 --> 02:08:58.831
Protection of Plant Varieties
and Farmers' Rights Authority,

02:08:58.831 --> 02:08:59.832
and it agreed.

02:08:59.832 --> 02:09:04.470
PepsiCo, Lay's, cannot claim
a patent over a seed variety.

02:09:04.470 --> 02:09:05.904
It was revoked immediately,

02:09:05.904 --> 02:09:08.240
and the Indian potato
farmers are now flush

02:09:08.240 --> 02:09:10.743
with low-moisture-potato money.

02:09:10.743 --> 02:09:13.278
Let's go!

02:09:15.781 --> 02:09:18.183
So, which country has
the unhealthiest chips?

02:09:18.183 --> 02:09:20.385
Let's compare the classics first.

02:09:20.385 --> 02:09:23.722
A 28-gram bag of classic Lay's in the US

02:09:23.722 --> 02:09:27.593
contains 160 calories,
10 grams of total fat,

02:09:27.593 --> 02:09:30.763
1.5 grams of saturated
fat, 15 grams of carbs,

02:09:30.763 --> 02:09:33.232
and 170 milligrams of sodium.

02:09:33.232 --> 02:09:35.901
OK, so our Lay's nutrition
is per 100 grams.

02:09:35.901 --> 02:09:37.102
So I did a little bit of math

02:09:37.102 --> 02:09:39.338
to compare it to the US 28 grams.

02:09:39.338 --> 02:09:40.305
Actually, Joe did the math.

02:09:40.305 --> 02:09:42.040
So if the math is wrong, blame Joe.

02:09:42.040 --> 02:09:44.977
OK, so we have 154.8 calories,

02:09:44.977 --> 02:09:46.812
total fat, 9.8 grams,

02:09:46.812 --> 02:09:49.581
of which saturates are 3.7 grams,

02:09:49.581 --> 02:09:51.183
carbs are 14.7 grams,

02:09:51.183 --> 02:09:54.686
and sodium, 142.8 milligrams.

02:09:54.686 --> 02:09:56.355
Wow, that was pretty close, actually.

02:09:56.355 --> 02:09:57.956
We're under the US in every metric

02:09:57.956 --> 02:10:02.594
except for saturated fats,
where we are over 164%.

02:10:02.594 --> 02:10:05.230
And I think that's because
we use palm-olein oil

02:10:05.230 --> 02:10:08.534
to fry our chips, and it's
very high in saturated fats,

02:10:08.534 --> 02:10:11.069
unlike the US vegetable oil.

02:10:11.069 --> 02:10:13.772
What about the least-healthiest
chip in each country?

02:10:13.772 --> 02:10:15.774
Over here, there are a lot of them

02:10:15.774 --> 02:10:19.878
that are tied to 160
calories per 28-gram bag.

02:10:19.878 --> 02:10:21.513
Show list.

02:10:21.513 --> 02:10:24.716
But we did find that the 160-calorie chips

02:10:24.716 --> 02:10:27.252
with the highest fat content are these.

02:10:27.252 --> 02:10:28.754
No!

02:10:28.754 --> 02:10:31.423
The cheddar and sour
cream, I love these guys.

02:10:31.423 --> 02:10:34.026
Making them the least healthy.

02:10:34.026 --> 02:10:35.894
If I did have a bag that small,

02:10:35.894 --> 02:10:38.497
it would contain all of this.

02:10:38.497 --> 02:10:42.067
And here in India, our
highest-calorific chip is

02:10:42.067 --> 02:10:43.468
classic salted.

02:10:43.468 --> 02:10:44.303
How lame.

02:10:44.303 --> 02:10:47.339
How is this the most calorific
chip we sell here, Lay's?

02:10:47.339 --> 02:10:48.574
If I had to run an extra mile,

02:10:48.574 --> 02:10:50.609
it wouldn't be for classic salted.

02:10:50.609 --> 02:10:53.312
So you know what the next
most-calorific chip is?

02:10:54.379 --> 02:10:56.081
Magic masala, baby.

02:10:56.081 --> 02:10:57.216
Blue Lay's.

02:10:57.216 --> 02:10:58.717
We had to end with this one.

02:10:58.717 --> 02:10:59.852
Super calorific.

02:10:59.852 --> 02:11:02.554
I don't know why I'm
proud of that, but good.

02:11:02.554 --> 02:11:05.457
Great to know that this
is and forever will be

02:11:05.457 --> 02:11:07.526
the maharaja of Lay's.

02:11:07.893 --> 02:11:09.294
Nikhil: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

02:11:09.294 --> 02:11:10.796
we wanted to find out all the differences

02:11:10.796 --> 02:11:13.232
between Taco Bell in India and the US.

02:11:13.232 --> 02:11:15.634
This is "Food Wars."

02:11:19.071 --> 02:11:22.207
Here in India, our typical
tacos come in orders of one;

02:11:22.207 --> 02:11:25.410
two, in a two-taco meal
with fries and a drink;

02:11:25.410 --> 02:11:27.379
three, taco-trio combo,

02:11:27.379 --> 02:11:29.982
which comes with nachos and a drink;

02:11:29.982 --> 02:11:32.885
or, on weekends, they have a special offer

02:11:32.885 --> 02:11:35.354
where you can get eight tacos

02:11:35.354 --> 02:11:39.858
in their weekend taco party extravaga --

02:11:39.858 --> 02:11:41.193
what's it called?

02:11:41.193 --> 02:11:43.662
Taco, taco, t --

02:11:43.662 --> 02:11:46.398
Eight weekend party pack taco ...

02:11:47.332 --> 02:11:50.068
Eight-taco weekend party pack!

02:11:50.068 --> 02:11:51.603
Have a party with your friends.

02:11:51.603 --> 02:11:53.138
Only if there are eight of them

02:11:53.138 --> 02:11:55.440
and they all are OK with
having just one taco.

02:11:55.440 --> 02:11:57.943
In the US, our standard Taco Bell tacos

02:11:57.943 --> 02:11:59.444
come in orders of one,

02:11:59.444 --> 02:12:00.779
three with a drink,

02:12:00.779 --> 02:12:03.382
and the 12-taco box.

02:12:03.382 --> 02:12:05.183
12 tacos, one box.

02:12:05.183 --> 02:12:06.018
How you doing?

02:12:06.018 --> 02:12:09.087
Here in India, our classic
burrito is 16.5 centimeters,

02:12:09.087 --> 02:12:10.622
or 6.5 inches.

02:12:10.622 --> 02:12:14.026
Our US burrito is 5 inches across.

02:12:14.026 --> 02:12:16.428
In terms of girth -- this is
the first time I've measured

02:12:16.428 --> 02:12:18.130
the girth of anything, promise.

02:12:18.130 --> 02:12:19.131
7 inches.

02:12:19.131 --> 02:12:20.365
Joe: Also about 5 inches.

02:12:20.365 --> 02:12:22.000
And that's what matters most.

02:12:22.000 --> 02:12:25.203
OK, now to measure the weight
of our classic burrito.

02:12:25.203 --> 02:12:26.038
Damn!

02:12:26.038 --> 02:12:27.172
This is a big boy.

02:12:27.172 --> 02:12:29.241
291 grams.

02:12:29.241 --> 02:12:31.843
Joe: 185 grams.

02:12:31.843 --> 02:12:35.948
Our classic quesadilla
is just shy of 11 inches.

02:12:35.948 --> 02:12:36.815
Joe: 10 inches.

02:12:36.815 --> 02:12:39.651
And as for weight, boop, boop, boop, boop.

02:12:39.651 --> 02:12:41.920
And it weighs 174 grams.

02:12:41.920 --> 02:12:44.122
Joe: 202 grams.

02:12:44.122 --> 02:12:47.159
At an Indian Taco Bell, the
largest item we have on our menu

02:12:47.159 --> 02:12:50.996
is the aforementioned
weekend eight-taco party

02:12:50.996 --> 02:12:54.232
picnic popping what
the f--- is this thing?

02:12:54.232 --> 02:12:57.736
Eight-taco weekend party
pack, and it's always a party.

02:12:59.237 --> 02:13:01.506
So, the vegetarian version is 499 rupees,

02:13:01.506 --> 02:13:04.643
and the non-vegetarian
version is 599 rupees.

02:13:04.643 --> 02:13:06.578
In the US, our biggest menu item

02:13:06.578 --> 02:13:10.215
is the supreme variety taco party pack.

02:13:10.215 --> 02:13:14.753
It is 12 supreme tacos,
and it runs $21.99,

02:13:14.753 --> 02:13:18.857
or 1,751.65 Indian rupee.

02:13:20.092 --> 02:13:22.361
Here's everything you'll
find at a Taco Bell in India

02:13:22.361 --> 02:13:24.162
that you will not find in the US.

02:13:24.162 --> 02:13:26.965
And here is everything at a US Taco Bell

02:13:26.965 --> 02:13:29.067
you can't find in India.

02:13:29.067 --> 02:13:30.836
Let's taco about it.

02:13:30.836 --> 02:13:34.039
Here in India, all of the
tacos have a vegetarian option.

02:13:34.039 --> 02:13:36.041
It's because even though
India is a primarily

02:13:36.041 --> 02:13:37.442
non-vegetarian country,

02:13:37.442 --> 02:13:39.544
we have a huge population of vegetarians

02:13:39.544 --> 02:13:42.047
or people who have different preferences

02:13:42.047 --> 02:13:43.849
of what kind of meat they like to eat.

02:13:43.849 --> 02:13:45.884
And so it's great for most
of these fast-food chains

02:13:45.884 --> 02:13:47.753
to have a lot of veg options.

02:13:47.753 --> 02:13:50.522
All of them have the option
of either pinto beans,

02:13:50.522 --> 02:13:53.759
fajita veggies, or Mexican paneer,

02:13:53.759 --> 02:13:56.962
and they're also in
increasing order of spice.

02:13:56.962 --> 02:13:59.231
The cheesy double-decker taco.

02:13:59.231 --> 02:14:01.400
Honestly, I actually
really like this taco.

02:14:01.400 --> 02:14:02.901
I know it's sacrilege for some people

02:14:02.901 --> 02:14:05.504
to eat a soft-shell and a
hard-shell taco together,

02:14:05.504 --> 02:14:08.840
but when you parcel this stuff
and get it delivered to you,

02:14:08.840 --> 02:14:11.009
both the tacos become soft shell.

02:14:12.778 --> 02:14:13.612
Really yum.

02:14:13.612 --> 02:14:16.681
All right, the next taco I'm
going to eat is a crunchy taco,

02:14:16.681 --> 02:14:19.284
plain and simple. It's
got pinto beans in it.

02:14:19.284 --> 02:14:22.154
[sighs] It's unfair to
dis on a crunchy taco

02:14:22.154 --> 02:14:24.689
after you've ordered it from
a restaurant that's far away,

02:14:24.689 --> 02:14:26.758
because look at this.
It's become soggy already.

02:14:26.758 --> 02:14:29.394
So I'm going to be gentle
on my criticism of this.

02:14:29.394 --> 02:14:32.297
But you, you soft-shell
tacos are getting it, huh?

02:14:33.331 --> 02:14:35.033
There's still some decent crunch to it.

02:14:35.033 --> 02:14:38.036
Here in India, pinto beans
are what we call rajma,

02:14:38.036 --> 02:14:39.371
and they're a staple.

02:14:39.371 --> 02:14:40.939
We f---ing love our rajma.

02:14:40.939 --> 02:14:43.542
So it's a perfect match
to put them in a taco.

02:14:43.542 --> 02:14:45.010
Next up, another crunchy taco.

02:14:45.010 --> 02:14:47.712
This one is the Mexican paneer.

02:14:47.712 --> 02:14:50.382
Now, paneer, if you're
unaware, is cottage cheese.

02:14:50.382 --> 02:14:52.050
We make it all over here in India.

02:14:52.050 --> 02:14:53.285
We basically curdle milk,

02:14:53.285 --> 02:14:56.721
add some sort of fruit
or vegetable acid to it,

02:14:56.721 --> 02:14:57.722
like lemon juice,

02:14:57.722 --> 02:14:59.691
and you get cottage
cheese, which is paneer.

02:14:59.691 --> 02:15:03.028
I'm curious to know
what makes this Mexican.

02:15:03.995 --> 02:15:05.997
Paneer is one of the most
popular things you'll find

02:15:05.997 --> 02:15:07.499
in India at any restaurant.

02:15:07.499 --> 02:15:09.568
This paneer tastes chalky,

02:15:09.568 --> 02:15:11.236
like most processed paneer

02:15:11.236 --> 02:15:12.537
that you'd store in a freezer would.

02:15:12.537 --> 02:15:15.173
If you prefer your paneer chunky,

02:15:15.173 --> 02:15:16.274
you might enjoy this.

02:15:16.274 --> 02:15:17.142
Me, not so much.

02:15:17.142 --> 02:15:19.978
Now on to the soft-shell tacos.

02:15:19.978 --> 02:15:23.415
This one is Mexican paneer,
the same thing I just had.

02:15:23.415 --> 02:15:26.151
This Mexican paneer is
a little bit more spicy.

02:15:26.151 --> 02:15:27.719
My favorite thing about tacos is that

02:15:27.719 --> 02:15:30.522
not every bite is uniform,
so you get a lot of

02:15:30.522 --> 02:15:32.824
different textures and
flavors in each bite you take,

02:15:32.824 --> 02:15:34.826
and I guess that's proving
its point over here.

02:15:34.826 --> 02:15:36.128
OK, so the next one we're going to try

02:15:36.128 --> 02:15:38.964
is a soft taco with fajita veggies inside.

02:15:39.831 --> 02:15:41.700
I'm opting out of the fajita veggies

02:15:41.700 --> 02:15:43.034
as a filling in general.

02:15:43.034 --> 02:15:45.070
And finally we have
our last veggie option,

02:15:45.070 --> 02:15:49.741
which is a veggie fiesta,
which has tater tots.

02:15:50.809 --> 02:15:51.910
Win. That's a win.

02:15:51.910 --> 02:15:53.311
If I was going to Taco Bell

02:15:53.311 --> 02:15:55.280
and had to order a veggie
taco for some reason,

02:15:55.280 --> 02:15:58.383
my option would be a
crunchy pinto bean taco.

02:15:58.383 --> 02:16:00.118
And now for our non-vegetarian tacos.

02:16:00.118 --> 02:16:02.387
Please note that all of
the meat in our tacos

02:16:02.387 --> 02:16:03.655
is chicken and not beef.

02:16:03.655 --> 02:16:06.158
This is because we have a
huge percentage of Hindus

02:16:06.158 --> 02:16:08.426
here in India, and they do not eat beef.

02:16:08.426 --> 02:16:11.663
This makes all of our
non-veg tacos exclusives!

02:16:11.663 --> 02:16:12.898
Because, yes, in the US

02:16:12.898 --> 02:16:15.100
you can substitute your beef for chicken,

02:16:15.100 --> 02:16:17.002
but it's not on the
official menu, all right?

02:16:17.002 --> 02:16:18.370
It's a modification,

02:16:18.370 --> 02:16:21.540
which means these are
more exclusives to India.

02:16:21.540 --> 02:16:23.008
OK, so you have two options of filling,

02:16:23.008 --> 02:16:25.677
either Mexican chicken or grilled chicken.

02:16:25.677 --> 02:16:28.980
We're starting off with a
grilled-chicken crunchy taco,

02:16:28.980 --> 02:16:31.816
which has severely disintegrated.

02:16:31.816 --> 02:16:33.585
Not bad. This is also kind of the test

02:16:33.585 --> 02:16:36.288
of Taco Bell's structural integrity.

02:16:36.288 --> 02:16:37.122
Pretty good.

02:16:39.257 --> 02:16:41.526
That's a win from me. What
else do you want, Taco Bell?

02:16:41.526 --> 02:16:44.429
This taco, though, has seen better times.

02:16:45.363 --> 02:16:48.166
It kind of reminds me of a rajma chawal.

02:16:48.166 --> 02:16:49.834
And when you're chewing on a rajma chawal,

02:16:49.834 --> 02:16:51.469
that's how soft the chicken is.

02:16:51.469 --> 02:16:53.038
There are a lot of
comparisons you can make

02:16:53.038 --> 02:16:54.739
with Mexican and Indian food.

02:16:54.739 --> 02:16:56.775
We have something exactly
like this in India.

02:16:56.775 --> 02:16:59.010
It's called a chapati, and
it's made out of wheat.

02:16:59.010 --> 02:17:01.479
The tortillas in Mexico are
typically made with corn.

02:17:01.479 --> 02:17:03.248
The one in Taco Bell is made out of maida,

02:17:03.248 --> 02:17:04.583
which is all-purpose flour.

02:17:04.583 --> 02:17:05.917
I can't speak for Mexican cuisine,

02:17:05.917 --> 02:17:08.687
but there's definitely a lot
of Indian flavors in this.

02:17:09.688 --> 02:17:12.257
This is actually a soft
grilled-chicken taco,

02:17:12.257 --> 02:17:14.659
and I can wholeheartedly
say worst of the bunch.

02:17:14.659 --> 02:17:15.594
Don't get this one.

02:17:15.594 --> 02:17:19.764
A cheese double-decker taco
with grilled chicken again.

02:17:19.764 --> 02:17:21.600
Come on, man. I wanted the Mexican one.

02:17:21.600 --> 02:17:22.801
But the hard-shell taco

02:17:22.801 --> 02:17:25.337
is disintegrating into a soft-shell taco.

02:17:26.438 --> 02:17:27.439
It's nothing special.

02:17:27.439 --> 02:17:29.140
Chicken fiesta taco.

02:17:29.140 --> 02:17:31.109
Oh, my God!

02:17:31.109 --> 02:17:32.477
I didn't expect that at all.

02:17:35.680 --> 02:17:38.183
I've just been chewing
for so long. I'm so tired.

02:17:38.183 --> 02:17:40.986
Oh, damn. The aftertaste
of this is really good.

02:17:40.986 --> 02:17:42.354
There's a lot of nice spice to it.

02:17:42.354 --> 02:17:44.189
Now we have a very special taco.

02:17:44.189 --> 02:17:45.724
As you can see, this one is still wrapped,

02:17:45.724 --> 02:17:47.392
because I've never seen this in my life.

02:17:47.392 --> 02:17:49.661
It's called a naked chicken taco.

02:17:49.661 --> 02:17:50.829
Pause for a moment.

02:17:50.829 --> 02:17:52.330
What do you think that means?

02:17:52.330 --> 02:17:53.632
Oh,

02:17:53.632 --> 02:17:54.833
my

02:17:54.833 --> 02:17:55.734
God.

02:17:55.734 --> 02:17:57.602
Ladies and gentlemen,

02:17:57.602 --> 02:17:59.404
the naked chicken taco.

02:17:59.404 --> 02:18:02.874
Crew: Whoo! [applauding]

02:18:02.874 --> 02:18:05.010
Genuinely feels like
I just undressed food.

02:18:05.010 --> 02:18:07.245
So, there's no chicken filling inside it

02:18:07.245 --> 02:18:09.748
because the chicken is the taco!

02:18:09.748 --> 02:18:12.817
That's right. That's how far
we have come as the human race.

02:18:12.817 --> 02:18:15.420
We have taken this bird and
turned it into a freaking

02:18:15.420 --> 02:18:18.223
pancake and folded it over cheese!

02:18:18.223 --> 02:18:20.392
Your scientists were too
busy trying to figure out

02:18:20.392 --> 02:18:21.559
whether they could do it.

02:18:21.559 --> 02:18:23.595
They didn't stop to think
whether they should do it.

02:18:28.833 --> 02:18:30.869
I think that might be one
of the worst things I've had

02:18:30.869 --> 02:18:31.770
on this show.

02:18:31.770 --> 02:18:34.439
Oh, God. Oh, God.

02:18:34.439 --> 02:18:36.007
I'm gonna be honest, it actually
looks pretty good to me.

02:18:36.007 --> 02:18:37.776
That reminds me of the KFC double down,

02:18:37.776 --> 02:18:40.078
which I did actually enjoy. I'd try it.

02:18:40.078 --> 02:18:42.547
Starting off, soft taco
and soft Taco Supreme,

02:18:42.547 --> 02:18:43.882
which is beef.

02:18:43.882 --> 02:18:45.317
Flimsiest thing in the world.

02:18:45.317 --> 02:18:46.318
Ew!

02:18:46.318 --> 02:18:49.754
This stuff is, oh, this stuff
is sweating already. Ugh.

02:18:49.754 --> 02:18:52.424
So, I don't know how many
vegetarians are watching now,

02:18:52.424 --> 02:18:54.392
but ... look at what you're missing?

02:18:54.392 --> 02:18:56.261
I think I just created a few vegetarians.

02:18:56.261 --> 02:18:57.729
I mean, I like how they taste,

02:18:57.729 --> 02:19:00.231
but, I mean, Taco Bell's got
so much fun stuff on the menu.

02:19:00.231 --> 02:19:01.766
What are you doing eating regular tacos?

02:19:01.766 --> 02:19:02.634
Like, get out of here.

02:19:02.634 --> 02:19:05.170
Crunchy taco, which we saw earlier.

02:19:05.170 --> 02:19:06.171
Fantastic.

02:19:06.171 --> 02:19:07.439
A little more stuff in it,

02:19:07.439 --> 02:19:09.274
the beef Supreme Taco.

02:19:09.274 --> 02:19:10.642
They really load it up with the veggies.

02:19:10.642 --> 02:19:12.410
India. India. India!

02:19:12.410 --> 02:19:13.244
Look at me.

02:19:13.244 --> 02:19:14.846
This is my favorite thing
in the Taco Bell menu.

02:19:14.846 --> 02:19:17.382
I sing its praises at every
Taco Bell "Food Wars."

02:19:17.382 --> 02:19:20.952
It is the nacho cheese
Doritos locos tacos.

02:19:20.952 --> 02:19:25.023
Some genius somewhere
connected Taco Bell and Doritos

02:19:25.023 --> 02:19:29.294
to make a hard-shell taco that
is, in fact, a Doritos shell.

02:19:30.962 --> 02:19:31.796
Mm.

02:19:31.796 --> 02:19:34.566
Comes in standard and, of course, supreme.

02:19:35.734 --> 02:19:37.268
This, I've been looking
forward to this all day.

02:19:37.268 --> 02:19:39.471
It's burrito time, baby!

02:19:39.471 --> 02:19:42.040
I've gotten a Mexican paneer version here

02:19:42.040 --> 02:19:44.709
as well as a pinto beans version.

02:19:44.709 --> 02:19:46.544
I think I'll go with the pinto beans one.

02:19:46.544 --> 02:19:49.481
By the way, this tray is all
of the vegetarian burritos,

02:19:49.481 --> 02:19:51.583
and this is the non-vegetarian tray.

02:19:51.583 --> 02:19:52.484
Happy baby.

02:19:52.484 --> 02:19:54.419
India has a lot of roll culture.

02:19:54.419 --> 02:19:57.288
We have kati rolls, we have Kolkata rolls,

02:19:57.288 --> 02:20:00.392
we also have shawarmas,
which we are a huge fan of.

02:20:01.726 --> 02:20:04.496
Most Indians, this
basically will feel like

02:20:04.496 --> 02:20:08.099
you took rajma rice and you
shoved it inside a maida roti.

02:20:08.099 --> 02:20:09.934
I think I'd go with a taco over this.

02:20:09.934 --> 02:20:12.303
Next up, we have tikka masala.

02:20:12.303 --> 02:20:13.938
But, I found this out recently,

02:20:13.938 --> 02:20:16.141
it was actually invented by the British.

02:20:16.141 --> 02:20:19.677
So, clearly inspired by
India, but invented by them.

02:20:19.677 --> 02:20:21.179
Another thing that the
British took from us

02:20:21.179 --> 02:20:22.981
that we haven't been paid back for.

02:20:24.149 --> 02:20:26.818
We have a flavor here
which is called achari,

02:20:26.818 --> 02:20:28.386
and it's basically like a pickle.

02:20:28.386 --> 02:20:31.623
This is more achari than
chicken-tikka-masala-y.

02:20:31.623 --> 02:20:34.292
Also, I would be lying if I
didn't admit that, Taco Bell,

02:20:34.292 --> 02:20:37.362
it's already doing its thing
to my digestive system.

02:20:37.362 --> 02:20:40.198
Taco Bell is notorious for
making you go to the bathroom.

02:20:40.198 --> 02:20:42.434
Zoom in to my stomach
right now and just listen

02:20:42.434 --> 02:20:45.403
to the noises, and
let's get a translation.

02:20:45.403 --> 02:20:48.239
[farting]
♪ Oh, my God ♪

02:20:48.239 --> 02:20:51.443
And now for Sriracha veg burrito.

02:20:51.443 --> 02:20:52.410
It's now running the risk

02:20:52.410 --> 02:20:54.412
of offending three different cultures.

02:20:54.412 --> 02:20:57.182
I don't normally eat a
burrito by ripping it in half.

02:20:57.182 --> 02:20:58.783
Actually, that sounds awesome.

02:20:58.783 --> 02:21:00.718
We should do that more often.
Like, a double-handed --

02:21:00.718 --> 02:21:02.287
don't clip that.

02:21:02.287 --> 02:21:03.555
Hm. You can skip it.

02:21:03.555 --> 02:21:05.990
We have the seven-layer burrito.

02:21:07.025 --> 02:21:09.828
This one tastes like all
of these put together.

02:21:09.828 --> 02:21:11.629
And we have one last veg wrap.

02:21:11.629 --> 02:21:13.832
Ah, guys, I can't do this.

02:21:13.832 --> 02:21:15.200
It's the same thing!

02:21:15.200 --> 02:21:17.502
It's just tater tots, that same filling.

02:21:17.502 --> 02:21:19.304
I bow down in defeat, Taco Bell.

02:21:19.304 --> 02:21:20.638
You have vanquished me.

02:21:20.638 --> 02:21:22.640
Moving on to the non-vegetarian burritos,

02:21:22.640 --> 02:21:24.709
and we're hoping some of these

02:21:24.709 --> 02:21:27.078
are a little more
distinct from the others.

02:21:27.078 --> 02:21:29.714
All right, we have a classic
Mexican chicken burrito.

02:21:31.449 --> 02:21:32.517
This is so bad.

02:21:32.517 --> 02:21:33.485
This is damn bad.

02:21:33.485 --> 02:21:35.320
Let's just say I'm glad
you didn't call yourself

02:21:35.320 --> 02:21:36.387
burrito bowl.

02:21:36.387 --> 02:21:39.524
Next up, tikka masala, but now in non-veg.

02:21:39.524 --> 02:21:42.260
["Piano Man" harmonica playing]

02:21:43.361 --> 02:21:44.662
This is actually quite good!

02:21:44.662 --> 02:21:47.699
This one doesn't taste as dry
as the other ones I've had.

02:21:47.699 --> 02:21:50.568
And, of course, we have the seven-layer

02:21:50.568 --> 02:21:52.103
non-vegetarian burrito.

02:21:52.103 --> 02:21:54.639
Instead of paneer, we
have grilled chicken.

02:21:54.639 --> 02:21:56.107
Let's just do the slap test again.

02:21:57.408 --> 02:21:58.243
Oof.

02:21:58.243 --> 02:21:59.544
Yeah, you could really hurt somebody

02:21:59.544 --> 02:22:00.545
with the seven-layer one.

02:22:00.545 --> 02:22:02.547
OK, we have one last burrito, which is --

02:22:02.547 --> 02:22:04.249
wait, what is this?

02:22:04.249 --> 02:22:06.718
This is not -- why have you done this?

02:22:06.718 --> 02:22:09.120
This burrito looks like the love child

02:22:09.120 --> 02:22:10.989
of all other burritos over here.

02:22:10.989 --> 02:22:13.591
These burritos are definitely
related, and this is

02:22:13.591 --> 02:22:15.126
the product of incest.
[baby cries]

02:22:16.394 --> 02:22:17.629
Wow, it's actually not that bad.

02:22:17.629 --> 02:22:18.796
Honestly, out of all of these,

02:22:18.796 --> 02:22:22.534
I'd prefer to finish this one
because it's just smaller.

02:22:22.534 --> 02:22:24.302
The pain will end faster.

02:22:24.302 --> 02:22:25.370
Burritos.

02:22:25.370 --> 02:22:27.539
Might not be visually the most exciting

02:22:27.539 --> 02:22:30.108
part of the video, but please don't leave.

02:22:30.108 --> 02:22:32.844
Maybe just open some clips
of "Family Guy" next to it,

02:22:32.844 --> 02:22:34.979
so you can watch that and
this like you're on TikTok.

02:22:34.979 --> 02:22:37.949
The double steak grilled cheese burrito

02:22:37.949 --> 02:22:42.153
and the spicy double steak
grilled cheese burrito.

02:22:42.153 --> 02:22:43.821
And, right, it's grilled
cheese 'cause they

02:22:43.821 --> 02:22:45.490
grill it shut with cheese.

02:22:45.490 --> 02:22:46.324
Genius idea.

02:22:46.324 --> 02:22:48.259
Yeah! Look at that, it
has jalapeños on it.

02:22:48.259 --> 02:22:49.193
Oh, that's fantastic.

02:22:49.193 --> 02:22:51.162
That's a really great idea.

02:22:51.162 --> 02:22:52.931
Oh. Yeah, this rules.

02:22:52.931 --> 02:22:54.365
A beefy quesarito.

02:22:54.365 --> 02:22:55.800
When these things cool off, though,

02:22:55.800 --> 02:22:57.035
it's just a lot of cheese in there.

02:22:57.035 --> 02:22:58.202
Oh, and it has rice in it.

02:22:58.202 --> 02:22:59.037
Well, burritos have rice,

02:22:59.037 --> 02:23:00.104
I don't know why I'm so surprised by that.

02:23:00.104 --> 02:23:01.339
Rice in a burrito?!

02:23:01.339 --> 02:23:03.675
Same thing but with black beans.

02:23:03.675 --> 02:23:06.110
I mean, it's already kind of
dripping out there already.

02:23:06.110 --> 02:23:08.947
Grilled No. 1, beans and
cheese in there, you see that?

02:23:08.947 --> 02:23:10.682
And the red is those chips.

02:23:10.682 --> 02:23:11.849
They put those crispy chips in there.

02:23:11.849 --> 02:23:12.984
Five-layer burrito.

02:23:12.984 --> 02:23:14.018
It used to be seven-layer.

02:23:14.018 --> 02:23:16.154
Took out two layers and added a beefy one

02:23:16.154 --> 02:23:17.188
for some weird reason.

02:23:17.188 --> 02:23:19.891
I assure you there's five
layers and beef inside this.

02:23:19.891 --> 02:23:21.492
No, I'm not doing that. I'm not

02:23:21.492 --> 02:23:23.695
some weird fetish that on the internet

02:23:23.695 --> 02:23:26.698
that I'm not aware of,
slapping faces with burritos.

02:23:26.698 --> 02:23:27.599
Burrito Supreme.

02:23:27.599 --> 02:23:28.499
Look, it's so much different

02:23:28.499 --> 02:23:30.068
from the last thing we
were just looking at.

02:23:30.068 --> 02:23:31.536
But that one's just like ...

02:23:32.637 --> 02:23:33.905
"CK," Chipotle chicken.

02:23:34.906 --> 02:23:36.107
Yeah, chipotle mayo's legit.

02:23:36.107 --> 02:23:37.642
I got an extra one, if anyone wants it.

02:23:37.642 --> 02:23:39.711
Go ahead and comment below,
and I'll mail it to you.

02:23:39.711 --> 02:23:40.778
Beefy melt.

02:23:40.778 --> 02:23:42.347
Beef and melted cheese.

02:23:42.347 --> 02:23:43.348
I can't believe it!

02:23:43.348 --> 02:23:44.616
Together at last!

02:23:45.617 --> 02:23:47.118
I mean, it tastes like all the other ones.

02:23:47.118 --> 02:23:49.253
Feel like we could pare
this menu down a little bit.

02:23:49.253 --> 02:23:51.689
Last and not least, cheesy bean and rice.

02:23:51.689 --> 02:23:54.225
Now for India's specialities.

02:23:54.225 --> 02:23:56.527
I am excited for the diversity.

02:23:56.527 --> 02:23:57.528
That's all I'll say.

02:23:57.528 --> 02:23:59.564
Very representative of our country.

02:23:59.564 --> 02:24:01.432
Let's start off with the chalupa.

02:24:01.432 --> 02:24:02.667
The humble chalupa

02:24:03.668 --> 02:24:04.535
is nice.

02:24:04.535 --> 02:24:05.703
If you guys are at home wondering

02:24:05.703 --> 02:24:08.706
what the difference between a
normal taco and a chalupa is,

02:24:08.706 --> 02:24:09.540
you should Google it.

02:24:09.540 --> 02:24:11.309
What is this, an education show?

02:24:11.309 --> 02:24:12.477
I'm just here to eat, man.

02:24:12.477 --> 02:24:14.178
For my Indian brethren,
it's kind of the difference

02:24:14.178 --> 02:24:16.247
between a chapati and a patuda.

02:24:16.247 --> 02:24:17.515
They actually fry it a little bit.

02:24:18.383 --> 02:24:20.018
Mm, mm, mm!

02:24:20.018 --> 02:24:22.053
But that was a very
horrible place to bite,

02:24:22.053 --> 02:24:23.354
because I only got chicken.

02:24:23.354 --> 02:24:26.324
I have a soft spot for the
chalupa, and it gets my approval.

02:24:26.324 --> 02:24:28.126
We have the vegstar wrap.

02:24:28.126 --> 02:24:29.027
Voilà.

02:24:29.027 --> 02:24:31.696
So inventive. Let's take a
burrito but make it flat.

02:24:31.696 --> 02:24:32.664
Oh, wow.

02:24:32.664 --> 02:24:35.233
Don't make me eat this, Insider, please.

02:24:36.834 --> 02:24:37.835
Ugh!

02:24:37.835 --> 02:24:40.738
I'm coming from a country
where we're used to eating

02:24:40.738 --> 02:24:44.142
something like this, a chapati,
with a sabzi on the side,

02:24:44.142 --> 02:24:46.077
which is a curry which has vegetables

02:24:46.077 --> 02:24:48.546
and fresh paneer and maybe some chicken.

02:24:48.546 --> 02:24:51.749
So to eat something like this
just feels not even subpar,

02:24:51.749 --> 02:24:52.984
it just feels wrong.

02:24:52.984 --> 02:24:54.152
I'm actually curious to know

02:24:54.152 --> 02:24:56.120
if any Mexicans watching this video

02:24:56.120 --> 02:24:57.121
can let me know in the comments

02:24:57.121 --> 02:25:00.491
whether you feel like
Taco Bell has done justice

02:25:00.491 --> 02:25:02.694
to representing your cuisine in any way.

02:25:02.694 --> 02:25:04.896
Next up, we have a chickstar.

02:25:04.896 --> 02:25:06.164
Round of applause.
[crickets chirping]

02:25:06.164 --> 02:25:07.198
I'm just going to keep this

02:25:07.198 --> 02:25:11.536
UFO of man's worst
accomplishment over here.

02:25:11.536 --> 02:25:13.371
Quesadilla, fajita veg.

02:25:13.371 --> 02:25:14.205
Very thin.

02:25:14.205 --> 02:25:15.740
Curious to know how they have fit

02:25:15.740 --> 02:25:17.675
a lot of fajita veggies into it.

02:25:18.643 --> 02:25:19.477
They haven't.

02:25:19.477 --> 02:25:20.311
How do people do this?

02:25:20.311 --> 02:25:23.114
My God. I just realized,

02:25:23.114 --> 02:25:24.449
Joe is insane.

02:25:24.449 --> 02:25:26.384
How have you eaten so much Taco Bell, Joe?

02:25:26.384 --> 02:25:27.685
Yeah, I'm insane.

02:25:27.685 --> 02:25:30.822
I lost my mind somewhere
during the Japan season.

02:25:30.822 --> 02:25:31.656
Oh well.

02:25:31.656 --> 02:25:33.357
And it's strange, 'cause
I'm still an intern.

02:25:33.357 --> 02:25:34.559
We're doing rice bowls now.

02:25:34.559 --> 02:25:35.393
Ugh!

02:25:35.393 --> 02:25:37.161
Yeah, it looks really good

02:25:37.161 --> 02:25:40.264
if it was abstract art in a museum

02:25:40.264 --> 02:25:43.167
about 20 meters away from your eyeballs.

02:25:43.167 --> 02:25:45.136
But when you come close
and then you're faced

02:25:45.136 --> 02:25:46.771
with the proposition of eating it,

02:25:46.771 --> 02:25:49.207
ugh!

02:25:49.207 --> 02:25:51.442
I can feel my body rejecting this.

02:25:52.543 --> 02:25:53.377
Otherwise, it's fine.

02:25:53.377 --> 02:25:54.946
I mean, it's just very average.

02:25:54.946 --> 02:25:56.447
It's just a normal rice bowl.

02:25:59.450 --> 02:26:01.085
We have the same thing, another rice bowl,

02:26:01.085 --> 02:26:03.755
but this time it's got some
grilled chicken in there.

02:26:04.922 --> 02:26:05.823
That was really good.

02:26:05.823 --> 02:26:07.525
This feels like the safest bet.

02:26:07.525 --> 02:26:10.194
Ah! I don't know what anything is still.

02:26:10.194 --> 02:26:11.729
So let's go through it together.

02:26:11.729 --> 02:26:12.597
The first thing,

02:26:12.597 --> 02:26:17.034
this is either a black bean
chalupa or a dirty diaper.

02:26:17.034 --> 02:26:17.902
I can't tell.

02:26:17.902 --> 02:26:20.371
'Cause it's thick and wrinkly

02:26:20.371 --> 02:26:22.707
and just dripping with black goo.

02:26:22.707 --> 02:26:23.541
Don't want that.

02:26:23.541 --> 02:26:25.643
Oh! It's this, yeah!

02:26:25.643 --> 02:26:27.178
I mean, every time these
Doritos shells show up,

02:26:27.178 --> 02:26:28.012
I'm just happy.

02:26:28.012 --> 02:26:30.748
Dorito cheesy gordita crunch nacho cheese.

02:26:30.748 --> 02:26:32.150
They put every word in that.

02:26:34.285 --> 02:26:36.921
Oh, it's that thing, but not nacho'd.

02:26:36.921 --> 02:26:38.990
Once you have the Doritos shell version,

02:26:38.990 --> 02:26:42.360
to go back is like, no way. No way!

02:26:42.360 --> 02:26:44.028
I've touched the sky.

02:26:44.028 --> 02:26:46.764
I can stay on the ground no longer.

02:26:46.764 --> 02:26:50.668
And then we have two
Crunchwrap Supreme options,

02:26:50.668 --> 02:26:53.004
black bean Crunchwrap Supreme,

02:26:53.004 --> 02:26:55.139
and then the regular Crunchwrap Supreme

02:26:55.139 --> 02:26:56.908
is, of course, filled with beef.

02:26:56.908 --> 02:27:00.178
OK, it's time now for India's sides menu,

02:27:00.178 --> 02:27:03.181
starting off with Mexican corn salad.

02:27:04.382 --> 02:27:06.684
You don't need to add so much sauce to it.

02:27:06.684 --> 02:27:08.319
I feel like this could've
been a lot simpler,

02:27:08.319 --> 02:27:09.887
and people would appreciate it more.

02:27:09.887 --> 02:27:13.791
Next up, we have loaded
fries and loaded nachos.

02:27:13.791 --> 02:27:16.427
So, typically, Taco Bell
does not serve loaded nachos

02:27:16.427 --> 02:27:17.862
and loaded fries here in India,

02:27:17.862 --> 02:27:19.564
but we found a restaurant
that was kind enough

02:27:19.564 --> 02:27:21.165
to send it to us anyways.

02:27:21.165 --> 02:27:23.534
I will say, this is
probably my favorite thing

02:27:23.534 --> 02:27:24.836
about Taco Bell in India.

02:27:24.836 --> 02:27:27.839
The loaded nachos are banging,

02:27:27.839 --> 02:27:29.273
when you get them at the restaurant.

02:27:30.474 --> 02:27:31.642
Oy.

02:27:31.642 --> 02:27:33.377
But, yeah, there's a reason
they don't deliver it.

02:27:33.377 --> 02:27:34.979
That tastes like wet cardboard.

02:27:34.979 --> 02:27:37.048
And now we have two barf bags.

02:27:37.048 --> 02:27:37.882
Just kidding.

02:27:37.882 --> 02:27:39.383
Chicken nachos.

02:27:39.383 --> 02:27:42.553
They had chicken tacos, and
now there are chicken nachos.

02:27:42.553 --> 02:27:46.557
And our second doggy bag has -- whoa!

02:27:46.557 --> 02:27:50.194
That was alarming. Because
what I saw was this.

02:27:50.194 --> 02:27:52.864
I did not expect this
to come out of that bag.

02:27:52.864 --> 02:27:53.898
Crispy chicken strips.

02:27:53.898 --> 02:27:55.766
Sides, baby.

02:27:55.766 --> 02:27:56.601
We got 'em.

02:27:56.601 --> 02:27:59.070
Cheesy fiesta potatoes.

02:27:59.937 --> 02:28:01.072
There's better things
to be had on the menu,

02:28:01.072 --> 02:28:01.906
but I do like those.

02:28:01.906 --> 02:28:03.641
Black beans, black beans and rice,

02:28:03.641 --> 02:28:06.644
and you can get a guacamole side.

02:28:06.644 --> 02:28:08.412
Now, here are some
items that are available

02:28:08.412 --> 02:28:10.114
both in India and the US

02:28:10.114 --> 02:28:11.515
but are still very different.

02:28:11.515 --> 02:28:12.516
For example,

02:28:12.516 --> 02:28:16.554
this is India's quesadilla,
grilled cheese quesadilla.

02:28:16.554 --> 02:28:17.388
But as you can see,

02:28:17.388 --> 02:28:21.192
it's filled with a lot of fajita veggies,

02:28:21.192 --> 02:28:23.561
it's got this special creamy sauce,

02:28:23.561 --> 02:28:25.830
and it's topped with a lot of jalapeños.

02:28:25.830 --> 02:28:29.033
Whereas in the US, it
comes with just cheese.

02:28:29.033 --> 02:28:30.468
How boring is that?

02:28:30.468 --> 02:28:32.570
Correct. And this is what it looks like.

02:28:32.570 --> 02:28:33.671
Incredibly boring.

02:28:33.671 --> 02:28:35.606
Another big difference is here in India,

02:28:35.606 --> 02:28:37.842
our nachos are all seasoned,

02:28:37.842 --> 02:28:41.012
so they already have a masala
or some sort of spice to them.

02:28:41.012 --> 02:28:44.215
Our nacho chips in the US are
just regular tortilla chips

02:28:44.215 --> 02:28:45.416
with nacho cheese.

02:28:46.884 --> 02:28:48.352
Here in India, in our veg options,

02:28:48.352 --> 02:28:51.055
we use pinto beans, or rajma.

02:28:51.055 --> 02:28:53.958
Whereas in the US, our bean
of choice is the black bean.

02:28:53.958 --> 02:28:55.693
Exclusive US sauces.

02:28:55.693 --> 02:28:57.361
Hey, you know what that means.

02:28:57.361 --> 02:28:58.930
Sauce talk.

02:28:58.930 --> 02:29:01.599
It's now time for
India's exclusive sauces.

02:29:01.599 --> 02:29:03.134
We have quite the wide range.

02:29:03.134 --> 02:29:05.069
We have cool ranch.

02:29:05.069 --> 02:29:06.604
Because there's a lot of spice

02:29:06.604 --> 02:29:08.639
in a lot of these burritos and tacos,

02:29:08.639 --> 02:29:11.075
I imagine if you're somebody
who can't tolerate spice,

02:29:11.075 --> 02:29:12.476
definitely get a side of this.

02:29:12.476 --> 02:29:14.679
Then there is spicy salsa.

02:29:14.679 --> 02:29:15.980
I tasted it. It's really nice.

02:29:15.980 --> 02:29:17.548
It's got a lot more spice to it,

02:29:17.548 --> 02:29:20.584
but also the flavor of
imli, which is tamarind.

02:29:20.584 --> 02:29:22.420
We use it in a lot of our dishes,

02:29:22.420 --> 02:29:23.988
especially South Indian dishes.

02:29:23.988 --> 02:29:25.156
Then there's a chocolate sauce,

02:29:25.156 --> 02:29:26.757
which I imagine is for churros

02:29:26.757 --> 02:29:29.327
or some sort of dippable dessert.

02:29:29.327 --> 02:29:31.562
But if you want to dip
your quesadilla into this,

02:29:31.562 --> 02:29:32.697
I'm not going to judge.

02:29:32.697 --> 02:29:34.765
Next up we have lava sauce,

02:29:34.765 --> 02:29:37.401
which doesn't really
look as much like lava,

02:29:37.401 --> 02:29:40.104
but it definitely has a kick to it.

02:29:40.104 --> 02:29:44.008
Chicken tikka masala sauce,
which looks more like lava.

02:29:44.008 --> 02:29:46.043
Down in the end here we
got reduced-fat sour cream.

02:29:46.043 --> 02:29:48.546
Who doesn't like chips
and sour cream, right?

02:29:48.546 --> 02:29:49.547
Could use some fat.

02:29:49.547 --> 02:29:51.882
Then, moving on, we have a chipotle sauce.

02:29:51.882 --> 02:29:53.784
Chipotle sauce is very good.

02:29:53.784 --> 02:29:55.553
Mm. Mm. Mm. Mm.

02:29:55.553 --> 02:29:57.321
Avocado ranch.

02:29:57.321 --> 02:29:58.589
Mm!

02:29:58.589 --> 02:29:59.790
I love it. More of that, please.

02:29:59.790 --> 02:30:00.958
And they have a spicy ranch.

02:30:00.958 --> 02:30:02.727
How spicy could it be?

02:30:02.727 --> 02:30:03.561
Not very.

02:30:03.561 --> 02:30:04.528
And finally, the red sauce.

02:30:04.528 --> 02:30:07.531
OK, it is finally dessert time.

02:30:07.531 --> 02:30:09.767
I've eaten a lot of savory food,

02:30:09.767 --> 02:30:11.569
and I'm excited for the desserts.

02:30:11.569 --> 02:30:12.703
Good old churros.

02:30:12.703 --> 02:30:14.038
I am a big fan of churros.

02:30:14.038 --> 02:30:16.307
They send you one chocolaty dip.

02:30:17.341 --> 02:30:19.577
I feel like you can't
really go wrong with churros

02:30:19.577 --> 02:30:21.946
if you want to call yourself a restaurant.

02:30:21.946 --> 02:30:24.715
And next is something I
have never seen before.

02:30:24.715 --> 02:30:26.283
Cinnamon twisties.

02:30:27.651 --> 02:30:29.987
I could see myself, you
know, at 3 a.m. in the night,

02:30:29.987 --> 02:30:32.690
sad, vulnerable, eating
a whole packet of these.

02:30:32.690 --> 02:30:33.824
So that means it's a good dessert.

02:30:33.824 --> 02:30:35.893
Taco Bell used to sell quesadillas

02:30:35.893 --> 02:30:38.996
filled with chocolate, and
they were called chocodillas.

02:30:38.996 --> 02:30:40.531
But I guess they've stopped that now.

02:30:40.531 --> 02:30:42.433
Taco Bell is against puns.

02:30:42.433 --> 02:30:45.536
The only US exclusive
dessert we have are these,

02:30:45.536 --> 02:30:47.138
the Cinnabon Delights.

02:30:47.138 --> 02:30:49.106
As Cinnabons, I'm pretty
sure this is filled

02:30:49.106 --> 02:30:50.775
with some sort of cream cheese, right?

02:30:51.776 --> 02:30:52.943
I assure you there's cream cheese in this

02:30:52.943 --> 02:30:54.278
or whatever, their frosting.

02:30:54.278 --> 02:30:55.746
Someone's got to eat it. That
definitely can't go to waste.

02:30:55.746 --> 02:30:57.581
Eat it now!

02:30:57.581 --> 02:30:58.949
Right? They're fantastic.

02:30:58.949 --> 02:31:01.352
All right, it's time for
India's exclusive drinks.

02:31:01.352 --> 02:31:03.220
What could we do without them?

02:31:03.220 --> 02:31:05.289
Nothing. I would've choked to death

02:31:05.289 --> 02:31:07.625
on all that burrito maida wrap.

02:31:07.625 --> 02:31:09.927
First up, the soft drinks that we have,

02:31:09.927 --> 02:31:12.196
we sell 7Up and Mirinda over here,

02:31:12.196 --> 02:31:14.131
but actually in Bengaluru

02:31:14.131 --> 02:31:15.900
I've seen a lot more variety of drinks.

02:31:15.900 --> 02:31:17.968
So I think it varies from store to store.

02:31:17.968 --> 02:31:20.304
Next up, Taco Bell sells juices.

02:31:20.304 --> 02:31:22.440
This one was a mixed fruit juice,

02:31:22.440 --> 02:31:23.707
but I drank it all,

02:31:23.707 --> 02:31:25.376
and I can tell you, it was pretty good.

02:31:25.376 --> 02:31:27.478
They also sell a
cranberry and apple juice,

02:31:27.478 --> 02:31:29.413
but the stores that we asked in Mumbai

02:31:29.413 --> 02:31:30.815
did not have those available.

02:31:30.815 --> 02:31:32.817
And finally, they sell milkshakes.

02:31:32.817 --> 02:31:35.953
This is mango. This is
chocolate. Cookie crumble.

02:31:35.953 --> 02:31:38.622
The true test of a milkshake
is to test the fruit one

02:31:38.622 --> 02:31:40.758
and see if it's still fresh.

02:31:40.758 --> 02:31:41.959
Hey, that's pretty good.

02:31:41.959 --> 02:31:43.160
The mango milkshake.

02:31:43.160 --> 02:31:44.862
US exclusive drinks.

02:31:44.862 --> 02:31:46.664
There's literally a million,

02:31:46.664 --> 02:31:49.066
yes, really, of soft drinks

02:31:49.066 --> 02:31:51.535
you can get at Taco Bell
you can't get in India.

02:31:51.535 --> 02:31:54.505
So I just went and got a diet Pepsi

02:31:54.505 --> 02:31:55.573
and, of course,

02:31:55.573 --> 02:31:56.474
[clown horn honking]

02:31:56.474 --> 02:31:58.209
Baja Blast.

02:31:58.209 --> 02:32:00.945
After doing this, what, three,
four times at this point,

02:32:00.945 --> 02:32:03.013
I'm actually starting to like Baja Blast.

02:32:03.013 --> 02:32:05.816
You can actually get a
whole bunch of soft drinks

02:32:05.816 --> 02:32:07.218
at the US Taco Bell.

02:32:07.218 --> 02:32:09.386
♪ All of these ♪

02:32:09.386 --> 02:32:10.921
I wasn't getting 20 drinks.

02:32:10.921 --> 02:32:13.257
Get yourself a bottle, OJ, Tropicana.

02:32:13.257 --> 02:32:16.026
Also something you can get
are things called freezes,

02:32:16.026 --> 02:32:18.195
which at one point were frozen

02:32:18.195 --> 02:32:20.131
slushy- or Slurpee-like drinks.

02:32:20.131 --> 02:32:22.833
You can get, of course, a
Mountain Dew Baja Blast.

02:32:22.833 --> 02:32:25.069
And also get yourself wild cherry freeze.

02:32:25.069 --> 02:32:27.204
Oh, f---.

02:32:27.204 --> 02:32:28.973
That's cough syrup.

02:32:28.973 --> 02:32:30.674
Also, you can get coffee,

02:32:30.674 --> 02:32:32.877
both iced and hot.

02:32:32.877 --> 02:32:34.345
Iced coffee.

02:32:34.345 --> 02:32:35.713
Oh, no, wait, that's soda. What is this?

02:32:35.713 --> 02:32:37.715
Ignore that. Put that over there.

02:32:37.715 --> 02:32:38.983
The Cinnabon Delight coffee.

02:32:38.983 --> 02:32:40.384
OK, so they accidentally
gave us two of these.

02:32:40.384 --> 02:32:43.687
Iced coffee that's flavored
like the Cinnabon Delights.

02:32:43.687 --> 02:32:45.089
Are you kidding me?

02:32:45.089 --> 02:32:47.691
I can just feel my life expectancy

02:32:47.691 --> 02:32:49.994
just getting closer and closer.

02:32:49.994 --> 02:32:52.496
Just like, sip, mm,

02:32:52.496 --> 02:32:54.832
he ain't seeing his 80s, mm.

02:32:54.832 --> 02:32:56.233
But it's worth it. That's delicious.

02:32:56.233 --> 02:32:58.402
You can also get those coffees hot.

02:32:58.402 --> 02:33:00.738
Taco Bell breakfast, baby.

02:33:00.738 --> 02:33:02.039
I think this is just about everything.

02:33:02.039 --> 02:33:04.408
Once again, I can't tell what anything is.

02:33:04.408 --> 02:33:07.244
It's all just a sea of beige.

02:33:07.244 --> 02:33:08.579
Let's find out together.

02:33:08.579 --> 02:33:10.814
This one just says bacon.

02:33:10.814 --> 02:33:11.782
Thank you for that.

02:33:11.782 --> 02:33:13.284
Burrito with bacon.

02:33:13.284 --> 02:33:14.351
I'm like the Riddler over here.

02:33:14.351 --> 02:33:16.887
Just like, hey, figure it out.
Question mark, question mark.

02:33:16.887 --> 02:33:18.989
I mean, it's a bit unnatural
how yellow that is.

02:33:18.989 --> 02:33:21.425
It's really bright. It's a bit concerning.

02:33:21.425 --> 02:33:23.627
This one's going to be the
one with steak, I assume.

02:33:23.627 --> 02:33:25.963
Yeah. [laughs] Who's hungry?

02:33:27.064 --> 02:33:28.299
The steak's a little weird.

02:33:28.299 --> 02:33:29.967
Maybe don't get the
steak one specifically.

02:33:29.967 --> 02:33:32.570
Do you see this condensation?

02:33:32.570 --> 02:33:34.338
How bad this food is sweating?

02:33:34.338 --> 02:33:36.507
Breakfast Crunchwrap Supreme.

02:33:36.507 --> 02:33:38.842
Oh, there's sausage inside of this.

02:33:38.842 --> 02:33:39.910
Look, comes inside.

02:33:39.910 --> 02:33:41.111
It's like the magic ticket.

02:33:41.111 --> 02:33:43.247
Now I get to work at
Taco Bell or something.

02:33:43.247 --> 02:33:44.515
Their sausage is good, though.

02:33:44.515 --> 02:33:45.683
Get yourself a hash brown.

02:33:45.683 --> 02:33:47.051
They also have breakfast salsa,

02:33:47.051 --> 02:33:49.019
but the Taco Bell I went
to did not have any.

02:33:50.955 --> 02:33:52.122
Let's talk about nutrition,

02:33:52.122 --> 02:33:53.724
everybody's favorite topic.

02:33:53.724 --> 02:33:55.059
That's why you come to "Food Wars,"

02:33:55.059 --> 02:33:56.393
'cause you love fast food,

02:33:56.393 --> 02:33:58.395
but mainly, you love nutrition.

02:33:58.395 --> 02:34:02.132
In India, a typical soft-shell
Mexican chicken taco

02:34:02.132 --> 02:34:05.102
will be 185 calories.

02:34:05.102 --> 02:34:08.939
In the US, our standard chicken
soft taco is 160 calories.

02:34:08.939 --> 02:34:12.443
So we have fewer calories,
fat, carbs, and sodium,

02:34:12.443 --> 02:34:13.544
but more protein.

02:34:13.544 --> 02:34:15.179
Next up is the chicken quesadilla.

02:34:15.179 --> 02:34:18.482
Ours has 268.5 calories.

02:34:18.482 --> 02:34:20.684
And ours is 510 calories.

02:34:20.684 --> 02:34:23.153
Now, please note the sodium
level on our quesadilla.

02:34:23.153 --> 02:34:26.924
It's over half the daily
recommended amount.

02:34:26.924 --> 02:34:29.827
That's a salty quesadilla.

02:34:29.827 --> 02:34:34.131
In India, a vegstar
wrap is 239.9 calories.

02:34:34.131 --> 02:34:35.399
Closest we have to that is our

02:34:35.399 --> 02:34:37.134
black bean Crunchwrap Supreme.

02:34:37.134 --> 02:34:41.438
Again, double the calorie count,
get a load of that sodium.

02:34:41.438 --> 02:34:44.808
Are you looking for the most
calorific item here in India?

02:34:44.808 --> 02:34:47.845
Well, look no further
than the cinnamon twists!

02:34:47.845 --> 02:34:51.915
Each of these packets will
cost you 480.9 calories!

02:34:51.915 --> 02:34:53.717
Here in the US, if
you're having a hard time

02:34:53.717 --> 02:34:56.553
finding calories at a
Taco Bell, check out this.

02:34:56.553 --> 02:34:59.657
The double beef grilled cheese burrito.

02:35:01.558 --> 02:35:03.894
So, Taco Bell in India does not disclose

02:35:03.894 --> 02:35:05.162
any of their ingredients,

02:35:05.162 --> 02:35:06.363
but I thought it would be interesting

02:35:06.363 --> 02:35:07.665
to talk about two of the ingredients

02:35:07.665 --> 02:35:10.434
that we have here that
are unique to India.

02:35:10.434 --> 02:35:11.969
No. 1 is paneer.

02:35:11.969 --> 02:35:14.305
So, the problem with the Mexican paneer

02:35:14.305 --> 02:35:17.274
that was served to me in
this batch of Taco Bell

02:35:17.274 --> 02:35:18.776
is that it tasted like

02:35:18.776 --> 02:35:20.477
the processed paneer you get at stores.

02:35:20.477 --> 02:35:22.513
It tasted like something that
had been stored in the fridge.

02:35:22.513 --> 02:35:25.115
Also, because paneer is
so popular here in India,

02:35:25.115 --> 02:35:28.052
every single fast-food
restaurant has paneer options.

02:35:28.052 --> 02:35:30.220
You know, when you know
how well it can be done,

02:35:30.220 --> 02:35:32.056
I didn't like the paneer that much

02:35:32.056 --> 02:35:34.758
in the burritos and tacos I had today.

02:35:34.758 --> 02:35:37.828
The next ingredient I want to
talk about is tikka masala.

02:35:37.828 --> 02:35:38.662
I thought it was OK.

02:35:38.662 --> 02:35:40.964
It had a lot of flavor.
It was quite spicy.

02:35:40.964 --> 02:35:44.001
But the thing that makes
tikka masala so exciting

02:35:44.001 --> 02:35:46.870
is that it's always made
from fresh tomatoes.

02:35:46.870 --> 02:35:48.872
And so you can sort of
tell there's a difference

02:35:48.872 --> 02:35:50.240
when it's in the sauce form.

02:35:50.240 --> 02:35:52.676
However, I will say it's
always a valiant effort

02:35:52.676 --> 02:35:54.178
to see these fast-food companies

02:35:54.178 --> 02:35:56.513
and people who come here
from abroad in general

02:35:56.513 --> 02:35:57.815
adapt to the Indian palate

02:35:57.815 --> 02:36:00.351
and try to make cuisine that matches ours.

02:36:00.351 --> 02:36:02.419
In the US, we do disclose our ingredients,

02:36:02.419 --> 02:36:04.288
and here's a few you should be wary of.

02:36:04.288 --> 02:36:08.292
First is brominated
vegetable oil, aka BVO.

02:36:08.292 --> 02:36:11.195
BVO is an emulsifier found
in citrus-flavored sodas

02:36:11.195 --> 02:36:13.163
that specifically use citrus oils,

02:36:13.163 --> 02:36:14.598
and it's considered a health risk

02:36:14.598 --> 02:36:16.767
when ingested in large amounts.

02:36:16.767 --> 02:36:18.235
In one case, a man who drank

02:36:18.235 --> 02:36:20.738
2 to 4 liters of BVO soda per day

02:36:20.738 --> 02:36:23.574
developed bromism and experienced symptoms

02:36:23.574 --> 02:36:25.943
such as memory loss and
extreme muscle fatigue.

02:36:25.943 --> 02:36:28.278
It can be found in the
ingredients of three

02:36:28.278 --> 02:36:32.116
of the cantina-menu freezes:
the beach berry freeze,

02:36:32.116 --> 02:36:35.152
the ginger mule freeze,
and the party punch freeze.

02:36:35.152 --> 02:36:36.587
The last one, the party punch freeze,

02:36:36.587 --> 02:36:41.091
also contains yellow
No. 5, aka tartrazine,

02:36:41.091 --> 02:36:43.093
which is subject to
restriction outside the US

02:36:43.093 --> 02:36:45.028
in places like the EU and India,

02:36:45.028 --> 02:36:48.399
as it, quote, "may have an
adverse effect on activity

02:36:48.399 --> 02:36:50.067
and attention in children."

02:36:50.067 --> 02:36:52.269
And you can find it in
several Taco Bell menu items,

02:36:52.269 --> 02:36:55.472
specifically the Doritos locos
taco nacho cheese shells,

02:36:55.472 --> 02:36:58.075
oh, no! I had, like, three of those today.

02:36:58.075 --> 02:36:59.410
And Baja Blast,

02:36:59.410 --> 02:37:01.078
gah! Just when I was starting to like it.

02:37:01.178 --> 02:37:04.281
I just want to shout
out Joe Avella and say

02:37:04.281 --> 02:37:06.250
I understand what trauma
you must be going through

02:37:06.250 --> 02:37:08.519
after doing so many Taco Bell episodes.

02:37:08.519 --> 02:37:10.487
You're a brave, brave man, Joe.

